#passage(("We have the word Islam, we have the word Muslim; they are very commonly used words, but what do they mean? Islam comes from the Arabic word استسلام (Istislam), means to submit to God, to submit to something, so Islam is the submission! Full submission to The Creator. Submitting and surrendering your will to the will of the Almighty Creator. So, إسلام (Islam) is \"Submission\" and a Muslim is someone who does the act of Islam: \"he submits to The One True God\", He surrenders to the will of The Creator. So, when you hear someone using the word \"Muslim\", it's literally, if you want to translate it, you will translate it into \"Submitter\".", "And I would say that's very important; it's very unique from other faiths and religions. For example: if you look at Christianity, which is predominant in this country, Christianity comes from Christ, a follower of Christ. If you look at Judaism, it comes from Judah, who's the head of one of the 12 tribes. If you look at India, you've got Hinduism which is attributed to the country; you've got Buddhism attributed to Buddha. So if you look at other religions or other faiths, it's always attributed to an individual, or is attributed to a land or a group of people or a race or something like that. The thing about Islam is that it's free completely from any prejudice, or your own race, or your own people, or your own country. It's not about that; it's about God! Submission to The One True Creator, to The One True God.", "That's why the majority of Muslims in the world are not Arabs! There is a common misconception that people have; they think that the majority of Muslims are Arabs. But actually over 80% of Muslims are not Arabs, from different countries. You got British Muslims, you got Chinese Muslims, Japanese Muslims, Pakistani Muslims, Turkish Muslims, Arab Muslims, from every part of the world; you've got people following the religion, because it's a way of life that you implement in your day-to-day life. So, it has nothing to do with where you were born or what you believe in.", "So, the word \"Allah\": what does this Allah mean? The word Allah is just the Arabic word for God. Allah is like الإله \"The God\". You find Coptic Christians in Egypt, they will use the word Allah as well. So it's not a term unique to Islam; it's just a term that refers to God, but it's a very unique term in its meaning. Because the word Allah in the Arabic language does not have a feminine version or a masculine version; Allah is just Allah. It's a word that is gender neutral; it's not masculine nor feminine. It perfectly describes God because we don't believe Allah is a man. We don't believe Allah is a man with a beard sitting somewhere. We believe God is beyond the conception of a human being, so that's why that word fits the Creator perfectly.", "Also the word Allah you cannot put it in plural; it's just One. Uniquely One. You cannot make it more than one, which is also symbolizes the idea that Allah or God is just One. While \"god\" for example, the English word, it can be god and goddess, a feminine version, or god and gods, multitude of different gods. That's what makes the word very unique.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Non-Muslim Audience Asks Muslim Difficult Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=imKsFyzx-Yo", ((210, "3:30–3:57"), (246, "4:06–4:45"), (285, "4:45–5:17"), (326, "5:26–6:06"), (379, "6:19–6:43"),), id: 436)
