// U ML064:216-259 | The Muslim Lantern | 3
#passage(("Muslims don't believe the Jews and the Christians are monotheistic in every way, especially the Christians. We believe they are polytheistic in their belief. They believe Jesus is God, they believe in the Trinity. So I would disagree with this idea that says that the Shahada (Testimony of Faith) is mirrored within the Christian and Jewish Faiths. The shahadah is also not just that there is One God. That's an incorrect definition of the shahadah.", "Shahada is أَشْهَدُ أَنْ لاَ إِلَهَ إِلَّا الله (ashHadu an la ilaha illa Allah). أَشْهَدُ (ashHadu) means I testify or bear witness. لاَ إِلَهَ (la ilaha), لا (la) means NO. إله (ilaha) is from ألِه ،يألَه، إلاهةً، فهُوَ مَألوه. مَألوه is مَعبود, the one who is worshipped. So, لاَ إِلَهَ (la ilaha: there's nothing worshipped). There's nothing WORTHY of worship, in the Islamic definition. So when we say لاَ إِلَهَ إِلَّا الله (la ilaha illa Allah: there's nothing worthy of worship except Allah).", "So when you look at the Jewish tradition and the Christian tradition, we say definitely this idea is not mirrored within the Jewish or Christian tradition. And if it was, you're going to have all of these verses in The Quran saying, \"O People of the Book\", O People of the Book do this, O People of the Book believe, O People of the Book do not exaggerate in your religion (anNisa4:171). Because if they already have the Shahada, then all what The Quran is going to be doing is to tell them to follow The Prophet.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| Responding To Professor Jiang's Lecture On The Islamic Golden Age | Muhammed Ali!”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6SVGKQ-xiGs", ((765, "12:45–13:04"), (784, "13:04–13:27"), (812, "13:32–13:49"),), id: 438)
