#refbox("Reference text: Quran 4:171, quran.com (Saheeh International)", (("4:171", "O People of the Scripture, do not commit excess in your religion or say about Allāh except the truth. The Messiah, Jesus the son of Mary, was but a messenger of Allāh and His word which He directed to Mary and a soul [created at a command] from Him. So believe in Allāh and His messengers. And do not say, \"Three\"; desist - it is better for you. Indeed, Allāh is but one God. Exalted is He above having a son. To Him belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth. And sufficient is Allāh as Disposer of affairs."),))
// U ML340:187-210 | The Muslim Lantern | 3
#passage(("Allah sends Prophets and Messengers. Those Prophets and Messengers have one message: There's One Creator. He's worthy of worship. People, when they hear the word \"worship\", usually has a negative connotation, but worship for us, from Islamic perspective, is a very unique term. Because worship in Islam is not just bowing down to an individual, or prayer. Worship in Islam is anything you do for the sake of God!", "So, if I'm walking in the road and there is a hazard and I remove the hazard, that's an act of worship in Islam. If I smile in someone's face, this is an act of worship in Islam. So, Islam has every act that you do that God is pleased with; it's an act of worship. In fact some acts that a human can do can be the highest forms of reward that you can get. For example: being good to your mother, your parents, your wife, and your family. This is the highest level of Good Deeds that a person can do, and to us, this is the highest form of worship! Because if it's something that God is pleased with, then it's something that is worshipping.", "So, the description of Allah is that Allah is Uniquely One, Allah is Independent, Eternal. We rely on Allah when we need something; people are in difficulty ask God. So we depend on him, and everything in the universe depends on him. He doesn't beget nor he's born, so he doesn't have children, parents, grandparents, reproductive organs. Is not like us as human beings, and there is nothing like onto Allah. This is a description of the creator that the Prophets and Messengers come to call you to. And then the Quran is that message for human beings to read.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Non-Muslim Audience Asks Muslim Difficult Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=imKsFyzx-Yo", ((725, "12:05–12:27"), (750, "12:30–12:57"), (781, "13:01–13:37"),), id: 439)
