#passage(("[Tawheed] means monotheism. First description of Allah is given in the Quran chapter 112. Allah says: say Allah is [Ahad], means uniquely one. So these four verses gives the full description of God.", "Now [Tawheed] refers to three things: the lordship of God, which means only God has the attributes of kingship, absolute kingship, creation, sustaining the creation, given provision and all of these things. So these actions that are actions of God, we only attribute them to God. Only God is the absolute powerful, absolute sustainer, absolute king, all of these things, only God. That's one part.", "The second part is all the attributes of worship, actions of worship should only be devoted to him. So praying is only to God. Sacrificing is only to God. All of these things, fasting is only to God. You don't fast to your friend. You don't prostrate to your neighbor. You don't do any of these things. This is now [polytheism]. You're worshiping other than God. And all the names of attributes are unique to him. The names contain attributes as well. He has 99 names and attributes. All of these are only given to that creator. So only that creator is the most loving, is the most merciful, is the most beneficent.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Passionate Christian Argues For The Trinity With A Muslim! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ntsF1iRj8IM", ((4235, "1:10:35–1:11:23"), (4283, "1:11:23–1:11:54"), (4314, "1:11:54–1:12:34"),), id: 441)

