 of Light and the Lord of Darkness, the Lord of creation and then the Lord of provision and then the Lord of War. This is the opposite of that. So this thing of singling Allah is very easy to come with.", "Most people who believe in God, if not all, if you say to them do you believe God created you, say yes. You believe God is the one who gives lives, you'll say yes. Even the disbelievers of [Quraysh], did they admit to this or no? Even they did. But we still call them, Allah called them [mushrik], even though they say they believe that Allah is the one who created them. So it's not enough to say I believe and singling out Allah. That's why we saying believe in Allah four things; that's why you need to know them; you could believe in two but doesn't mean you fully believe in Allah.", "So even some people's friend, he also believed in this. What did he say to Allah? He said my Lord. He said he believes Allah is the Lord, but did that mean he's a Believer now? You going to see him pray next to you in the Masjid? No, because the believing Allah requires four things.", "What is the problem that they had? It is now the third thing, which is singling Allah in the actions that we do. That's why we mention the example of making an [oath] with other Allah; that's an action that we do. So singling Allah in the action, meaning the prayer for example, prayer an action that you do; these actions of worship, you have to single Allah alone; he's the one that you do it for him. Meaning if you start praying now to anyone sitting down here, what does it mean? You're a disbeliever straight away. You're worshiping other than Allah.", "Singling Allah in the actions that you do: absolute [reliance] on Allah; the absolute help when you're in a state of need is from Allah; the fasting that you do is only for Allah; making an oath is only for Allah; making a promise with Allah, it's only Allah. All of these things, slaughtering: that's why you see these magicians, they slaughter a chicken f