#passage(("The Creator we believe in as Muslims is mentioned: Allah is describing Himself in chapter:112 (alikhlass). Allah says (alIIkhlas112:1-4): (Say, Allah is uniquely One). Uniquely One means in his oneness, He's unique. He's not like anyone. And أحد (Ahad), which is the word used, means Allah is completely One. So we don't believe Allah has persons, three in one, four in one, eleven in one. Allah is just Allah; He doesn't have children.", "We believe Allah says: قُلْ هُوَ ٱللَّهُ أَحَدٌ ٱللَّهُ ٱلصَّمَدُ (Say, Allah is One. Allah is The Absolute, The Eternal, Self-sufficient), meaning everything depends on Him. He doesn't need or depend on anyone. لَمْ يَلِدْ وَلَمْ يُولَدْ: He doesn't have children, like us, and He's not begotten; He doesn't have parents or grandparents. وَلَمْ يَكُن لَّهُۥ كُفُوًا أَحَدٌۢ (And there is nothing in existence comparable or equal to Him), meaning that anything you see, think about, imagine, or picture in your mind is not like Allah. Allah is unlike all of that. So that is the concept of God that we believe in.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “A Christian Testimony About Islam Part 2! Muhammed Ali - Speakers Corner”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iH3wQ8b4ls8", ((19, "0:19–0:37"), (41, "0:41–1:12"),), id: 453)
