#passage(("Allahﷻ says in the Quran, chapter:112 (Alikhlass): (And there is nothing like unto Him) (Alikhlas112:1-4), which would mean anything in the physical world or anything in reality does not resemble Him. It's not that it \"does not resemble\"; it's \"not like\" the Creator. The Creator is \"not like\" that thing. This is the description of Allah.", "Also Allah says in the Quran (Albaqarah2:255): (Allah, there is no Deity worthy of worship except Him). He's The Only One worthy of worship. (The Ever-Living, Self-Sustaining, drowsiness or sleep does not overtake Him. To Him belongs that which is in the Heavens and the Earth. Nothing can intercede in front of Him without His permission. His throne extends over the Heavens and the Earth.) The word كُرسي is used; there's a different explanation for that word. (Extends over the Heavens and the Earth, and its preservation does not weaken Him, does not tire Him, and He is The Most-High, The Most-Great.)",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Why Can't You Mock The Prophet of Islam? Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EUsqyD_oIC0", ((503, "8:23–8:51"), (537, "8:57–9:27"),), id: 454)
