#passage(("God is not like us; he's not a human being, he's not a man, a woman. That's what Muslims believe. A lot of people in the Christian tradition today, the mainstream Christianity, believe that Jesus is God, a human being is God. You have the Trinity: the Father, the Son and the Holy Spirit, the three are one. We don't believe that God is a human being. We believe that Jesus, Moses, Noah, Abraham, all of these people are Prophets and Messengers, meaning they are people that Allah chose, God chose, to send them to the world, to people, to tell us about the Creator, to tell us about our purpose in life, to tell us why we exist here, what is going to happen to us when we die.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Why Should I Accept Your Religion?! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rBgIryv7XPM", ((17, "0:17–0:55"),), id: 464)
// U ML390:20-33 | The Muslim Lantern | 1
#passage(("There are similarities between Islam and Christianity and there are differences between Islam and Christianity. We don't believe anyone died for our sins. We believe we're responsible for what we do. If I do wrong, I should be accountable. No one else dies for me. I have to be responsible for what I do. We believe the Creator is not a man or a woman. He's not us. He created the whole world. He's not like His creation. If I make a chair I'm not similar to the chair. As well, whatever we imagine, we cannot imagine the Creator in reality, but we know He's Loving, He's Merciful, we know He's just, He created us and He has given us laws.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Friendly Lady Amazed By Islamic Teachings! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OhPDOeUN5uU", ((33, "0:33–1:09"),), id: 465)
// U ML232:168-186 | The Muslim Lantern | 1
#passage(("Even morality we don't take it as a consequentialist thing. We believe God is an actual existent entity that exists, that's separate from this world that we live in, that created everything, that brought it to life, that gives guidance to the creation, that takes life from people, and that [sends] them revelation, prophets and messengers. So we believe Jesus, Moses, Noah, Abraham, these are messengers assigned by God. They have communication with God, which is an actual present entity, not consciousness. And we believe that humans have consciousness, but on a lower level. We have different levels of consciousness. We believe that consciousness is given by God. So not everyone has the same. Everyone has a soul, which some people call consciousness. But people have different levels of intelligence, etc. So not everyone is the same in every way. So this is the Islamic position.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Buddhist Monk Surprises Muslim With His Beliefs! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fHshN6fMzYo", ((443, "7:23–8:12"),), id: 466)
// U ML359:65-102 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("For example, if you look at the Hindu religion, there're different gods. There's a god with the elephant head, for example. These are not the gods that you believe in. So you don't believe in the Hindu gods. You don't believe in the Christian God, \"the father, son and holy spirit\". You don't believe in that as well! You don't believe in the Jewish god, necessarily, as well. The Jewish God has a bit of descriptions that I would say are deficiencies. I'll give an example.", "For example, God in the Old Testament according to the Jewish tradition was wrestling with Jacob, and Jacob was defeating Him and beating God, and God said 'Let me go', then he let Him go. And they said, 'Now you defeated God, you wrestled with God' (Genesis 32:22-32). And then God in the Bible had needs to be reminded by a Rainbow, for example, in the Old Testament (Genesis 9:13-16). He regrets creating human beings. Do you know what regret is? When you do an action that you do not know the outcome of, you regret it. That's what regret is. But God's All-knowing; how can God regret something when He's All-knowing? So I'm sure you don't believe in that type of God, that regrets, remembers by Rainbow, defeated by people. So when I say you believe in Allah, you do believe in Allah! Because all of these attributes, you don't believe in. So you believe in Allah.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “University Student Challenges Muslim On Religion! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0eOxOwACYXE", ((104, "1:44–2:07"), (133, "2:13–2:54"),), id: 467)
// U ML048:2-42 | The Muslim Lantern | 1
#passage(("We believe there's only one creator in the universe. One creator, Creator of everyone. People call the creator different names. The creator is one. The Christian God is the God of Jesus, the God of Abraham. Our God is the God of Jesus, the God of [Abraham].",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Englishman And Muslim Have An Honest Conversation About Immigration In Britain! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GgbY_TyTOTc", ((1, "0:01–0:22"),), id: 468)
// U ML207:285-311 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("There's no \"gods\", it's just ONE. If someone uses the term for something that isn't God, that doesn't mean there's now another God. All it means is that there's a misunderstanding of God. All it means is that there's a false idea that someone has of the Creator. I'll give you a very simple example. I can have a perception of you and I'll assume you're from Ghana. Another person has a perception that you're from Senegal. Another person has a perception that you're from Haiti. You are from one country. We have different perceptions about you; you're the same person, but some have false perceptions, some have true perceptions, based on where you're from.", "Now, the same thing with God. There's one God; different people have false ideas, false understandings, false perceptions, and some have a correct perception of what that Creator is. How can we know? The Creator has to tell you about Himself. So when you start telling me: \"I'm from this country\", then I know for a fact now you are from this country, and whenever anyone else makes another false assumption about you, that doesn't mean there's another Mark now! Just because he thinks you're from Senegal, that doesn't mean there's another Mark from Senegal. There is just one Mark, but there is a false understanding and a false belief about Mark. Same thing with the idea of the Creator.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Anonymous Atheist Attempts To Outsmart A Muslim! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WC2nmWKjHVQ", ((843, "14:03–14:39"), (883, "14:43–15:10"),), id: 469)
// U ML287:7-48 | The Muslim Lantern | 1
