#passage(("We don't believe God is a human being. Unlike Christianity, where it has been influenced by Greek mythology, Zeus and Thor and whatever, and then when Constantine adopted the Christianity, then he started introducing Jesus was God himself and God was a human being; we don't have that in Islam. So the idea that most people have in the west is a Christian idea. In Islam, Allah explicitly tells us in the Quran, chapter 112 of the Quran, Allah defines himself as the following: say Allah is uniquely one, independent, self-sufficient, everything depends on God, doesn't depend on anybody, he doesn't [beget] nor he's born, [unlike] us having human reproductive organs, and there is nothing like onto him.", "Allah tells us in the Quran do not give examples and parallels for Allah; there's nothing like Allah. Allah tells us in the Quran vision cannot encompass him and he encompasses all vision. Allah is unlike any deity or god that you might have heard, Hinduism or Christianity or whatever. In Islam, you have rules that you cannot liken Allah to his creation. This is the foundation of Islam. Anybody who likens Allah to the creation or thinks that Allah is like any of the creation is a disbeliever.", "Allah tells us in the Quran he doesn't need us. He's free. But he's given you goodness for you, for your own benefit. That's why I'm saying when we apply the Islamic commands, it's from our own benefit. It's not for Allah. Allah is the one who is self-sufficient and you are the ones in need of Allah. That's what Allah tells us in the Quran. That's why independent comes in the picture. When I define God to you, I said to you he's independent, needed by all existence. He doesn't need anything. He doesn't need anybody. We need the creator.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Buddhist Gets Defensive After A Muslim Highlights The Problems With Buddhism! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cCyN0gL4kEI", ((1370, "22:50–24:04"), (1444, "24:04–24:36"), (1488, "24:48–25:28"),)