#passage(("There's a difference. Difference there is that God isn't deficient, and the creation is deficient. When you say a realm, what are you thinking of? You're trying to restrict God to a form of something that humans exist in. We don't believe that. Just because there's a separation between us and God, that doesn't mean something restricts God. That doesn't follow. We exist in a realm that God has created. Now, outside that realm, if you're going to use that term, outside, and you're not going to think about the idea of space. Whatever we call space is this atoms and galaxies and stars and whatever. So, outside them, if you don't want to talk about outside them, can you even think about the idea of space? No, not really. We're saying right now we have the idea of space. We're saying God is not inside this atoms and space and galaxies and whatever, any of that. No. There's nothing that restricts God. So, just because we're restricted does not necessitate that God is also restricted.", "Let's have a better question to ask. How do you know about God if God doesn't tell you about himself? I'm not talking about the existence of God. I believe that's innate. I'm talking about the attributes and actions. Now you're going into details of what God does and doesn't do and what God is. So, I agree it's innate to know that God exists. So, that's something, but it's not innate to say that we innately know that everything is God and our body and soul. That's not innate. Where do you get that from?",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Claims That Pantheism Is More Rational Than Monotheism! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=C3BXt0zJr3o", ((1951, "32:31–34:13"), (2074, "34:34–35:23"),), id: 477)
