#passage(("If you mean omnipresent, he is in all of the creation, in everything. So, under my feet right now, I don't want to say this disrespectfully, but the god that you believe in is under my feet right now; I'm stepping on him. We don't believe that. We believe the Creator is transcendent. Allahﷻ is above everything, and Highness is an attribute of Majesty.", "God is Eternal, so nothing transforms anything into God. God was always All-knowing, always possessing His Knowledge. The attribute of Knowledge in God is eternal, meaning it has always existed. From the beginning, if you want to use the term \"beginning\" even when it doesn't apply to eternality, from the beginning and the start, using human language with its limitations, God was always knowledgeable. There's not a point in which God did not know something. But that's not Existence. You know, for example, that I'm here talking to you. Do I exist now inside your reality, or your mind? Do I now exist in a completely different universe or something? No! I exist where I am; you have the knowledge. Knowledge itself as an abstract concept, it's not like some \"I exist within you now\" just because you know that I'm talking to you, or that you know that I'm here, or you know that I have a YouTube channel or something. You can have Knowledge of something. Processing information does not mean that that physical entity now exists within you because you process that information.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Attempts To Explain The Concept Of God! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Y0EuiG8SUZM", ((398, "6:38–7:00"), (440, "7:20–8:32"),), id: 478)
