#passage(("God's Concept in Islam and Christianity is very different. This is a typical Christian answer, I would say, and the reason this answer is given is because Christians know their concept is illogical, so they have to make a new argument in which \"OK, it's illogical but no one can understand God\". So, that is a very common Christian argument, but the point is this. I usually say to them the following. First, let's talk about complexity. I would describe God with how He describes himself. I think the way that I described him, it's much easier to understand than to say uncaused cause.", "Muslims don't have this issue of saying we don't understand. We don't claim to understand God fully. But the Revelation that God gives us, we need to be able to understand. Otherwise it's unwise for Him to send us something we don't understand. It's like teaching a child quantum mechanics. A child does not understand, so it's unwise from you to try to give him something that is beyond his capacity of understanding.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Does The Quran Endorse Following The Bible?! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=H3iXYah0Nng", ((361, "6:01–7:29"), (466, "7:46–8:00"),), id: 480)
