#passage(("Prophet Muhammad is the last and final Messenger. We worship God, not any human being, and I said that because a lot of people think, for example, Christians worship Jesus, so some Christians have the misconception that we worship Prophet Muhammad, but we don't worship any human being. He's a Messenger ONLY, coming to deliver the Message of God. That's it. We worship God alone.", "Where does the Quran talk about this God, this human God, anywhere? Allah says in the Quran (alIkhlas112:1) (there's only One God), One Creator, Allah, which is not a human being. Allah defines Himself in the Quran, in chapter112:4, that He says: وَلَمْ يَكُن لَّهُۥ كُفُوًا أَحَدٌۢ, and there is nothing like unto God. Allah also says in the Quran in another place (ashShura42:11), لَيْسَ كَمِثْلِهِۦ شَىْءٌۭ (there is nothing that resembles God), nothing like God. So anything you see in the Creation is not God. So Allah defines Himself in the Quran as One God only, and that God is unlike anything, and is certainly not a human being. So anyone who believes that a human being is God is by default not a Muslim. This is polytheism. The biggest sin in Islam is to worship anything other than God.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Liberal Woman Debates Muslim On The Need For Religion! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kBJxu5UYcy4", ((1637, "27:17–27:43"), (1715, "28:35–29:35"),), id: 484)
