#passage(("That's not my opinion; you can ask any Muslim. Ask any Muslims, can a human being be God? If a human being can be God in Islam, we would not have an issue with the Christians of today, because the Christians of today believe Jesus, who is a human being, was God, part of the Trinity. That is what we argue with the Christians; every day we talk to them about Jesus not being God. So if we end up saying there's another prophet who is God, then there's no point of us discussing anything with the Christians. So that's common belief as well. No human being is God in Islam, PERIOD. It doesn't matter who that person is. Nobody is God.", "Prophet Muhammad, whom the Quran was revealed to, and who taught us how to understand the Quran, he told us: (Do not overpraise me, like the Christians overpraised Jesus and they made him God). A man said to the Prophet Muhammad \"what you will, and what God wills\". So the prophet said to him: \"Did you make me equal with God? Don't say this. Don't say me and God in one sentence,\" as if both of us make decisions. In Islam, Tawheed توحيد, this is the term we use, ABSOLUTE MONOTHEISM in worshipping One Creator Alone, is the PILLAR of the religion. This is what Islam is built upon.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Liberal Woman Debates Muslim On The Need For Religion! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kBJxu5UYcy4", ((1912, "31:52–32:25"), (1948, "32:28–33:04"),), id: 485)
