#passage(("When someone says Jesus Is God, there is a problem, because you're given the title of God. God is the all knowing. That's why when you call yourself God is a problem, because you're not all knowing. Your soul is not all knowing, [omniscient]. When we say God, God is not just the eternality, which is the post eternality related to the soul. The soul is not pre and post Eternal; it's post Eternal. God is both pre and post-eternal. The eternality of God is not dependent; our eternality is dependent on God. So there's a distinction between the post eternality that we possess and the one that God possesses. When we say God we include all the attributes: all knowing, all powerful, merciful, creator of the world, all of these things. So when you call anything else God, that is a mistaken identification of that thing, because that does not possess all of the attributes of what we call God.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Philosophers Challenge The Muslim Understanding Of God! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=agqDQQkQf2A", ((494, "8:14–9:09"),), id: 486)
