#passage(("There is a similar Narration that says (Adam was created on the image of Allah) خَلَقَ اللَّهُ آدَمَ عَلَى صُورَتِهِ. But our understanding of it is not like the Christian understanding of persons created in the image of God. There are multiple interpretations given by the scholars. Some of them would say, for example, that we do have attributes that are given by Allah, that Allah possesses, like the attributes of mercy or love or knowledge. These attributes we have is because Allah has given us those attributes.", "Other Scholars will say just because something is on the image of something else does not mean that it's like it. And we give an example of the Prophet, peace be upon him, Prophet Muhammadﷺ. He said for example that (The first group that will enter Paradise, they will be in the image of a full moon) أوَّلُ زُمْرَةٍ تَدْخُلُ الجَنَّةَ علَى صُورَةِ القَمَرِ لَيْلَةَ البَدْرِ. They are in the image of the moon in the night when it's full moon. No scholar would say that the believers will turn into a moon. But this is a likening in the image of an image; just because an image is resembling another image does not mean that now they look the same. So this is our explanation of this idea, while Christians would say no, \"in the image of God\" means actually God is a man, like they believe Jesus Christ is a man. We don't believe that.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist Irrational Criteria For God's Existence! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Xz7nptUD9Ug", ((916, "15:16–16:00"), (975, "16:15–16:50"),), id: 488)
