#passage(("We say Allah is above. We believe the throne is above everything; God is above everything. And by the way, highness is the attribute of perfection. It's why even in English you use the term looking down on someone; you look down on someone because when you're up, this is the attribute of perfection; when you're down it's an attribute of demeaning, it's a demeaning attribute. There's nothing that is above Allah. So he's above everything and everyone, both in status and in existence. Now when it comes to him being closer to us, that means in his hearing and his sight and his knowledge and everything he is closer to you, knowing everything, hearing everything, seeing everything, more than you would. That doesn't mean that we believe God himself is mixed within the universe. Why? It's a very simple reason: if I create a chair, do I become the chair or am I separate from the chair? I don't become the chair. I'm separate from the entity that I made, because I have to exist before.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Pantheist Challenges The Muslim View Of God! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=m4s4GlDTg28", ((582, "9:42–10:45"),), id: 492)
// U ML317:146-232 | The Muslim Lantern | 3
#passage(("If God's everywhere then he is in Heaven by definition. We believe that Allahﷻ is above His Creation; we do not believe He's mixed with His Creation. We don't believe He's in the Universe, we don't believe He's in everything like you do. So we don't believe that God is in the rapist, we don't believe that God is under my shoes right now. I'm not stepping on God, I don't believe He's under my sock. That's something that's not befitting the Majesty of the Creator. I don't believe He's in the toilet as well; that's something that does not befit the Majesty of the Holy Creator.", "Quran chapter 2 verse 115: this verse is talking about the Qibla, the direction of prayer, and if you do not know the specific direction of prayer, wherever you direct, Allahﷻ is there, meaning that Allahﷻ will accept your prayer if you do not know where to direct yourself. Wherever you direct yourself Allah sees you; that's what the verse means: فَأَيْنَمَا تُوَلُّوا فَثَمَّ وَجْهُ اللَّهِ. All of it is talking about the direction of prayer, which we call \"Qibla\". It's not talking about where Allahﷻ Himself exists; because Allah mentions clearly in the Quran in Surat Al-Mulk 67:16 أَأَمِنتُم مَّن فِي السَّمَاءِ (Have you felt safe of the One in the سماء, above). Allah mentions also in the Quran, Surat Taha 20:5 الرَّحْمَٰنُ عَلَى الْعَرْشِ اسْتَوَىٰ (He is above His Throne). So Allahﷻ explicitly mentions in the Quran that He is not mixed within the Creation, within the Heaven, this or that. He is above everything.", "We've got a very important rule that we apply when it comes to the Creator, is that: \"everything that you ascribe to Allah or negate from him needs evidence\". You've not seen God. Your mind which is limited is not an authority over God. You do not say what God is or can do, what he can't do, what he is, what he isn't, without God himself telling you what he is and what he is not. So I do not use the term limited or unlimited and this and that, because that's not in the Quran or in the Hadith. What is in the Quran is that Allah is separate from His Creation; Allah is above His عرش, above His Throne, above everything. Therefore that's what we believe and we stop there. I cannot use my mind to tell you exactly where God is and what attributes befit him and what does not befit him, because I'm a limited Creation. So I have to stick to what he told me; I have to limit myself to what he told me about Himself.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Sikh Challenges Muslim On The Preservation Of The Quran! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3FaWv_XB4Eo", ((390, "6:30–7:17"), (452, "7:32–8:19"), (566, "9:26–10:07"),), id: 493)
