#passage(("We don't say the Quran is eternal. We say the Quran is uncreated. These are two separate things. I don't take all your Muslim friends as a source; I take the scripture as a source. This is a clear misunderstanding of Christians of our scripture. What they do is that they misunderstand our scripture and then they introduce their theology into our scripture. When we say Allah's words are uncreated, we're referring to the speech of God, meaning God was always able to speak. It's not like the creation of God, one day God created the attribute of speech and he started to speak. No, God was always able to speak. This is the eternal part. When we say uncreated, meaning when God speaks, because God is uncreated, His words are also uncreated. This is our belief.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian in Complete Denial After a Muslim Shows Him This Verse! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kihhH9YMsRE", ((1217, "20:17–21:08"),), id: 507)

