#passage(("Concepts and attributes like love and hate do not exist in abstract. Meaning you cannot find love sitting down here today and shake his hand and say hello, how are you, and give it a hug. It has to exist within an entity, just like colors are also attributes. For instance, black does not exist in abstract; it has to be an object that we refer to as black, or a being that we refer to as black. So love: you cannot say God is love. God is loving, so he possesses the attribute of Love, cuz love itself does not exist in abstract, cuz it does not communicate or do or say. So you can say you feel like God is love, but it does not make any rational sense; it's not possible rationally to say that God is love.", "God is loving, but he's also just, and he just doesn't base things based emotions, because emotions can be right or wrong. There's the difference between the creation and the Creator: all wise, all knowing. There are many things you don't know, many things I don't know. And you think the Creator is a man? We don't believe that. Allah says in the Quran: say, Allah is uniquely one; Allah the independent, self-sufficient, everything depends on him, he doesn't depend on anyone; he doesn't beget, nor is he born (doesn't have children, doesn't have parents, have grandparents); and there is nothing like onto him. There is nothing like onto him, meaning anything we think about, anything we imagine, anything we see in the creation, Allah is unlike that.", "So you can't even imagine him. You can imagine, but your imagination is wrong, because it's based on your experience. You cannot imagine something outside your experience. Even fairy tale beings are just a combination of elements. For instance, you have this horse with a wing and whatever it is: just bring wing, which is an element that exists in a creation, and put it on a horse, and a horn, which exists in other creation, and put it. So even the imaginary things that we have is based on what we observe around us. So Allah is beyond all of that. But he has attributes we understand. We know what it means to be all knowing; we know what it means to be all powerful, and all of that.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Non-Muslim Lady Questions Muslim On Violence In Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UlHj8D6ex-Y", ((607, "10:07–10:53"), (653, "10:53–11:39"), (703, "11:43–12:26"),), id: 512)
