#passage(("I don't believe love exists everywhere. Love is an attribute; attributes do not exist in abstract. When you talk about love, which is an abstract concept, it exists within humans, that they possess the attribute of Love, or God possesses the attribute of Love, which means he's loving.", "I'm not saying love doesn't exist; I'm saying it's an [attribute]. That means you're saying an abstract concept has its own identity, which is not the case. Another attribute, power, knowledge, whatever attribute, do not exist in everywhere, as you're claiming about Allah attributs.", "The Rocks: they were created because God created everything in the world for the sustenance of the human. I've been given an attribute of Love by God, and God, he possesses the attributes of Love; he's loving, most loving. But the way you're thinking about it is that love is a concept that exists everywhere by itself, which is not the case. You're saying it's an outcome of love that The Rock exists, but that does not mean that love exists within the rock.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Philosophers Challenge The Muslim Understanding Of God! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=agqDQQkQf2A", ((563, "9:23–9:57"), (602, "10:02–10:28"), (633, "10:33–11:51"),), id: 513)
