#passage(("Your faith being rock solid means that you're able to answer any question that someone will come to you. You believe, for instance, that God is all knowing? The Bible says God knows everything. I think it's Matthew 7:21, where he says people come to him on that day, will say Lord, Lord, and then he says get away from me, I did not know you. So do you believe that God can be ignorant? Ignorance is the opposite of knowledge. Ignorance doesn't necessarily mean, for us as humans at least, something negative. But God should know everything all the time.", "So if the Christian understanding of God is a God doesn't know everything all the time, and Islamic understanding of God, that God knows everything all the time, it's a more perfect understanding by definition. I want God that knows me. So, God knows everything all the time, or he doesn't know: which one is it?",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Confident Christian Woman Attempts To Defend Christianity After Encountering A Muslim! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lT8zv4EK-fQ", ((682, "11:22–12:41"), (776, "12:56–13:16"),), id: 517)
