#passage(("That is our position on these issues, and I'm just explaining to you reasons we have these positions, and that's why they make perfect sense and they are in line with the teachings of the Quran. Because you say whatever is in the Quran is perfect, based on that, because it's from God. That's why you see it's making sense, and there's evidences for it, and supported by reasoning, because it's from God; it's not from me.", "So the question now is: if you base your morality on the Quran and you believe in God, what is the description of God you believe? Do you believe that God you believe in forgets, regrets, rests? Do you believe in these attributes, or do you believe that that [Creator] is all powerful, does not forget, therefore needing to remember; does not regret? Forgive? We believe in that as well, because the Quran starts, the beginning of every chapter, you say: in the name of Allah, the most beneficent, the most merciful. And the first chapter, you say twice: you say in the name of Allah, and then you say again in the second verse. So Mercy is essential part of Islam, but also Justice, and also punishment for those who deserve it, for those who do evil.", "So we look at everything in a balance. Allah, as the Quran says, he placed balance scales; that refers to the scales of judgment, but also refers to the creation: everything is balanced, everything is created in precise measure. That's what we believe. So if this is the case, and this makes sense to you, whatever is taught in here, and these teachings I was telling you about, God [resting] and forgetting, these are all biblical teachings, so how can someone say: all of the morality of Islam makes perfect sense, I believe in God and I believe in everything the Quran says, and I don't believe in the teachings of the [Torah], but I'm a Jewish person? How does that make sense to you?",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Ex-Muslim Transgender Confronts Muslim On LGTBQ! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/wa