#passage(("Many of what you said is not true; this is a misunderstanding of Islam. I'll give you an example. We only believe Allah creates: that's not true. The word create in the Arabic language is used for the creation as well, but only Allahﷻ can create from nothing. There's a difference: humans can shape things into different forms. The Quran explicitly uses the word \"creation\" for other than Allahﷻ. You claim Allah is the light; no, that's not what the Quran says. Quran says (An-Nour24:35): (Allah is the light of the Heavens and the Earth), the light of everything. There is a difference between saying it's just the light and the light of everything. Only Allah can speak in Parables: nothing in the Quran says that. So your list is completely a straw man list of things we don't believe in. The First and The Last are the titles used for Allahﷻ. Allahﷻ said that (Alhadid57:3): هُوَ الْأَوَّلُ وَالْآخِرُ (He is The First and The Last).",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Preacher Claims To Have Evidence For Christianity! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YRJIE9cDck0", ((2480, "41:20–42:06"),), id: 519)
