#passage(("Did they ever say that God is bound by something other than itself? That's a misunderstanding on your part. When they talk about law of non-contradiction, they refer that this thing is not possible in existence, meaning it cannot happen. It cannot be conceptualized; it cannot happen. If it cannot happen, then your question itself is contradictory. Not that there is an invisible law that exists, and the invisible law that restricts God. Nobody says that.", "Existence by definition is operating within rationality. Or does it operate within irrationality? Existence is governed by a certain specific consistent framework, rational framework, or things wouldn't be the way they are. You can become a banana tomorrow; right is wrong, or wrong is right; tall is short. No, there are certain things that govern existence, certain set of laws that God has put. So when you bring in a possibility that is against these governing laws, it makes no sense. It's a irrational scenario and possibility. It cannot happen within this realm of existence, because it follows these set of laws.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Confident Atheist Rejects Rationality In An Attempt To Disprove God! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xgMD6R0qr4g", ((125, "2:05–2:34"), (166, "2:46–3:29"),), id: 520)
