#passage(("He makes the claim that Allah is \"demanding something\", and at the same time, Allah \"needs it\". And both of them are false premises. Why? Because number one: if Allah \"demanded worship\" from us, then He could have created us worshiping Him! Because now we're arguing about a God that is All-Knowing and All-Powerful and All-Loving. Can an All-Powerful God create a Creation that worships Him all the time? Yes! He already did anyways, which is the Angels. So why would Allah demand our worship where He can literally make us worship Him? You see how stupid the argument becomes when you ask a very basic question?", "Then he says \"needs the worship\". Allah also says in the Quran (alKahf18:29) clearly: وَقُلِ ٱلۡحَقُّ مِن رَّبِّكُمۡۖ (And say that this is the Truth from your Lord) فَمَن شَاۤءَ فَلۡیُؤۡمِن وَمَن شَاۤءَ فَلۡیَكۡفُرۡۚ (Who wishes to believe, let him believe, Who wishes to disbelieve, let him disbelieve). Does that sound like someone DEMANDING your worship? Or does that sound like someone TESTING you? Telling you, you can either believe or disbelieve. There are rewards for this, there's punishment for this, and the choice is yours. How is that \"demanding\" worship?", "Now the \"need\": Allah explicitly tells us in the Quran that Allah doesn't need us. Allah says (Fatir35:15-16): یَـٰۤأَیُّهَا ٱلنَّاسُ أَنتُمُ ٱلۡفُقَرَاۤءُ إِلَى ٱللَّهِۖ (O mankind, you are the ones in need of Allah) وَاللَّه هُوَ الْغَنِيُّ الْحَمِيدُ (Allah is Self-Sufficient). Allah is self-sufficient! (If He wishes to remove you and bring a new Creation, He would) (And that is not difficult for Allah). Allah is refuting you again here, saying the point I was telling you: that if Allah wishes to replace us with another creation that worships Him, He can. He doesn't need us. So there is no need and there is no demand.", "Allah explicitly tells us on the Quran that these actions are for our benefit, for our guidance (alsra17:7). These prayers and good deeds that we're doing, all of this is for our guidance. It is not for Allah's benefit; He explicitly tells us that He doesn't need it from us.", "And I'll put this as a question for anyone who has any common sense or rationality: if God \"needs\", and like he says \"constant needs for glorification\", if He needs our glorification, then why does Allah not tell us to worship Him in the Afterlife? When the test in this life (which is whether we will obey God or not and worship Him, or we will choose disobedience), when this test is over, why does then Allah not require worship from us? Because according to you, He needs our constant worship and glorification! Then why does He just reward us and give us Paradise? The reason there is no more worship in the Afterlife, because it's no longer necessary for the test. Which means the worship was only necessary for the test; had nothing to do with the \"need\", that God needs glorification or whatever.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| 5 Reasons I Left Islam?! Hijabi Says Christians Will Go To Heaven?! | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wIhGWmIQTJY", ((1733, "28:53–29:27"), (1771, "29:31–29:58"), (1800, "30:00–30:32"), (1834, "30:34–30:45"), (1853, "30:53–31:50"),), id: 524)
