#passage(("3 conditions: Allahﷻ gives you permission; Allahﷻ is pleased with the person doing the intercession; He's pleased with the person that the intercession is done to. Only believers. I wouldn't use the word \"righteous\". Generally, a ‘believer’ is what we're saying, because it’s Allahﷻ's Will who He would accept intercession for, give permission to intercede. It's up to Allahﷻ. He determines, and He allows the person, to a believer only, to do an intercession. It's not like you're going to do an intercession for a disbeliever to enter paradise. It's not going to happen ever. So the other person has to also be a believer, because the believers, for example, would be punished for a period of time if they do evil and they die upon evil. That's not like you're just going to go to paradise like this, just because you're a believer. There's also punishment to purify you from these sins you didn’t repent from and stop.", "So an intercession could be a family member doing intercession for his other family members, for Allahﷻ to take them away from the fire, out of the fire, essentially. The Prophetﷺ, for instance, will do an intercession to take any of the believers off the fire. Anyone who believed, who had any atom of faith in his heart, there will be an intercession that will be done on the Day of Judgment, the Prophetﷺ will do, where people will be taken out. There'll be also other intercessions that the Prophetﷺ will do. So this is an example of an intercession that Allahﷻ would allow, that He told us about. And also Allahﷻ told us about, for example, a person who dies as a Martyr: he can do intercession, essentially, but he’ll be able to do intercession for some family members. So there're exceptions to that rule we're told about.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Enquires About Qur'an Contradictions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0shFTfDDiro", ((752, "12:32–13:37"), (821, "13:41–14:21"),), id: 571)
