#passage(("Define a Saint. How do you know who found favour in the eyes of God and who didn't? I'm trying to show you how that's an irrational belief, whether it is Catholicism, or Orthodox, whatever or whoever follows this idea of the existence of Saints. Why it is irrational? Because only God knows who is good in their heart or not, because these are internal things that no human being can see. Anyone can pretend to be good. That doesn't mean they're good. So you can say someone is a Saint, and he could be the most vicious, animalistic human being on earth. I don't need to give you examples with what some of these priests do with children or whatever; it's well known, very very well known. So these people, in the eyes of the people, before they're caught, they looked at the most pious people who are spending their lives calling people to the message of God and whatever. And when they die, maybe they will start making a statue for them as a Saint or whatever. But that person was living his life doing these things. The apparent is never a way for you to judge the Truthfulness and sincerity of an individual.", "Now, in Islam, there's a concept called ولي (Waliy). Waliy is someone who is, let's say, selected or chosen by God, very close to God. It's a status in Islam. It's not like a Saint. But in Islam, you cannot know who is a Waliy and who isn't, because Allah says in the Quran (Yunus10:62) أَلَآ إِنَّ أَوْلِيَآءَ ٱللَّهِ لَا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا هُمْ يَحْزَنُونَ (Indeed, the Awliya of God, there is no fear upon them, and they will not grieve). Then Allah defines them in the next verse (Yunus10:63) (those who believe or have faith, and they have God consciousness and piety in their heart). Now, we cannot know ever who these Awliya are by ourselves, because we cannot look in their hearts. So, that is the Islamic position. The only way you can know, for example, is through the text: if the Prophet, for example, says this person is a Waliy; in his life, he said this person is pious or this person is that, or he said he will go to paradise or something similar to that. So, through Revelation, ie God informing us through His Messenger or directly, this is how we can know whether someone is a Saint – I [don't] want to say Saint, this is the wrong term – is a waliy or not.", "By the way, there's many people who are called Saints in history, and you can look that they were not necessarily the greatest of people, that we'll discover later on. So, that's why in Islam, we don't have a concept like that, because nobody knows who has gained favour in the eyes of God and who didn’t. God hasn't told us!", "It's not a similar concept, because you're not allowed to call upon them when they're dead. You're not allowed to seek forgiveness from them and go talk to them and hold their stuff and have their pictures. All of this is POLYTHEISM in Islam. All of this is associating with God. All of it is extremely prohibited.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Orthodox Christian Surprises Muslim With Intelligent Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=P2cN0PEuavs", ((490, "8:10–9:49"), (594, "9:54–10:58"), (666, "11:06–11:25"), (696, "11:36–11:53"),), id: 573)
