#passage(("Behave like the righteous Companions, but don't mention their name when you pray, when you make دُعاء (Du'a: calling upon Allah). Don't seek aid from them; don't say \"Ali, help me, give me..\". Allah Subhanahu wa ta'ala says (Albaqara2:186) وَإِذَا سَأَلَكَ عِبَادِي عَنِّي فَإِنِّي قَرِيبٌ (If My servants ask you about Me..). We are servants of Allah. Allah says, (if My servants ask you about Me, say, \"I am near, I answer the call of the person who prays\"). Who answers? Allah answers! I don't call Ali, I don't call Omar. Even Prophet Muhammad, you don't go to his grave and ask him for help. Allahﷻ says in the Quran (Fatir35:14) إِن تَدۡعُوهُمۡ لَا یَسۡمَعُوا۟ دُعَاۤءَكُمۡ وَلَوۡ سَمِعُوا۟ مَا ٱسۡتَجَابُوا۟ لَكُمۡۖ وَیَوۡمَ ٱلۡقِیَـٰمَةِ یَكۡفُرُونَ بِشِرۡكِكُمۡۚ (If you call upon them – the dead or these people, righteous people that you call upon them – they will not hear your Du'a) (And if they heard, they cannot respond to you) (And on the Day of Judgment, they will disbelieve in your Shirk) – associating your partners with Allah – وَلَا يُنَبِّئُكَ مِثْلُ خَبِيرٍ (And no one can tell you more than Allah). This is the Quran; it's not my word. Allahﷻ says (Annaml27:80) إِنَّكَ لَا تُسْمِعُ ٱلْمَوْتَىٰ (Prophet Muhammad, you cannot make the dead hear). If the Prophet cannot make the dead hear, can we make the dead hear?", "When you pray to Ali in English, did Ali speak English in his life? When you pray in Turkish, does Ali understand Turkish? The answer is no! He was an Arab, he's a Qurayshi. He didn't speak any languages other than classical Arabic. Even those who speak to him in Arabic today, he would not understand them. Our Arabic has changed a little bit today. Number one, you gave Ali the attribute of understanding all languages, which is the attribute of Allah. Number two, you gave him the attribute of hearing all the voices. When you pray, and he prays, how can he hear both of you at the same time? Me and you we call, Allah hears us. You and me speak in any language; Allah understands it. That's Allah! The All-Knowing, The Supreme. Humans are not like that.", "Ali cannot aid himself. Only Allah can allow him to aid himself. His righteous deeds are the only reason Allah grants him success. And to us as well, Allah says your righteous deeds are going to benefit you (Annisa'4:122). Nothing else will benefit you! So when you call upon him, how do you assume he will answer you, if he can't understand your language or hear you? That's the شِرك (Shirk: ascribing partner[s] to Allah)! You say you believe in the Quran. Allah says that's Shirk – association of partnership – and Allah says he doesn't forgive that. Allah says He forgives every sin except that (Annisa4:48). How can you tell me \"I believe in the Quran\", and then the Quran says to you, don't do that, and you do that?",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Can You Call Upon The Dead in Islam?! A Conversation With Shia”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1hBChXORhQE", ((89, "1:29–2:44"), (169, "2:49–3:46"), (226, "3:46–4:21"),), id: 575)
