#passage(("There's this clip going on, and a missile went down or a fire shot or something. People had the microphone, and then he started saying a name they have for Ali. So imagine missiles are coming down; the first thing you think about: why don't you call upon the creator of the heavens and earth? Why don't you say ya Allah? If you're about to die – imagine I'm about to die – the last thing I want to say is the name of a human, whoever the human is, even if it's prophet Muhammad. That is even [shirk], to say prophet Muhammad.", "They bring a verse of the Quran: Allah says do not think those who were killed in the way of Allah dead; they are alive. But they don't finish the verse. It says: with their lord. If someone is with his lord, he's not in this life anymore. If he is with his lord, he cannot hear me, because he's not in this life anymore. When I say in the Arabic language, I am with my friend, it means I'm in my friend's house. I'm no longer here. In the Arabic language is for location. We believe there are three realms: the realm of this life, the [barzakh], which is a realm in between this life and the afterlife that the souls are in, and then the afterlife. So all of the believers that died upon belief are in the [barzakh].", "Like I said, this doesn't work in any way with the Quran, but let's take this interpretation. Let's say X is alive, a person who died, Ali or anyone you want to say, is alive. Even if I wanted to take this lousy interpretation, you are giving him divine attributes, because there's no way he's going to understand everyone, he's going to hear everyone, he's going to respond to everyone, unless this is the case. But they would say \"Allah gave him the ability.\" What's the difference between that and Jesus then?",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Sneako Questions The Muslim Lantern On Shia & Sunni Unity | The Iran War And More | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kdFNc6Jr6OQ", ((1788, "29:48–30:25"), (1834, "30:34–31:26"), (191