#passage(("There's another belief in which they say we call upon 'Ali as well, which is a very important thing to mention, because we say that can take you out of the fold of the religion: meaning that you can call upon someone who is dead and say \"help me\", \"aid me\", other than Allah. We say now, is there anywhere in the Quran that teaches you to do that, or says you can do that, or you should do that, to 'Ali or any of the Imams or anyone, even the Prophet?", "وَلَوْ أَنَّهُمْ إِذ ظَّلَمُوٓا۟ أَنفُسَهُمْ جَآءُوكَ فَٱسْتَغْفَرُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ وَٱسْتَغْفَرَ لَهُمُ ٱلرَّسُولُ لَوَجَدُوا۟ ٱللَّهَ تَوَّابًۭا رَّحِيمًۭا (anNisa4:64). I know the verse that you're referring to, by saying إذ... جاؤوك (they CAME to you). And إذ is used for the past tense, because they didn't come. So it's referring to something in the past tense. And it is \"coming to\", \"physically coming to\" the Prophetﷺ himself. But right now they don't go to the Prophet anyways. So this verse doesn't support them, because they go to 'Ali; they don't go to the Prophet. It is referring to going to the Prophet when he's alive, and referring to the Prophet seeking forgiveness for you. And the Prophet is not here today to seek forgiveness for you. So all of the things that are in the verse cannot apply today.", "But if I want to be nice, we'll say that this is referring to going to the Prophet. Prophets are not equal with the rest of the Creation. If something can be done with the Prophet, it does not mean that you can do it with the rest of the Creation. That's the first thing that we both agree on: the standard that Prophets have their own status and level, and things that they can do that we cannot do. So we're asking now for evidence for what they do, not what they say you can and you cannot. They go to 'Ali, and alHassan and alHussayn, these graves. Is there any verses, evidences for that?", "The Martyrs are not dead: وَلَا تَحْسَبَنَّ الَّذِينَ قُتِلُوا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ أَمْوَاتًا ۚ بَلْ أَحْيَاءٌ عِندَ رَبِّهِمْ يُرْزَقُونَ (alimran3:169) Do not think that those who are killed are dead.. they're alive. Allah says عند (with their Lord). So if they are عند for ظرفية, for the place (مكان), and they are with their Lord, not with you, then you cannot be talking to them. Do you know who's with you and who observes you? Allah! So now you're revealing the Truth that Shi'a worshiped the 12 Imams, and they give the characteristics of Allah to them. So this is the case: there is nothing in the Quran that would say you can do this.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Fully Dismantles The Shia Position! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=t7vhKiTrvNA", ((1232, "20:32–21:09"), (1297, "21:37–22:21"), (1344, "22:24–22:58"), (1382, "23:02–24:07"),), id: 578)
