#passage(("Let's be serious: if you're asking someone \"give me this book\", that means I know you can give me the book. When they ask Ali for something, they believe he can give them. I'm saying if you believe Ali can do Rizq, which is the attribute of Allah الرزّاق (Arrazzaq: The Provider), if you believe he can give you things, why do you need Allah?", "Personally, I know someone who heard a woman say in a mosque in Egypt – there are some people who are doing things like this, but not with Ali, with other people – she went and she said \"O..\" – a person called Badawi; they believe he's a righteous person – she said: \"O Badawi, I'm very upset\". He was supposed to respond, but he's dead! He's supposed to say \"why are you upset?\" Then she says: \"I've been asking you to give me a son, and you keep giving me daughters\". She believes a dead man in a grave is giving her sons and daughters. Allahﷻ says in the Quran (Ashurah42:49-50) يَهَبُ لِمَن يَشَاءُ إِنَاثًا وَيَهَبُ لِمَن يَشَاءُ الذُّكُورَ () أَوْ يُزَوِّجُهُمْ ذُكْرَانًا وَإِنَاثًا ۖ وَيَجْعَلُ مَن يَشَاءُ عَقِيمًا ۚ إِنَّهُ عَلِيمٌ قَدِيرٌ (He gives to whom He likes, women, female, and He gives whom He likes, male, or He gives you both, male or female, or He makes you not have children). That's an attribute of Allah! She's going to tell the man, you can give me these things.", "The 'Alawis are doing the same thing. There is no difference between those who are in Mecca worshiping idols, saying: these idols, we just make Du'a to them to bring us closer to Allah. The idols were a picture of someone who was dead. The difference is there's a picture, and you're doing it without a picture.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Can You Call Upon The Dead in Islam?! A Conversation With Shia”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1hBChXORhQE", ((753, "12:33–12:48"), (777, "12:57–13:43"), (823, "13:43–14:04"),), id: 580)
