#passage(("I'm worried about you. I don't want you to die, to go to Hellfire. I'm telling you, follow the Quran. You say, I believe it. I'm saying, read the Quran, and follow. I'm not saying, follow me; leave me, throw me in the bin. I'm nothing compared to anyone in the past. I just told you, the Quran says, Allah says, and the Prophet says: follow that, don't follow your forefathers. Wallahi (By God), they will not benefit you. Imagine a disbeliever is born here, and he says to you, my father was a disbeliever, I'm going to be a disbeliever. Wouldn't you tell him: \"Believe in Allah, you're going to lose\"? I'm telling you the same thing: your forefathers are not going to benefit you.", "Allah says on يوم القيامة (Yawm Alqiyyamah: the Day of Judgment), ('Abasa80:34-36) يَوْمَ يَفِرُّ الْمَرْءُ مِنْ أَخِيهِ (When you run away from your brother) وَأُمِّهِ وَأَبِيهِ (your mother and your father) وَصَاحِبَتِهِ وَبَنِيهِ (his wife and his children). If you run from your children and your wife, you leave it. لِكُلِّ امْرِئٍ مِّنْهُمْ يَوْمَئِذٍ شَأْنٌ يُغْنِيهِ (Every person has his own business); he cares about himself. Am I going to Hellfire, or am I going to heaven? You see Hellfire in front of you, you see people thrown in there, you see chains, you see angels, you see all of these things. You will not be thinking \"my forefather..\". Your forefather, he will tell you \"I never knew you\". Allah says (Azzukhruf43:67) الأخِّلاء (alakhila': the closest friends) are enemies on the Day of Judgment, except those who are pious, following the Quran. Be of those pious people. The Quran is what is going to lead you to leave this thing, calling upon Ali.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Can You Call Upon The Dead in Islam?! A Conversation With Shia”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1hBChXORhQE", ((453, "7:33–8:11"), (495, "8:15–8:59"),), id: 581)
