#passage(("Now imagine someone came up to you and told you that they believe in a being that controls all the atoms in the universe. Your reaction would be: you mean God, you're referring to God? And they would say: no, I'm actually not referring to God, I'm referring to my saint or my [Imam] that I make requests of; they have the ability to control all the atoms in the universe. So this person has this belief that this human has Godlike abilities.", "And not only that, but it goes beyond the polytheism that comes to mind, like Poseidon the god of the sea or Vulcan the god of fire, because these are limited compared to what this person is mentioning. We're talking about a saint that has control over all elements, all atoms in the universe, time and space. So they can bring the dead to life, they can switch the Sun and the Moon, they can do anything. Not even the polytheists in [Mecca] said this.", "Now this concept, that Allah subhana tala gave a human or a group of humans the ability to control all the atoms in the universe, this view: if you're going to claim that it's [not shirk akbar], then you can excuse anything as not [shirk].", "Usually when I speak to [Shias], even the ones that believe in this, they don't go around talking about it, because it's such a heretical, embarrassing, crazy belief; they just keep it to themselves. Now, not only does Daniel provide different defenses for it in order to undermine it, but he also tries to defend from the claim that he holds this belief, or holds a kufri version of this belief. He tries to make it again more [palatable], and you won't believe how he lies in order to do that. And I'm not even getting started with the other things that he spoke about, like, for example, saying that if you're a Muslim you can pray to Jesus.",), "Farid Responds, “Haqiqatjou is a Shirk Apologist”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nQExb2jL7uY", ((159, "2:39–3:11"), (195, "3:15–3:53"), (233, "3:53–4:15"), (265, "4:25–5:42"),), id: 583)
