#passage(("We believe the Quran is preserved. We believe in the prophets, Jesus, Moses, Noah, Abraham, Muhammad, all of these prophets and Messengers. Believe in the last day, the day of judgment: resurrection is going to take place, accountability for the Deeds, the end times; all of that is the concept of day of judgment. And the angels of God, the angel Gabriel, all of these angels. And Destiny: that things are happening under the word of God, and we're also choosing in the same time; we're not forced to do what we're doing.", "So these are the foundational Concepts in Islam. Five Pillars are to do with the actions; six articles of Faith are to do with the internal beliefs. And you [can't] be a Muslim if you don't believe any of these. You have to believe in all of these six articles of faith, and you have to do the Five Pillars as a Muslim. These are the Necessities.", "Prophet, like any other Prophet, is the vehicle of given revelation of God to the people. So essentially the messenger is called the messenger because it delivers the message of God. So Prophet Muhammad, there was one day Angel Gabriel came to him, and he was teaching the people, and he asked the prophet: [what] is Islam? And then he mentioned the Five Pillars. Then he says: what is [Iman], what is Faith? Then he mentioned six articles that you have to believe. And this is Angel Gabriel teaching the people, through God; the prophet is teaching the people foundations of religion.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Pantheist Challenges The Muslim View Of God! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=m4s4GlDTg28", ((235, "3:55–4:21"), (261, "4:21–4:33"), (289, "4:49–5:16"),), id: 590)
// U ML284:937-1009 | The Muslim Lantern | 5
#passage(("We know the diseases now; what are the cures of these diseases? The cures of these diseases: the first and most important thing to protect yourself from every disease, all of these diseases -The Shubuhat and the Shahawat-, is the عقيدة ('Aqeeda: Creed). What is 'Aqeeda?", "'Aqeeda Means the Pillars of إيمان (Iman: Belief): Believing in Allah, His books, His Messengers, The Revelation, Angels, اليوم الآخر (The Last Day), القدر (Predestination). These 6 articles, and 3 other things which the scholars add, are: The issue of the Sahaba, because of the disagreement that happened between us and the Shi'a; so they put it in the books of 'Aqeeda -our position of the Sahaba-. And then the issue of [Iman], because of the خوارج (Khawarij: The Dissidents outside Islam) and the مٌرجئة (Murjia: The Postponers), these deviant sects in the early Islam; so the Salaf, they put these issues in 'Aqeeda as well. And the issue of إمامة (Imama: Leadership), because of the Khawarij saying 'Uthman… and did Takfir (call him Disbeliever) 'Uthman رضى الله عنه (Radiya Allah 'anh: May Allah be Pleased with him), and they killed him. So these 3 مُلحقات (Extensions) with the 6 articles of Faith: this is the 'Aqeeda of a Muslim.", "You, as a Muslim, you need to know your 'Aqeeda. When I say to you: Who's Allah? You need to be able to tell me who's Allah. What's the Names and Attributes of Allah? You need to be able to tell me the Names and Attributes of Allah -Not all of them to say them by name, but to understand them-: to understand what we affirm from the Names of Allah, what we negate, what we accept, how do we understand these Names and Attributes, the meaning of these Names and Attributes of Allahﷻ ('azza wajal: Almighty and Majestic is He); that Worship is only singled out to Allahﷻ, you don't worship other than Allah, you don't call upon the dead people for helping you when they're not even there; they can not hear you. These things -these issues-, this is the Foundation of your Religion.", "To know what does believing in Allah means, and then to know what does it mean to believe in Prophets: Are these Prophets معصوم (Ma'ssom: Infallible) or not Ma'ssom, for example? What is the I'sma (Infallibility) for these Prophets? These Prophets and Messengers: What does it mean to be a Prophet or a Messenger? What's the difference between a Prophet and a Messenger? Are they the same level? These things are issues to do with the Prophets.", "The Books: Are these previous Books were corrupted, or not? Some Muslims today believe that we believe the Bible is mentioned in the Quran and the Bible is preserved! They think that the Quran affirms the Bible! Even knowing the Bible -the word \"Bible\"- is nowhere to be found in the Quran. They think we believe in the Bible because they've not studied! They don't understand what is believing in the Books, and the تحريف (Tahrif: Corruption) of the Books, and the levels of these Books. Are they all equal? What was written? Some of them were written by Allah, like the Torah التوراة (The Old Testament) was written by Allah: Allah wrote it with His Hand. It's a Hadith: وكَتَبَ التَّوْرَاةَ، وخَطَّ التَّوْرَاةَ بِيَدِهِ. In the Hadith there's a mention that Allah خَطَّ التَّوْرَاةَ بِيَدِهِ (He wrote the Torah with His Hands); that's what the Hadith is saying. So, some of them have been written directly by Allah; some of them are VERBATIM, the speech of Allahﷻ, like the Quran. We need to know: What is the Quran? Does the Quran have contradictions? Is it preserved? How is it preserved? Why are these other books changed? Where are the verses that say that these books are changed?",), "The Muslim Lantern, “The Situation Of The Ummah, The Disease & The Cure | Al Muwahiddeen Mosque - The Netherlands |”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0ycNKKOx2jg", ((3085, "51:25–51:41"), (3119, "51:59–52:42"), (3167, "52:47–53:18"), (3202, "53:22–53:42"), (3224, "53:44–54:41"),), id: 591)
// U ML239:866-929 | The Muslim Lantern | 4
#passage(("Believing in Allah requires four things. One of these things is believing in Allah's existence. Believing in Allah's existence has four evidences. Believing in Allah is the first article, so we're not yet talking about the other five articles.", "We need to take this matter seriously. There's an issue: there are people who are not spending time learning these fundamental things.", "Allah created you for this. Allah says they were only commanded to worship Allah alone sincerely. Allah says Allah created you only for that reason. Allah says he created the heavens and the Earth for that reason. Allah created seven, and he created the Earth, that the command of Allah descends. Why? So you can know that Allah is powerful, that you know Allah's attributes. He created all of this, you can know his attributes, and you don't know what believing in Allah means. It's a problem.", "We can talk about: these people are being bad, he stole my lunch, and this person is evil; and we can talk about these things. But we ourselves, our existence in this life: we do not know why we exist.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Aqeedah (Creed) And Its Significance In Islam | AIM Conference 2024 NJ | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ULnwXbVf_cM", ((2015, "33:35–34:06"), (2068, "34:28–34:37"), (2080, "34:40–35:21"), (2123, "35:23–35:35"),), id: 592)
// U ML239:3844-3891 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("Now, there are many people who criticize separation of certain things. They say: why do you separate believing in Allah? The reason is very simple: you do not need to believe in whatever number of Separation; you need to believe in the contents. Does anyone disagree with the contents of the Quran? If you disagree with the [contents], you're disagreeing with the Quran and Sunnah, how many you divide into. That's why I said, believing in Allah, I said three or four, because some people say three; some people say you don't have to say a specific number.", "[Sahaba] already understood by themselves naturally; they didn't need someone to divide \"this and this\" so you can easily understand. So these divisions are to make it easy. And some based it on this verse: we said the lordship of Allah; here, the worship, the actions that you do; the second part is the names and attributes of Allah.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Aqeedah (Creed) And Its Significance In Islam | AIM Conference 2024 NJ | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ULnwXbVf_cM", ((9185, "2:33:05–2:33:35"), (9247, "2:34:07–2:34:35"),), id: 593)

