#passage(("Here is a very important point, because here he confused the Islamic definition with the linguistic definition. So there is a technical definition to words, and there is a linguistic definition to words. So the word مُسلِم (Muslim) or Islam, it means submission – a Muslim is someone who submits. But Islam itself, from an Islamic worldview, when Allah uses the word Islam or The Prophet uses the word Islam, it doesn't mean just someone who submits his will to God; that can include so many different people. That word Muslim specifically means the one who believes in the 5 pillars and 6 articles of Faith. So a believer is the one who believes in 6 articles of Faith – A مُؤمِن (Mumin: Believer) – and a Muslim is someone who believes in the 5 pillars. And a Muslim can be a Mumin, a Mumin can be a Muslim; so every Mumin is a Muslim essentially. But when the two words are mentioned together, then we make a differentiation: that Islam refers to the 5 pillars and Iman refers to the 6 articles. That is a technical definition of the word Muslim.", "And we see this definition in the Narration of The Prophetﷺ, where Angel Gabriel himself comes to The Prophet, and then he's teaching the Companions the religion. And he says to The Prophet: what is Islam? Then The Prophet doesn't say \"submission to The One True God\" or \"submission to One God\". The Prophet says Islam is to testify there's nothing worthy of worship except Allah, and that Prophet Muhammad is His Messenger, then to pray 5 times a day: the 5 pillars of Islam. And then he asked him: what is Iman, faith? And then he says what are the 6 articles of Faith. So this is what a Muslim is.", "And he uses this wrong assumption, and based on this wrong assumption he is going to make a lot of issues and problems during his lecture. He's going to conflate a lot of different terms and a lot of different teachings, because he's mixing technical definition with the Islamic definition.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| Responding To Professor Jiang's Lecture On The Islamic Golden Age | Muhammed Ali!”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6SVGKQ-xiGs", ((448, "7:28–8:15"), (504, "8:24–8:52"), (534, "8:54–9:06"),), id: 594)
// U ML418:3-49 | The Muslim Lantern | 3
#passage(("We in Islam, we have something which we call \"Iman\". Iman is Faith. Iman to us is three things. Now, leave what people think. This is what Islam preaches. This is not Someone's subjective opinion. These are the conditions for someone to be a مؤمن, a believer in Islam.", "First is القَول باللّسان: statement with the tongue. First, you have to testify to what you believe in. You testify that Allah is The Only Creator. You testify that Prophet Muhammad is His Messenger, he was sent with the guidance, that the Quran is Allah's word. The second thing is you believe in the heart; التصديق بالقلب, which is affirmation in the heart. Affirming in the heart is the same thing you said with your tongue.", "Then the third thing is that you do the actions. These 3 things have to come together. If they're not present with one another, then there's an issue. You're not a believer in Islam unless you say the Shahada, which is Testimony of Faith. You're not a believer if you don't believe in your heart that Allah is The Creator, and the Prophet Muhammad is His Messenger, and the Quran is the Word of God. You're not a believer if you don't do any actions as well.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “A Christian Testimony About Islam Part 1! Muhammed Ali - Speakers Corner”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qLF3sGWkBek", ((18, "0:18–0:33"), (38, "0:38–1:08"), (93, "1:33–1:56"),), id: 595)
// U ML284:1095-1145 | The Muslim Lantern | 3
#passage(("The actions are part of Iman. There're many Ahadith on that. Just read the beginning of Surat alAnfal, where Allah mentions the Deeds and then He says that this is Iman. Allah says (alAnfal8:3-4) ٱلَّذِينَ يُقِيمُونَ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ.. أُو۟لَـٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلْمُؤْمِنُونَ حَقًّۭا (Those who establish prayer.. Those are the True Believers). And Allah mentioned Deeds, actions that you take, you do with your limbs. Prophetﷺ he said that: الإيمان بِضع وستون، أو بضع وسبعون شعبة -two narrations- (They are 70 odd or 60 odd things, branches). And he says one of them is removing the أذى (Harm) from the طريق (Road). It's an action: you remove harmful things from the road. That's Iman.", "So, if the people understood that, they would understand you can not say \"my heart is clean, and I'm a believer, I'm good..\" when you're not praying, when you're committing Zina, committing all of these Deeds. Because a lot of people, they want to counter the diseases in the Ummah, like Liberalism, Feminism, and all of that, with rationality. But the true disease is that the Ummah are empty in their hearts; that's why it can be filled with rubbish and garbage. If it was full, it would never soak anything.", "Either Sheikh alIslam Ibn alQayyim or Ibn Taymiyyah mentioned in this example. He said: You have this thing that you use to wash your clothes, the sponge. The heart is like a sponge. If you fill it with water, when you pour more water, is it going to absorb anything? It's not going to absorb. It has absorbed all the water in it. Or a glass: if you fill it, the glass is full! So when you get all of these problems -that people have trying now to infect your heart with-, your heart is full: full of Iman, full of 'Aqeeda, full of the Quran, full of Hadith. It's not going to seep through. But because the Ummah's heart is empty, the right way to deal with these problems is to teach them their own religion, so they understand why they believe what they believe.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “The Situation Of The Ummah, The Disease & The Cure | Al Muwahiddeen Mosque - The Netherlands |”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0ycNKKOx2jg", ((3562, "59:22–59:57"), (3601, "1:00:01–1:00:29"), (3633, "1:00:33–1:01:16"),), id: 596)
