#refbox("Reference text: Quran 4:59, quran.com (Saheeh International)", (("4:59", "O you who have believed, obey Allāh and obey the Messenger and those in authority among you. And if you disagree over anything, refer it to Allāh and the Messenger, if you should believe in Allāh and the Last Day. That is the best [way] and best in result."),))
// U ML239:1902-1984 | The Muslim Lantern | 3
#passage(("The second principle is that there is no difference between evidences when it comes to acceptance. Meaning, the Hadith of the Prophet sallallahu alaihi wasallam: if I bring you a Hadith of the prophet sallallahu alaihi wasallam, and it's authentically attributed to him, do you have any choice in rejecting it? Or you going to say, \"this Hadith, maybe the meaning is different, let me change the meaning\"? Or should we adopt that, accept it? What about if only one companion is narrating it? Do we say \"it's just companion\", or do we accept it?", "So, unlike the people from [misguidance]: they have set principles for the narrations that they would accept in Creed, in the names and attributes of Allah and everything. They would say, \"unless it's ex number of people, we can reject this.\" We say no: if a companion of the prophet sallallahu alaihi wasallam told us something about the Prophet, The Prophet said it, we accept it. Allah says in the [Quran]: whatever the prophet gives you, you take; whatever he [forbids] you from, you leave it. So if Allah is telling us that, why didn't Allah tell us: what the prophet gives you, based on how many chains of narration [transmitting] it, you accept it? Is that what Allah said? No.", "So we have people who differentiate: 5% of the sunah is [mutawatir], which means it's mass transmission from the Prophet sallallah wasallam, a mass transmission of people in every level of the chain, and they were based on the experience; they directly took it from the prophet. They cannot fabricate it or make it up in any way. They would say: if it's not [mutawatir], which is 5% of the Sunnah, we're not going to accept it. We don't care what you accept, what you don't accept: if the prophet sallam said it, and the scholars for 1,400 years [approved] that this is authentic Hadith, then what do we do? We believe, we accept, and we believe in the contents of that Hadith.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Aqeedah (Creed) And Its Significance In Islam | AIM Conference 2024 NJ | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ULnwXbVf_cM", ((4486, "1:14:46–1:15:24"), (4527, "1:15:27–1:16:11"), (4571, "1:16:11–1:17:23"),), id: 602)
