#passage(("I think that they are misguided and it's not about my opinion, it's about the fact that they go against the Quran and the Sunnah. I know what I'm saying is the truth, based on evidences. It is not just an opinion. There is a difference between تأصيل الحكم and تنزيل الحكم: difference between saying this is the ruling and then putting that ruling on a specific individual.", "بدعة (innovation) is misguidance and misguidance leads you to Hellfire. There's no doubt about that. But it doesn't mean that every single person who does a بدعة, that ruling applies to him. Not necessarily: there are people doing بدعة out of ignorance, people doing بدعة out of تأويل (interpretation), people doing بدعة out of many reasons. So you're making a correlation that doesn't work islamically; you need to study الأصول (Principles of Islamic jurisprudence) to understand this.", "Just because there's a ruling, it does not mean we apply that ruling to everyone who might do that. Just like if someone does a certain كفر (disbelief) act does not necessarily mean that person is a كافر (disbeliever). He might be doing it out of ignorance, he might be doing it out of تأويل. There are things that are called موانع الكفر. And تبديع (to innovate) is one of these things as well. I don't say someone is a مبتدع (innovator). I'm saying the group, based on their beliefs. I'm not talking about individuals. I'm opening the books of the أشاعرة, seeing what they believe.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Aggressive Ashari Interrogates Muhammed Ali On Stream!”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=k7SGfzzryjY", ((24, "0:24–2:10"), (133, "2:13–2:32"), (153, "2:33–2:52"),), id: 611)
// U ML354:147-194 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("Al-Razi rejects this hadith that is narrated by around 5 companions, and it's in Bukhari! Even if one companion and آحاد, it's still in Bukhari, which is the most authentic book of hadith. Now, al-Razi, he accuses the narrator of [lying]. He said, \"How would you accuse Ibrahim عليه السلام of lying? You should accuse the narrator of lying.\" And then he calls أهل السنة, people of us who believe in the Sunnah, Hashwiyyah حشوية (A derogatory term used by opponents of Ahlu al Sunnah). The hadith is in Bukhari, it doesn't matter what he believes.", "I don't consider al-Razi from أهل السنة. أهل السنة are the people of Sunnah. He rejects the Sunnah. How can you be from أهل السنة when you reject the Sunnah? Even the Quran! He says, even the Quran, if it goes against the intellect…",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Aggressive Ashari Interrogates Muhammed Ali On Stream!”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=k7SGfzzryjY", ((324, "5:24–5:52"), (373, "6:13–6:35"),), id: 612)
