#passage(("His question: he said a lot say that [Asharis] are majority, a lot of the previous civilizations or rulers in Islamic history, etc. What is the response to this?", "Let's demonstrate this fact: how many people sitting down here know their beliefs and can tell me about their books? How many people actually know about them, actually know what they believe? Raise your hand. 1, 2, three. Majority of the umah? If you go to the random person in the street and you ask him, he's going to say to you, \"Is that a food, a dish I'm going to eat on dinner, or what?\" Majority does not know their hand from their leg. This is a false claim in every measurement. You go, ask the people, you'll see.", "Now we say the first 300 years of Islam had the best of generations with the testimony of the Prophet, but there was [no Asharism], because the principles that he said in his books was not said before. And for you to claim that they believed them, you have no proof for that; you cannot bring proof for that. We say we believe the same thing, the same statements: we bring the statements and we say we believe it. You introduce new principles and you claiming that they believed it; you cannot prove that. This is what we respond to them by, this very quick response; we don't want to go into much detail.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Aqeedah (Creed) And Its Significance In Islam | AIM Conference 2024 NJ | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ULnwXbVf_cM", ((10176, "2:49:36–2:49:52"), (10194, "2:49:54–2:50:35"), (10244, "2:50:44–2:51:27"),), id: 615)
