#passage(("I wanted to give him a verse from the Quran. It's the last advice from the Quran. Allah عز وجل says in the Quran – Luqman عليه السلام, when he was giving advice to his son – he said: “وَٱغْضُضْ مِن صَوْتِكَ ۚ إِنَّ أَنكَرَ ٱلْأَصْوَٰتِ لَصَوْتُ ٱلْحَمِيرِ” [Quran31:19] (And lower your voice, indeed the worst of voices or the most despicable of voices is the voice of a donkey). He was raising his voice. So, it’s not from the آداب (good manners), from the أخلاق (good ethics) to do that.", "Why did I allow him to speak? For a few reasons: the first reason is, والله, we want guidance for everyone. We ask Allah عز وجل to guide everyone. Sometimes we are in misguidance, we don't know we are in misguidance. The second thing, the reason I wanted to do that is I wanted to show you those people who always call themselves Asharis, when they’re put on the stand, when they’re actually challenged about their beliefs, they don't know what they're talking about.", "They will reject what the Quran says, they will reject what the Hadith says, they will reject what the Salaf say: “Oh, Ibn Hajar said.” Al-Bukhari is from Salaf, and he’s saying what the Salaf are saying, and you are telling me about what Ibn Hajar says? If you brought Ibn Hajar today, he will say to you, “Follow what al-Bukhari says.” I had a long experience with them. They’re very, very rude. And you can see from their manners, you can know enough about their beliefs. May Allah guide us all.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Aggressive Ashari Interrogates Muhammed Ali On Stream!”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=k7SGfzzryjY", ((1589, "26:29–26:50"), (1614, "26:54–27:14"), (1640, "27:20–27:50"),), id: 616)
