#passage(("In Islam, there are things which can be visible to us as human beings when we are in this period of the test that we're living in right now, and there are things that are not visible to us. For instance, you would consider Paradise and Hellfire from the Unseen World, because we haven’t seen them but we still believe in them. We'd consider the Angels to be from the Unseen World, because they are beings that exist, in fact, they are around us, but we do not see them; therefore they are from the Unseen World. You can say the Creator is from the Unseen World, because we've not seen the Creator with the physical eyes that we use.", "Now many of these unseen things are going to become seen, for example after Resurrection. So we will see Hellfire, we'll see Heaven, we'll see Angels, we'll see many things that we do not see right now. Allah in the Quran mentions, in many different places, that there are Creation that we don't know. In chapter:16, for example (Surat anNahl16:8), after Allah mentioning the horses and animals that we see, Allah says (and He creates that which you do not know). So, there are creations that we are not aware of, that we've not seen ever in our life.", "Allah says in the Quran (alAaraf7:54) that He created the Heavens and the Earth. And we believe there are 7 layers of what we refer to as Heaven, which is the sky above, or the universe, or whatever term you want to use to it. We're just in the first lower one. In these seven, Allah mentions in the Quran (ashShura42:29) that He puts creation in them: وَمَا بَثَّ فِیهِمَا مِن دَاۤبَّةࣲۚ (Allah put in them Creation). \"Dabba\" is a term for something that makes a noise when it walks the earth. It's a creation, essentially. So Allah mentions that there are multiple creations like that.", "So there are many things that are from the unseen, meaning they are beings or things: it can be objects, it can be beings. It can be the Throne of God, for example, something we've not seen. It doesn't have to be a living being. But there are many things and beings that we have not seen, and the reason we believe in them is that we believe in what we're told. So there are many things of the Unseen World, though, we're not told about, so we have no clue what these things are; but we believe in what we're told because it comes from the Creator.", "If you mean the mind, then yes, we do not know what goes in the mind of other people, but only God knows. But I wouldn't necessarily use the term unseen for it, because the mind is not something to be seen anyways. That's a different question now, if you're talking about consciousness and the mind: is it a physical thing that you see anyway, so we can put it under objects of seen and unseen?", "We can see them. Can't we see them under a microscope? If the human being can see something, any human being, then it falls on the seen world. It's still seen; we’re talking about macro and micro. If you see something on a micro level is the same thing: I still saw it even if I don't see the minute details. Like a human body: I don't necessarily see every single atom of the body, but we still say that we see the body. So micro and macro don't change.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist Philosopher Challenges Muslim On The Creation Of The Universe! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Zm8zgi2WPO4", ((101, "1:41–2:08"), (135, "2:15–2:54"), (180, "3:00–3:29"), (211, "3:31–3:57"), (273, "4:33–4:56"), (319, "5:19–5:53"),), id: 617)
