#passage(("A metaphysical reality is wider from a Muslim point of view. Interaction with God is something that is metaphysical. You interact with the metaphysical essentially, if you want to use that term \"metaphysical\", with God; also with Angels, also with Jinn – you want to call them \"demons\" or you want to use a different term. These are also things which are not physical, but there's a level of interaction that takes place as well.", "Heaven is an actual place but it's not in this world. We believe it's above. There are seven layers. On top of these seven layers you have Heaven there. But it's an actual place that is created, where you will have actual gardens, you have actual rivers, you have actual rewards. It's an actual place that people will go to. After they're resurrected they will go there, either there or, of course, Hellfire.", "The Soul: it's a metaphysical thing. What we call the Soul is not a physical reality; it's not something you can touch and put under a microscope, or see.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Attempts To Explain The Concept Of God! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Y0EuiG8SUZM", ((725, "12:05–12:30"), (761, "12:41–13:01"), (804, "13:24–13:30"),), id: 618)
