#passage(("The general rule is you cannot do [tamthil] with something you've not seen and you've not been told about. So you will be speaking now about things you'll be lying about. Because you are likening these unseen beings or unseen things: if they're unseen things, you're likening them or you're giving examples to them, you're saying it's like this even though you have no proof; you're lying essentially. It also falls under: angels are male. Who says angels are male? There's nothing in the Quran that says this terminology.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Aqeedah (Creed) And Its Significance In Islam | AIM Conference 2024 NJ | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ULnwXbVf_cM", ((9427, "2:37:07–2:37:52"),), id: 619)
