=== 10.2 The nature of the jinn
// NODE P02.C04.S02
#author("The Muslim Lantern")
// U ML026:29-85 | The Muslim Lantern | 6
#passage(("The topic of the jinn is a very fascinating topic. The idea of the unseen in general is something that always captivates humans. It's something that makes us curious, that we want to learn about it. And idea of jinnkind, the word is very specific to Islam, but it refers to these beings that exist with us, that live with us, that we cannot see. And you can see different civilizations throughout human history that talked about similar things. Whether you want to look at Christianity and Judaism, for example, they have the idea of demons and the idea of Satan. If you want to look at the Japanese, they have these ideas of spirits or spiritual beings or ghosts. These are all terms used to describe the same thing.", "So, the jinn is a creation that God has created. It is other than human beings, that exists with us in the same world, in the same realm, but we don't see them. However, they have influences on our life. Sadly, there's a lot of myths, there's a lot of false information out there about the jinn and their interaction with humans, how they can influence us. It's a part of our faith and belief to know how we interact with the jinn, how much influence do they have on us, what kind of interactions takes place on a daily basis between us and them.", "The first thing I want to say is that the jinn is an unseen world. The jinn are created from smokeless fire. So, they can do things which we cannot do: they can go through objects, they can possess, they can shapeshift. They have certain things that they're able to do that we are not able to do. However, they are an unseen world. So, the things that I'm telling you right now about them are based on the Quran and Sunnah. It's based on what the Prophet told us, it's based on what Allah told us. Why? Because they are an unseen world. And if it is an unseen world, then you cannot use reasoning, you cannot use guesswork, you cannot use personal experience to come to a conclusion and say that the jinn is like this or the jinn is like that.", "Allah says in the Quran, \"Satan or the jinn, they see you from where you don't see them.\" So, they are able to see us, but we are not able to see them. But, the world of the jinn is very similar to our world. It's quite like our world in reality. So, from the jinn, they have righteous people and they have people who are not righteous. That's why Allah says in the Quran – and the jinn speaking about themselves in the chapter Surat al-Jinn – they say that from us are the righteous and from us other than those who are not righteous. And we were different sects, different groups. And from us are the Muslims, the believers, and the disobedient ones can be anything. So, from among them there is the disbeliever, the atheist, the Jew, the Christian. They have all of these different religions and beliefs and ideas.", "And the prophet is sent to them the way he's sent to us. So, they're all commanded to follow the prophet Muhammad. And that's why in the Quran you see Allah: \"When we sent you a group of the jinn listening to the Quran.\" So, when they came, they said, \"Listen.\" And when [the recitation] was over, they went back to their people. They went back to the other jinn. And they said, \"We heard the book after the book of Moses guiding us.\" So, the Quran is a guidance sent to them, and they are commanded to follow the Quran, all of them, the way we are commanded to follow the Quran. They are commanded to follow the teachings of prophet Muhammad the same way we are commanded to follow these teachings.", "That's why Allah says that the prophet sent as a mercy to al-alameen. And you see in the Quran Allah addressing the jinn and the mankind. For example: \"Which of the favors of your Lord do you both deny?\" Referring to mankind and jinn. And that's why, if we understand this idea – that they're also commanded to follow the same sharia, the same that we are commanded to follow – that makes it easier for us to understand the world more and then to make assumptions about them.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “How To Protect Yourself From Jinn, Possession, Magic & The Evil Eye In Islam - Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dDdEEnJpWmI", ((100, "1:40–2:20"), (140, "2:20–3:07"), (187, "3:07–3:47"), (227, "3:47–4:41"), (281, "4:41–5:18"), (319, "5:19–5:53"),), id: 623)
