#passage(("We believe the Jinn are not a creature that you can put under a microscope, for example. Allah says in the Quran that they see us from where we don't see them (Ala'raf7:27), and they're created from fire (Alhijr15:27). So, they're not created from dust as we’re created from dust or clay (Alhijr15:26). So they don't have the same substance as us.", "When you ask for evidence, which a lot of people do, who come from an Atheistic perspective, they mean scientific evidence. And they don't understand that science is a method that studies the physical only, the materialistic only; therefore it has to be something that you're able to put under a microscope or measure with the five senses. So when you ask for that sort of evidence, you're using a wrong measurement to find the evidence for something that doesn't fit that criteria.", "You will find people who experience supernatural things in their life; this is something that is very well known. Especially you see the people who take all of these drugs and mushrooms and all of these things, that they tend to see different things that they refer to as aliens, which in reality probably they're seeing Jinn; the Jinn are telling them to do specific things. So people come in contact with these things; there's countless numbers of personal experiences that people can tell you about this.", "So if the Quran is true, then by extension, it mentioning the Jinn becomes a fact, objective fact. It being something mentioned in the Quran is evidence. The second thing is all of these supernatural experiences that people have and encounter, because it's not one or two experiences. It is a common experience and a common pattern that happens on a wide scale of different individuals. They report similar things, which shows that this is something that is actually real and it takes place.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Popular Youtuber Asks Muslim Difficult Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S7bA8bsNs20", ((1457, "2