#passage(("The misunderstanding is arising from the misconception that you think that Satan was an angel. Satan was never an angel in Islamic worldview. Satan was always a jinn. It's a Christian concept where they believe in fallen angels and that Satan – Lucifer – was an angel, and then he rebelled against God and all of this stuff. This is a Christian concept. In Islam, this is not the case. Allah explicitly says it in the Quran (alKahf18:50): كَانَ مِنَ الْجِنِّ (he was from the jinn) فَفَسَقَ عَنْ أَمْرِ رَبِّهِ (then he disobeyed his Lord). So he was from the jinn, Allah clearly says in the Quran.", "Why is Satan not an angel, for a fact – because there are even some Muslims who are confused there, and they may think he's an angel – what are the evidence that he isn't? There are 3 evidences in the Quran. The 1st evidence is that Allah describes angels in the Quran to be beings that don't disobey Allah. Allah says in the Quran (atTahrim66:6) لَّا يَعْصُونَ اللَّهَ مَا أَمَرَهُمْ وَيَفْعَلُونَ مَا يُؤْمَرُونَ (They don't disobey any command that God gives them and they do as they're commanded) بَلْ عِبَادٌ مُّكْرَمُونَ (The righteous servants, the honored servants..) (alAnbiya21:26-27) (They don't precede Allah in speech. They do as they're commanded..). That's the description given in the Quran. So angels never disobey God. It cannot happen. It's not a possibility. They can't disobey the Creator. So that's the first reason that we know that he couldn't have been an angel.", "Num:2 is, Allah explicitly says in the Quran: كَانَ مِنَ الْجِنِّ (that he was from the jinn). So Allah explicitly tells us that he wasn't an angel.", "Now the 3rd reason is that he says in the Quran خَلَقْتَنِي مِن نَّارٍ وَخَلَقْتَهُ مِن طِينٍ (alAaraf7:12) – about Adam – (You created me from fire and you created him from clay). So if Iblis, Lucifer or Satan, is created from fire – the Prophet told us that the angels are created from light – so he cannot be an angel if he's created from fire. He told us the jinn are created from fire. So now we know for a fact that he's a jinn: because Allah said so, because he disobeyed God, and because he's created from fire. So there's no doubt that he was from the jinn. But many scholars would say he was doing righteous deeds, doing good deeds, and then he was elevated to be among righteous servants like the [angels].",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Truth Seeker Presents Muslim With Genuine Questions About Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fbAbWBPDY6M", ((132, "2:12–2:49"), (169, "2:49–3:27"), (212, "3:32–3:37"), (219, "3:39–4:11"),), id: 630)
