#refbox("Reference text: Quran 2:102, quran.com (Saheeh International)", (("2:102", "And they followed [instead] what the devils had recited during the reign of Solomon. It was not Solomon who disbelieved, but the devils disbelieved, teaching people magic and that which was revealed to the two angels at Babylon, Hārūt and Mārūt. But they [i.e., the two angels] do not teach anyone unless they say, \"We are a trial, so do not disbelieve [by practicing magic].\" And [yet] they learn from them that by which they cause separation between a man and his wife. But they do not harm anyone through it except by permission of Allāh. And they [i.e., people] learn what harms them and does not benefit them. But they [i.e., the Children of Israel] certainly knew that whoever purchased it [i.e., magic] would not have in the Hereafter any share. And wretched is that for which they sold themselves, if they only knew."),))
// U ML314:755-783 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("So we believe that there is something Supernatural called Magic, and there are certain practices that a person can do in order for him to do certain effects to influence other people. But they can only influence other people with the Will of Allah. Magic is something created by Allah, but it cannot have a power except if Allah allows it to have power. For example, I have power – physical power – but I cannot harm anyone except if Allah is allowing me to do that action.", "Even the Devil is created by God; everything is created by God. But people can use magic in a way to harm other individuals, to harm other people, and then Allah can protect those people, or Allah can allow it to happen as a test for that individual. But in order for someone to use Magic, they have to commit disbelief: they have to, for example, sacrifice to other than God. That is the only way someone can do Magic: because you commit disbelief, and then you can use Magic. There are certain things that you can do, and there are certain ways to protect yourself from Magic in Islam, as well certain things that you can say that Allah can protect you and shield you from Magic happening.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Does Jesus Possess The Attributes of God?! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2Jp6DQffnZg", ((2294, "38:14–38:34"), (2330, "38:50–39:31"),), id: 637)
// U ML174:130-189 | The Muslim Lantern | 3
#passage(("Black magic: we don't call it black magic. The reason we don't use the term black magic is because people use it as if there is good magic and bad magic, and the bad magic is the black magic. No, in Islam all magic is bad magic, so it's just magic. Magic does not allow you to know the future. Magic is more of an influence you have over other beings, for instance other humans: you can make them visualize things that are not real, for instance. This an example of magic that we've seen in the Quran, where Moses, for example: we had The Magicians, and [it seemed] to him that the sticks were actual snakes. That's a form of magic. For instance, magic to separate between you and your wife, as Allah mentions in the Quran.", "And magic, in which you connect with Jin: Jin do not know the future. And Allah says explicitly in the Quran: when Solomon – Allah's given him the ability to control the Jin, to make them work for him – Allah said when he died, the Jin, if they knew the Unseen, they would have found out that he died, because they didn't know he died until the stick in which he was reclining on fell, and he fell. He was sitting down on his throne. So they didn't even know that he died. So Allah saying: if they knew the Unseen, they would have not continued to work while he was dead. So even the Jin do not know the Unseen.", "And if doing magic will make you know the future, the world we're living in will be different: everyone will go to this casino and just empty all the money inside. You'll control the whole world, because you would know the future through that. But nobody knows the future, through magic or otherwise. And plus, if you say you believe in magic, you're [bringing] a hypothetical example which has no proof. So [what] is the alternative? Because if there isn't an alternative, then he has to be a messenger.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Pakistani Ex-Muslim Confronts A Muslim On Following Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9vJWVgYof2A", ((263, "4:23–5:06"), (306, "5:06–5:51"), (351, "5:51–6:21"),), id: 638)
#author("Farid Responds")
// U FR231:465-545 | Farid Responds | 2
#passage(("The first thing: it seems like he's conflating between [hasad] and black magic. These are two completely different things. And he's basing his rejection of the existence of black magic in our times due to his lack of experience with it, or he's never come across it. This is not a reason to reject the existence of black magic. I've never seen anything myself; I've seen some really funky things that I can't explain, but I wouldn't necessarily call it magic.", "And it's quite worrying when someone's going to reject the existence of it today simply because they've never come across anything of that nature. I know people that have come across that, and almost everyone knows someone that's come across that, people who aren't even religious. I know people have non-religious family members who share stories of the supernatural. So I have no reason to reject that.",), "Farid Responds, “Shocking Views of Shabir Ally”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uHU5W5UVHkQ", ((1020, "17:00–17:41"), (1076, "17:56–18:28"),), id: 639)

=== 10.5 Jinn possession and ruqyah
// NODE P02.C04.S05
#author("The Muslim Lantern")
// U ML026:86-228 | The Muslim Lantern | 18
#passage(("Someone can ask the question, \"Can the jinn harm humans? And are they accountable for that if they choose to harm a human being?\" First we need to understand that there are two types of harms that the jinn can cause: one that is visible and one that is hidden. For example, a hidden type of harm is that the jinn can eat with you when you're eating. And then the barakah, the blessing in the food, is decreased because the jinn is eating with you. For instance, when you sleep, they can show you nightmares and bad dreams, and that is a form of them harming us in a hidden way. And there is an apparent, visible form of harm that they can cause to you. And that can be, for example, diseases, jinn possession, and things of that sort.", "If a person enters their house and they do not mention the name of Allah, they don't say Bismillah, the Shaitan can enter with you. And then they can cause corruption. They can cause harm through them entering with you in the house. Now, what's the evidence for that? The evidence for that is the Hadith of the Prophet Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam when he said, \"If a person enters his house and he mentions the name of Allah, the Shaitan would say to the rest of the jinn, 'There is no place for you to stay and there is no food.' However, if the person does not mention Allah's name, then the Shaitan will say that you have a place to stay. And if he doesn't mention Allah's name when he eats, then the Shaitan will say you have food today.\"", "Now, how many jinn enter you? Allah knows best. 1,000 jinn can enter you, 500, 300, 200. You don't know how many of them can enter. And they can go all around the house. They can hide, they stay in the rooms, in the closets, and under the beds, here and there. It doesn't matter, they go in everywhere. And they stay in the house.", "Then they start to cause harm. Like what? For example, your wife is there and you say to her, \"Bring me a glass of water,\" or, \"Can I have a glass of water?\" Then the Shaitan or the jinn whispers to her – what does he say? \"Tell him go get it yourself.\" And then she says, \"Go get it yourself.\" And then an argument starts, a fight starts. They are causing all these types of harms in the house. And the solution is very simple: you mention Allah's name when you enter. It's a very simple thing. The same thing when it comes to food. You know the Hadith about saying Bismillah so the Shaitan doesn't eat with you.", "However, there is a specific narration where the Prophet was sitting and was about to eat, and the Sahaba were about to eat. And the Sahaba would wait for the Prophet before they eat, for him to say Bismillah, to mention the name of Allah, and then eat. And then this young girl comes, this Jariya comes running, and she's about to take from the food, so the Prophet holds her hand. Then you have this Arabic guy coming as well, running, and he was about to take from the food, so the Prophet holds his hand. And then the Prophet says to the Sahaba – because the Sahaba don't see; the world of the Jinn is unseen – the Prophet, he says that in his hand now he's holding the Jinn, because the Jinn was trying to eat the food using that girl and using that guy, because Allah's name was not yet mentioned. He's holding the hand of the girl and he's holding with it, because imagine the girl's hand is there and the hand of the Jinn is right next to it, trying to grab from the food and eat.", "So the Prophet is teaching us this: there is interactions, real interactions, going on a day-to-day basis. Entering your house, eating the food, entering the bathroom: the things that you're doing on a day-to-day basis, when you are not fortifying and protecting yourself, the Jinn have an influence on you in your life. So it's very crucial, very important for us to understand that these [adhkar] and the things that we mention and the things that were taught in the Quran and Sunnah are not just mentioned there for the sake of it. They're mentioned so we can fortify and protect ourselves from this unseen world, which we cannot observe with our own eyes.", "Someone could say then, okay, what if my young daughter or my young son enters the house without saying Allah's name? Because we know the kids, they're not like adults. So, you teach your kid: if you saw your kid coming in the house without mentioning Allah's name, take the kid, hold his hand and take him outside the house and say to him, say Bismillah or mention Allah's name, say Assalamualaikum, and then enter with him. So, you can teach him this as a habit. And if he goes out and come and says Allah's name, Bismillah, Assalamualaikum, and enters, then the jinn will come out. So, it's very important that we do that.", "Similarly, eating food: maybe there's a little girl or a guy coming to eat the food. Before they eat, you say Bismillah, eat a small piece of the food, because now you mention Allah's name on the food, and then they can eat. No problem, because Allah's name is now mentioned on the food. Even if they're young and they don't mention, you start and say Bismillah on your own, and then they can start eating after you.", "So, what we need: to internalize these ahadith, to internalize this understanding. A lot of people complain about being harmed by the jinn or having issues in their life, but we are not applying the things that protects us.", "And that's why the Prophet, he told Anas ibn Malik, he said to him, \"Ya bunayya, oh young boy or oh my son, if you enter upon your family, if you enter your house, fasallim, say Assalamualaikum.\" So, now we took from the hadith before, about the shaytan saying to the other jinn, \"Enter,\" we took from it that we say Bismillah or mention Allah's name. And Assalamualaikum, we take from this narration. So, now before you enter your house, say Bismillah, Assalamualaikum, and you enter your house.", "Now, I want to talk about something which is very important, which is the idea of mixing between jinn [possession] and psychological illnesses and diseases. It's a very problematic issue that a lot of people do. However, we got to understand, when you go to people that do ruqyah or try to help you, or try to help others, or if you are a person yourself doing ruqyah, we need to avoid assumptions, because they can cause huge harm and huge issues.", "For instance, someone goes to a person who does ruqyah and they are not a qualified person. And they go to them, and you read the Quran or something, or someone moves a little bit or whatever, so he starts giving them a bunch of assumptions: you have this, you have that. That can destroy someone's life.", "So, it's very important for the person who does it and the person that go to them: you make sure that you go to someone qualified, number one. And whoever is doing ruqyah, that he is sure not to use assumptions, but to be certain about the things that he says to the people. If you say to someone that you have [sihr], imagine. And then the person, he doesn't really have it. Now, everything that happens – he's walking and he trips – oh, it's because of the [sihr]. It's because of hassad, because of this. He loses his wallet – oh, it's because of hassad, because of [sihr]. So, you start causing this form of delusion in the mind of a person that can completely destroy their life.", "So, it's very important that we use the Quran and Sunnah and double-check and make sure that the person who is helping others is using the Quran and Sunnah and is certain of what he's doing, rather than misguiding people and confusing them.", "Also, another issue is where people, they think everything is [sihr]. Without even going to someone, they think everything is hassad, envy, evil eye, [sihr], jinn possession; they think everything is that, because they don't want to take accountability. Allah in the Quran tells us, \"Whatever calamity happens to you is because of what your hand have earned.\" And Allah also mentions that some people, if a good happens to them, they say it's from Allah; if bad happens to them, they say it's from Allah. \"Say it's from yourselves.\"", "There are some bad things that can happen to us in our life. We lose our job, we get divorced, all of these things. That has nothing to do with hasad. Has nothing to do with evil eye. Has nothing to do with seher. Has nothing to do with jinn possession. Not everything that happens in our life, we start saying this is seher, this is magic, this is jinn possession. That's why it's very important that we make distinctions and we understand the difference between this and between other things.", "I have had this personal experience in my family, a close relative. And they would bring all of these people for ruqyah, and they will do all sort of things, all sort of practices that are not based on the Quran and Sunnah. And they would say she has this, she has that, or he has this, he has that, and all of this stuff. And in the end this was a psychological disorder, let's say a bipolar disorder. Went to a person of knowledge, a person who understands psychological illnesses. Just as we believe that the jinn exists and evil eye is true and envy is true and seher is true and magic is true, and all of these things we believe in them, at the same time, we don't say that everything is that. So we have to have this middle ground of understanding the difference between the two.", "Even the doctors: you may come to a doctor who says to you, \"Okay, this is not my specialty. Go to a cardiologist. Go to an abdomen doctor. Go to this.\" He's a doctor, and then this is a doctor of the body. You could say, \"Okay, do radiation, because I just want to make sure. I want to double check.\" So that same idea needs to apply when it comes to this idea of seher. We need to be sure, double check, and not just say things.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “How To Protect Yourself From Jinn, Possession, Magic & The Evil Eye In Islam - Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dDdEEnJpWmI", ((353, "5:53–6:30"), (390, "6:30–7:02"), (422, "7:02–7:20"), (440, "7:20–7:51"), (471, "7:51–8:50"), (531, "8:51–9:25"), (565, "9:25–10:03"), (609, "10:09–10:30"), (630, "10:30–10:42"), (650, "10:50–11:19"), (683, "11:23–11:57"), (720, "12:00–12:16"), (737, "12:17–12:48"), (768, "12:48–13:06"), (795, "13:15–13:43"), (825, "13:45–14:09"), (850, "14:10–14:50"), (890, "14:50–15:12"),), id: 640)
// U ML079:73-93 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("But then again, you run to the problem that I already told you: that this is the case with other faiths as well. We believe in possession as Muslims. We believe that people can be possessed, and we believe in something called رُقْيَة (Ruqya), which is a form of exorcising – if you want to use that term – removing the demons, or removing the satan, or whatever is possessing that individual. We have that in Islamic tradition; Prophet himself did it in a Narration. It's not something we don't believe in. It's something we believe in. There's never ending amount of stories of people who ask Allah for something. Plenty of stories of people, how they became Muslim: they saw themselves doing pilgrimage in Mecca, and then they did pilgrimage in Mecca, or something of that extent.", "So the point I'm trying to make is that shouldn't keep you in Christianity, because that's not unique to Christianity. And if you believe in God being One, then calling yourself a Christian would be betraying what God taught you about Himself, because you know that God never told you He was three in one. And for you to say I'm still going to call myself a Christian – which entails that God is 3in1 – is essentially saying: doesn't matter if God is telling me something, I'm still going to follow something other than what He told me.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “This Christian Came To Convert Muslim But He Didn't Expect This! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MGZ5L15SzXk", ((269, "4:29–5:15"), (317, "5:17–5:42"),), id: 641)
// U ML026:229-355 | The Muslim Lantern | 14
#passage(("So there are types of healers, or types of people who do ruqyah. Let's say there's two types. One type is who just learned from other people. He look at someone who does ruqyah, he did the ruqyah. He watched something and he learned, and he started doing it. And then people started coming to them. And there is another person who studied. He's a alim. He's a person of knowledge. He studied the Quran and Sunnah: what do they say about the world of the jinn? What do they say about their interactions and influences on us? And how to protect and fortify yourself from the Quran and Sunnah? So, if you go to someone to do ruqyah on you, be sure that a person is from the second type, and not the first type, of someone who just looked and started practicing and copying other people.", "Some of them will tell you things like: the jinn starts to speak, and they say to us, go do that. Start spraying this in the house. Go to that place, you will find this. Go to this place, you will find that. And the person who is not a person of knowledge, who did not learn from the Quran and Sunnah, would listen to the jinn, and would tell you, oh, the jinn is telling us, then this must be true. However, a person of knowledge from the Quran and the Sunnah, you know what he would say? If someone is possessed by a jinn, and you start speaking to them, and the jinn starts to telling you, do this or don't do that, then the person of knowledge will say first: how are you advising me, when you are a sinner? You are a fasq. You're someone who's disobeying Allah and his messenger.", "Why? Because that jinn is possessing a human being, and it is haram for the jinn. We already said, all of the things in the Sharia, the jinn are also commanded to follow, like the Quran and the prophet. So, harming you by possessing you is haram for that jinn. So, if that jinn is doing something haram already, what makes you think he's going to start giving you good advice, and you should listen to what they say and start applying it? So, a person of knowledge will first say to them that first you have to repent. You have to leave this person that you're possessing. You have to repent to Allah before you start giving me advice. So, it's very important to make these distinctions.", "Now the question is, how can we be certain if something is jinn possession or if something is just a psychological illness? There are signs. What are these signs? The Quran is a healing. If it's being recited on someone, it has an influence on it. There are people who say, \"Oh, I have jinn possession, I have sihr, I have this.\" And Quran is recited day and night and there's no influences on them. They don't have anything.", "A person who's possessed by jinn, how can we be sure? Once you recite the Quran on them, they become unconscious. So, that is a sign. And then if they speak, if the jinn speaks, they speak with a different voice. It could be a different language even; that jinn could be from a different place. So, if someone says, \"I'm jinn possessed,\" they don't become unconscious, there is no different voice that is being said; they say to you, \"Look, oh, the jinn is speaking. I can't control my voice. I just hear what the jinn is saying.\" That's false. That person is not being possessed by jinn.", "What if there's a jinn now, and he starts speaking with a different voice, but he starts giving you advice? Let's say he tells you any type of advice: \"The person who led me to possess you is in this place, is in that place. Do this, do that.\" If you hear someone who's being possessed by jinn, and the jinn is speaking and is telling you to do something, first thing you do is to Compare it to the Quran and Sunnah. Why? Because the default in what they say is lying. Now, he's a disobedient jinn who's possessing someone.", "We know the hadith where the shaytan tells Abu Hurairah to recite Ayatul Kursi, because it's going to be a protection for you before you sleep until you wake up. So, Prophet said, \"Sadaqaka.\" He said the truth, wa huwa kadhub. Kadhub means it's from fa'ul, that he's an excessive compulsive liar. He lies all the time. So, let's say 90% of what he says, 95% of what he says, is a lie.", "So, if what they say is in accordance to the Quran and Sunnah, then we can believe that part. However, anything else they say, the default position is that they're lying. The same as the case with Abu Hurairah: what was taken is what the Prophet did takrir of, what he affirmed, which was the recitation of Ayat al-Kursi. So, we accepted that because we compared it to the Quran and Sunnah. However, anything else that's being said is not to be applied.", "And you'd have a lot of these people who do ruqyah. They come with all types of myths. Some people will tell you to spray salt in the house – and these exist in many cultures, these practices – spray salt in the house and the jinn will not enter. Or take this amulet, or hang this on your wall, or say these specific words.", "And like we said from the hadith before: where did you get this information from? This is the world of the unseen. If you believe that spraying salt or doing this or that or this amulet or hanging this thing is influencing the jinn – what's your source of knowledge? It's either the wahy, you get revelations from the Quran and Sunnah, which we know you don't have, or the jinn told you something. And we said the case with the jinn is that the majority of what they say is lying.", "So, we cannot use personal experiences to apply these things. Most of those, the people who do ruqyah who haven't studied the Quran and Sunnah, they'll say someone did it and it worked. That's not how we approach the world of the unseen. We approach the world of the unseen using the Quran and the Sunnah.", "You'll have some of these so-called, as well, people who do ruqyah. They'll say, \"I'll use a jinn to get another jinn.\" So, now imagine a person, you are doing ruqyah on them, and then the jinn starts to speak. And he says to you, \"I can help you. Okay, I repent, I can help you.\" You'll ask him, \"How can you help me?\" He says, \"Look, I'm going to start helping you. Whenever you see someone possessed next time, just say something and I will go into that human being, and then I will start helping you and I'll fight them out.\"", "Those people who are not experienced from the Quran and the Sunnah, they will be happy. They will like this. However, a person who studied the Quran and the Sunnah understands that this is haram, because the jinn entering a human being, it's a masia. It's an act of disobedience. So, you would not give permission to the jinn to do something like this.", "So, when you are well acquainted with the teachings in the Quran and the Sunnah, you don't fall into these issues, and you don't cause harm to others by doing the wrong practices. Because remember, the healer is Allah, not the jinn. So, you say to that jinn: we have the Quran, we have the book of Allah. We don't need you. Don't need you entering anything anywhere. Reciting the book of Allah Azza wa Jal is enough to heal the person that needs healing. It's very very important.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “How To Protect Yourself From Jinn, Possession, Magic & The Evil Eye In Islam - Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dDdEEnJpWmI", ((912, "15:12–15:48"), (951, "15:51–16:31"), (991, "16:31–17:14"), (1035, "17:15–17:38"), (1060, "17:40–18:15"), (1095, "18:15–18:51"), (1132, "18:52–19:15"), (1156, "19:16–19:38"), (1180, "19:40–19:54"), (1198, "19:58–20:21"), (1221, "20:21–20:36"), (1239, "20:39–21:13"), (1274, "21:14–21:35"), (1297, "21:37–22:01"),), id: 642)
// U ML026:400-467 | The Muslim Lantern | 9
#passage(("We know in the Quran and Sunnah we have things that are specified to recite, like we said before, sleeping, [Ayat] al-Kursi; things that we can do for ruqyah, like, for example, Surat al-Fatiha, or al-Mu'awwidhat, Qul A'udhu bi Rabbil Falaq, Qul A'udhu bi Rabbin Nas, and these verses and chapters. However, do we only need to recite these specified verses, or anything from the Quran? The answer is it's permissible to recite anything from the Quran.", "Allah Azza wa Jalla says, \"Wa nunazzilu minal Qur'ani ma huwa shifa'un wa rahmatun lil mu'minin.\" We send down from the Quran what is healing. So, the Quran, all of it is a book of healing. And Aisha, Allah be pleased with her, there was this narration: Abu Bakr entered upon her, and she was doing ruqyah, so he said to her, \"Erqiha bi kitabillah.\" Do ruqyah on her with the book of Allah. So, it is permissible.", "However, what is not permissible is where you get certain people who say: say these specific number of verses, or these specific verses in this specific order, in this specific time, in this specific way. It's permissible for you to do, but it's not permissible for you to make it like it's some form of legislation and start advising people to do this specifically. You cannot say, \"I recited this specific set of verses in this specific set of way, therefore it works, therefore you need to recite it as well.\"", "Now, we get to this question: what does a person do if they start feeling like they have sehir, like they have hasad, or they have evil eye, or they have any of these things? The first thing you need to do is to do ruqyah upon yourself. Why? Because the messenger, that is what he told companion who came to the prophet and he said, I find this feeling of pain in my body since I accepted Islam. Then the prophet recommended him to do ruqyah on himself, and he said to him, say Bismillah three times. So he said what the prophet commanded him. He said, I said it, so Allah removed that from me.", "Some of us get this pain, get this harm, but we don't do this. Try it and you will see the effect, the influence, because that was pain in his body. So you feel some sort of a pain in your body. And I have tried this myself. I had this pain in my back that I felt, that was out of nowhere. And I said this [dhikr] and it was gone. It didn't even take days or whatever. It was gone instantly. [We were] given this revelation so we can apply it to ourselves.", "Now, let's say you do it on yourself a few times and it doesn't work. Is it permissible for you to go to someone else to do it on you? It is permissible for you to go to someone else to do it on you. However, it's not going to be the same. Why are we saying do the ruqyah on yourself first? Because you're the one suffering. So you will be more humble, more in need of Allah, when you are calling upon Allah, when you're doing the ruqyah. It wouldn't be the same for someone like a stranger who's not you. He wouldn't be feeling the same way.", "And the closer you are to Allah, the more humble you are, the more dependent you are on Allah, the more likely that Allah will answer your prayer. That's why prophet told us that you are the closest to Allah in the state of prostration. You're more humble, you're more humiliating yourself, you're more coming closer to Allah, so you are closer in your sujood, because you are in that state.", "So, it is permissible: if you try on yourself multiple times, it doesn't work, then you go to someone. It is not haram. But, it's not recommended, because there's a hadith of the Prophet Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam where he said that there's a group of people that will enter paradise without hisab, without accountability before or any punishment. And then he mentioned one of the characteristics of these people: la [yastarqun]. They don't ask someone else to do ruqyah on them. You can do ruqyah on people, but asking someone to do ruqyah on you will exclude you from being from those group of people.", "However, remember what we said: go to someone who's qualified. There is many people online – I don't want to mention names – but people doing all crazy sorts of things. They put their hand in someone's mouth and crazy things, not from the Quran and Sunnah. And the majority of them are liars. And people follow them. So, it's very important to be clear on what is from the Quran and Sunnah and what is not from the Quran and Sunnah.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “How To Protect Yourself From Jinn, Possession, Magic & The Evil Eye In Islam - Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dDdEEnJpWmI", ((1515, "25:15–25:39"), (1541, "25:41–25:57"), (1559, "25:59–26:26"), (1594, "26:34–27:22"), (1642, "27:22–27:54"), (1678, "27:58–28:27"), (1707, "28:27–28:49"), (1730, "28:50–29:17"), (1758, "29:18–29:59"),), id: 643)
// U ML026:608-676 | The Muslim Lantern | 8
#passage(("Some others will say to close your eyes. And look what some of these evil people will do. You will go to a person who does ruqyah, and be like, close your eyes. Then you close your eyes, and then you will start seeing that your uncle – oh, your uncle is the one who did sihr to you. He put it somewhere in that room, and you go and you find something in your closet or something. And then families get separated. I have many stories where I have people saying, \"Oh, my aunt did sihr on me.\" The shaytan throws this vision when they close their eyes, and they see something, and he visualizes something to them so he can cause separation.", "Allah in the Quran tells us that the shaytan only wants to put enmity and hatred between you and each other. And Allah tells us that which separates between the husband and wife. This is what the shaytan wants: to separate between you and your wife, cause enmity between you and other people. We have families that don't speak to each other for years and years: oh, this person did sihr to me; this person was the cause of hasad or eye. No proof. They either go to some scam artist that tells them this stuff, or they just cause assumptions.", "This is a very, very evil door that people must be aware from. And you need to be certain, using the evidence from the Quran and Sunnah, descriptions in the Quran and Sunnah. It's the only way you could be certain that someone did it to you.", "So now we ask a question: is the cure for sihr and hasad and [possession], is it different cures or the same cure? Now, for evil eye, we talked about the wudu and washing with wudu. This is mentioned in the [narration]. However, for hasad, for envy, or magic, or [possession], Ruqyah influences all of these things. And of course, the best ruqyah is found in the Quran and Sunnah. This is how you heal yourself.", "However, when we say that ruqyah influences all of them, the ruqyah have to be done correctly. A lot of people do ruqyah, but they say, \"Oh, I did ruqyah.\" If I had the penny for each time someone said, I did ruqyah and nothing happened, I'd probably be rich. But are you doing the ruqyah correctly or not? So, the question is this: how do we do ruqyah the right way?", "The first thing you need to understand is: do you internalize that you're using the Quran as a healing? That you're using the Quran: this is what you're going to use, Quran and the Sunnah, the revelation from Allah, to heal yourself. The second thing is that you understand that the Quran by itself doesn't heal. Allah is the one who heals. The Quran is a means, is a [sabab] for us to heal. The third thing: you internalize that you are following the Prophet Muhammad in these practices.", "Then, you need to know the meaning of the words that you say, the [dhikr] that you say, or the dua, or the Quran. You need to know the meaning of these things. Because remember: ask Allah and you're certain that Allah will answer you, because Allah does not accept from a heart that is distracted. So, you need to be internalizing, understanding the meaning of the words, and your heart is present when you're saying that. And lastly, you need to humble yourself to Allah. Need to feel that you are in need to Allah when you're making this ruqyah. You're asking Allah sincerely to heal the person, or to heal yourself, from whatever is happening to them.", "So, a lot of us say things like the [adhkar] of the [Sabah] and [Masah] to protect ourselves. However, we don't understand their meaning. If you want to protect yourself, you need to understand their meaning. So, I recommend everybody get a book of the explanation of these, of Sabah and Masah. Understand their meaning. Think about what you're reading when you're reading it. And if you're used to saying, change the orders, because if you change the order it doesn't become a habit. So many things, when we say a lot, becomes a habit, and then your mind is not present when you're saying them. But if you change the order, you force your mind to think.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “How To Protect Yourself From Jinn, Possession, Magic & The Evil Eye In Islam - Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dDdEEnJpWmI", ((2289, "38:09–38:44"), (2326, "38:46–39:17"), (2359, "39:19–39:30"), (2380, "39:40–40:20"), (2422, "40:22–40:44"), (2447, "40:47–41:12"), (2473, "41:13–41:54"), (2514, "41:54–42:30"),), id: 644)

=== 10.6 The evil eye
// NODE P02.C04.S06
#author("The Muslim Lantern")
// U ML026:468-607 | The Muslim Lantern | 14
#passage(("Now, what is the difference between ain, evil eye, and hasad, envy? Are they the same thing? Because a lot of people confuse these two things. It's very important for us to understand that they're not the same thing. So, hasad can only come from an evil soul or evil person that wishes that the ni'mah, that the blessing that Allah has upon you, is gone. This is what hasad is: someone looks at you with the evil that he wishes that whatever good that you have is gone.", "Evil eye, ain, is that you like something, but you don't mention Allah's name on it, so harm falls on that thing, because you don't mention Allah's name on it when you are finding beauty in it or adornment in it or likeness. You forget to mention Allah's name or you don't mention Allah's name. The evil eye can happen from a righteous person. It can happen from a father to his son. Can happen from a husband to his wife. And it is not happening with an evil intent like hasad.", "And the evidence is that you have the Hadith of Amir ibn Rabi'ah, where he saw one of the other Sahabah, Sahl ibn Hunayf. He was doing [ightisal], and he saw his skin, and he [said], I've never seen beautiful skin. So he fell. And then the Prophet said, \"Who are you accusing? Who do you think is the cause of this?\" So they mentioned Amir ibn Rabi'ah. So the Prophet said, \"Why would one of you kill his own brother?\" And here [we] understand the solution: if someone has an evil eye specifically, what to do. Prophet told him to do wudu, and then to use that water that he used for wudu to pour it on the person who has been affected by ayn. And the Prophet poured it on him, so he recovered. He stood up like nothing happened to him.", "Amir ibn Rabi'ah is from the people of Badr, of the Sahabah from Badr. He's a righteous person. So he affected another person with ayn or evil eye, whatever translation you want to use for it. And he didn't do it with a bad intention. So it can happen from a righteous person, it can happen from you to your own son.", "So that's very important now that we understand: if someone comes to you and asks for wudu, that is afraid that you have affected them with evil eye – so they want to ask you for wudu so they can do ghusl with it, or wash their body with it, so they can make sure that they're no longer affected – is that you don't say, \"How can you come and ask me? I'm not an evil person to do envy.\" It's not hasad. We're talking about ayn. You could do it when you're not feeling it. You could do it and be from the Sahabah from Badr. It doesn't matter. So do not feel offended if something like this happened.", "Now, something very very important. And this happens to a lot of people, but they don't understand. Your own baby starts to cry at night. None of the people go and do ruqyah. Recite on him, do some ruqyah. It is free. Takes you a few minutes. Try and do ruqyah on your son. They go to this doctor and that doctor, and sometimes it doesn't help. Perhaps he's been affected by you or by someone else. So, first do ruqyah. If it doesn't work, you and your wife do wudu and try pour it on that child and see. And go and see the doctors if this is not influencing. However, use this in your life, because that could be the cause, when you are going and trying to find another way of healing.", "And that's why we can fall into abandonment of the Quran. Allah says in the Quran, and the messenger said, \"Oh Allah, my people have abandoned this Quran.\" So, the talk about different types of abandonment: the abandonment of actions, that we don't do the actions of the Quran, and an abandonment of healing. Some people go throughout their entire life and they never do ruqyah on themselves even once. Do it. If you having illness, sickness, disease, feeling headache, feeling something, do this. Make this a part of your life. Allah's revealed to us this because these are acts of worship that we need to implement on ourselves, and there is a healing and a barakah and a shifa and a blessing in them. So, we need to apply them in our lives.", "So, how do we protect ourselves and avoid evil eye, and giving someone evil eye? It's for us to say barakah. So, let's say, for example, may Allah give barakah. You say words of barakah. Now, some people think that we should say masha Allah, and a lot of people say this. If they see something, they say masha'Allah, and they think masha'Allah is how you avoid doing evil eye towards that thing. So, asking for baraka versus saying masha'Allah: Masha'Allah is not related to that. That's not the teaching of the prophet. The teaching of the prophet in relation to that: if you see something you like, you ask for baraka. You ask for blessing. Say Allahumma barik alayhi. Allahumma barik fihi.", "Now, where does the idea of masha'Allah come from? It comes from the Quran: the verse that talks about the garden, and one that says to the other: masha'Allah, there is no power except with Allah. This was the believer speaking to a disbeliever. The person who was entering that garden was a disbeliever. And that's why you see in the Quran, in the verses, that he says, \"I don't think that the hour will come. I don't think that the day of judgment will come.\"", "So, that other believer was telling him, \"If only – if you enter this paradise – you believed in a creator and you said that this was from Allah. It was with the power of Allah. It's not from my power. It is what Allah willed.\" So, he's referring to a specific belief: that this was with the power of Allah. What Allah willed, is not with my power. This is not in relation that if you see something you like, you say masha'Allah. So, the correct practice is what? If we see something and we want to avoid evil eye or any of that, that we ask for baraka. We say Allahumma barik. For instance, any words of baraka, any words of asking for baraka, you can use and say to avoid evil eye.", "Now, some people will tell you things like what? Looking at mirrors leads you to [jinn possession] or something. Is there evidence from the Quran and Sunnah? No. We know that from the Quran and Sunnah we have narrations that the prophet would look. There is nothing in the Quran and Sunnah that prevents you, or tells you not to look in the mirror, or not to look in the mirror for this period of time, or not to do that. So, there is no evidence for that. Remember, I told you anything of the unseen must be evidence from the Quran and Sunnah. So, if you would, mention Allah's name, say bismillah, and look. However, there isn't anything in the Quran and the Sunnah that says if you look for an extensive period of time. So, be aware of these practices.", "Some people, they close the door of the bathroom. I know some people like that. Close the door of the bathroom because they're worried about jinn coming out or something. Remember the hadith we just told you: you could enter your house without saying Allah's name, and the jinn can come in. It's nothing to do with the bathroom. Plus, you think the physical door is going to prevent the jinn from coming out? The jinn can be like the wind, and they can go through objects. They're created from smoke and fire. They can go through under the door. They can go anywhere. You closing the door of the bathroom or opening it is not going to change that. You got to be aware of these practices.", "You get someone who's not practicing using the Quran and Sunnah: \"Oh, I can sense this person has jinn. This person has sihr.\" Where did you get this evidence from? It's either a jinn that throws these ideas in your mind – and we said they're liars – or you're claiming to get some revelation. So, if you see people telling you to do all of these myths that I'm telling you, all of these are signs to you that these people are not qualified. They haven't studied the Quran and the Sunnah.", "I'm giving you all of these examples so you can understand and be able to differentiate: if [someone's] family member was possessed or had these issues, and they wanted someone to do ruqyah on them, that if you hear these things, and you hear these recommends – oh, put salt here, close the bathroom door, hang this amulet, say this 20 times, do this, do that – if you have these people saying these things, then you know that that person is not qualified. So, do not listen to them, and find the person who is qualified, who uses the Quran and the Sunnah.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “How To Protect Yourself From Jinn, Possession, Magic & The Evil Eye In Islam - Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dDdEEnJpWmI", ((1800, "30:00–30:25"), (1828, "30:28–30:59"), (1861, "31:01–31:41"), (1901, "31:41–31:56"), (1919, "31:59–32:32"), (1953, "32:33–33:20"), (2000, "33:20–34:04"), (2046, "34:06–34:58"), (2101, "35:01–35:24"), (2124, "35:24–36:03"), (2163, "36:03–36:39"), (2199, "36:39–37:15"), (2237, "37:17–37:38"), (2258, "37:38–38:08"),), id: 645)

=== 10.7 Protection from jinn and the evil eye
// NODE P02.C04.S07
#author("The Muslim Lantern")
// U ML026:677-925 | The Muslim Lantern | 24
#passage(("How do I protect myself from jinn, possession, evil eye and all of these things? The first thing you do is praying Fajr. A lot of people are going to find difficulty in this. But do you want protection? Prophet said whoever prays Fajr, he is in the safekeeping and the protection of Allah.", "Second thing is one of the most powerful you could say 100 times a day: a protection for him from the jinn until the end of his day. If you say it earlier, the best; but even if you don't, you say it later on so you can protect yourself. It's very important. Don't be lazy.", "The day and night that I was telling you: get a book, understanding their meaning and saying them. You say them after Fajr, after Maghrib. They are day and night reminders and they have words of protection that protects the person until the morning comes. It protects the person until the night comes. If you're suffering, if you're having issues, even if you're not, you see the people around you who suffer from jinn or any of these things. You want to be protected, this is how you do it.", "Also, for the men to pray in Jama'ah, praying congregation. Because the Prophet Alayhi Salaam, talking about the Shaitan, he said Alaykum [bil] Jama'ah, upon you is the Jama'ah, fainnama ya'kul al dhib min al ghanam al qasiyah. Because the wolf eats from the lone sheep, the sheep that has gone away from the rest of the pack. So that Shaitan targets you when you're alone. But your prayer in Jama'ah is a protection for you.", "And lastly, rely on Allah Azza Wajjal in all your affairs. Have tawakkul, reliance on Allah Azza Wajjal, that he's the protector. I understand in my heart Allah Azza Wajjal is the one who protects me. If you do these things and you keep these things, by the will of Allah Azza Wajjal you will be protected from anything evil that can happen.", "How can we protect our children from evil eye or jinn possession or magic or sihr or any of these things? We have a dua that Prophet Alayhi Salaam used as a protection for Hasan and Husayn, his grandchildren. Prophet Sallallahu Alayhi Wasallam would say u'idhukuma bi kalimatillah al tammah min kulli shaytanin wa hammah wa min kulli aynin lammah. What is the meaning of this? If you want to be protected you got to understand the meaning of the dua you make, the dhikr that you make. Prophet Alayhi Salaam says u'idhukuma, so I seek refuge in Allah or in the words of Allah, kalimatillah al tammah, with the perfect words of Allah.", "What is this kalimatillah al tammah? Some scholars they said it's the Quran. Or it's the qadar, the words that Allah uses to determine things. Or it's the perfect words of Allah, complete perfect words of Allah that Allah Azza Wajjal says in the Quran: Qul law kana al bahru midada li kalimati Rabbi la nafida al bahru qabla an tanfada kalimatu Rabbi walaw ji'na bi mithlihi madada. If the sea was like ink so we can use to write the words of Allah, these perfected words of Allah, it wouldn't suffice even if the whole world was the sea. Even if you bring other seas, it wouldn't suffice the words of Allah Azza Wajjal. So these perfected words, it is the attribute of Allah. We seek refuge in the words of Allah, perfected words of Allah, from every shaitan, min kulli shaitanin, wa hammah. Hammah is something that bites and has a poisonous bite. Let's say a scorpion, a snake. Wa min kulli ainil lammah, from every envious eye.", "So, this hadith you say to protect your children. If it's a boy, au'idhuka bi kalimatillahi tammah and the rest of the hadith. If it's a girl, au'idhuki. And for two, au'idhukuma. And if it's a group of children, au'idhukum bi kalimatillahi tammah.", "You can also recite the Mu'awwidhat, Qul hu Allahu Ahad, Qul a'udhu bi rabbil falaq, Qul a'udhu bi rabbin nas, on your kids. At the time of sleep, have them do wudu. Recite Ayat al-Kursi. So, after you do that, you blow and wipe over them three times, or over yourself if you're the one doing it, three times as a form of protection. Cuz maybe they had an evil eye in the morning. Maybe they had [sihr]. If you do this before they sleep, you are protecting your children from evil things.", "When we recite min sharri al-waswasi al-khannas, from the evil of al-waswas, the one who whispers, al-khannas, what does that even mean? This is about understanding what we're reciting. Abdullah ibn Abbas, he says, \"A shaitan, jinn or the shaitan, is staying on the heart of the son of Adam. If you mention Allah, then he does khunus.\" Khannas means that he runs away, he moves away, or he leaves. He retreats. That's why he's called al-khannas. And if you forget the remembrance of Allah, he whispers. So, we can be always in a state of protection from the Shaitan's whispers if we're always mentioning Allah.", "Now, what about protecting your house? First, when you enter the house, you say \"Bismillah Assalamualaikum.\" You mention Allah's name and you say \"Assalamualaikum.\" Then, you're sure that the jinn are not entering with you.", "Remove music from your house. I know some people find this difficult. When Allah says \"Bisautika\", with your voice, referring to the Shaitan, look at the narrations that talk about music and singing. This is the tafsir of the Sahaba. It brings them closer. It's the voice of the Shaitan.", "Keep constant dhikr and adhkar in the house and Quran playing, for example, or some good dhikr or remembrance of Allah playing in the house or recited in the house. Keep it always on so you can protect your house. Recite Surah Al-Baqarah in your house, because the Prophet told us the Shaitan yanfiru, he runs away or is repelled from the house that Surah Al-Baqarah is recited in.", "Also, don't hang pictures around the house. This doesn't include the things you need for necessity or things you're keeping in drawings like your ID. We know the Hadith, the angels don't enter a house that has pictures, images. And if the angels don't enter, then the Shaitan will enter.", "Don't leave crosses in your house. Now, someone come and say, \"But what kind of a Muslim has a cross in his house?\" We'll say that this is not referring to an actual cross, but two objects come together and crucify, like two pens, become a crucifix. So, be careful in your house not to leave these things. Cuz as Aisha reported, the Prophet said, \"La [yatruku] shayan fihi tasalib illa [naqadahu].\" The Prophet wouldn't leave anything that had any crosses in it except that he would remove it. Also, the clothing in the house, or the kids' clothing, or the bed coverings, or any of these things, make sure they don't have crosses or pictures. Same idea.", "Then, also understand that the house that you do qiyam al-layl in, our night prayer, it's protected. Cuz you have the dhikr of Allah happening in it. And the more recitation of dhikr of Allah is there, then your house will be protected.", "The last thing is the dogs. Shouldn't have dogs in the house. We know the hadith of the Prophet alayhi wasallam. He had an appointment with Jibreel, and Jibreel didn't come. And the Prophet alayhi wasallam did not know; when he came out, then he saw Jibreel, and then he asked him why he didn't enter. So, Jibreel alayhi wasallam told him because there was a dog in the house. Now, you can keep a dog in Islam outside the house for protection. You can use a dog for farming, you can use a dog for hunting. It's not an issue. They're creation of Allah. However, keeping them in the house prevents angels from entering, and you want the angels in your house so you do not have shayatin and jinn in your house.", "We need to put these things into practices. Not just listen and hear, \"Okay, I understand. Now I know what I can do so I can protect myself.\" No, you need to actually implement these things.", "Also, if you enter into another location, and you want to protect yourself, the prophet Sallallahu alayhi wasallam says, Man nazala manzilan, whoever enters a place. It could be a scary place, an abandoned house, whatever, and you're afraid. Anywhere you enter, in a hotel, in a place you enter. Faqala, say, \"A'udhu bi kalimatillahi tammat min sharri ma khalaq.\" I seek refuge in kalimatillahi, in the words of Allah. Tammat. From the evil, from anything that Allah created. The prophet said, \"Lam yadurruhu shay'un hatta yartahila min manzilihi.\" Nothing will harm him until he leaves that place.", "Now, the last thing is some people suffer from nightmares. How do we deal with nightmares? First, to protect yourself before you sleep, you say Ayat al-Kursi. Internalize the meaning; these things need to be present when you're doing the dhikr. As the hadith of the prophet Sallallahu alayhi wasallam says, the shaytan will not come to you until you wake up.", "But the dreams themselves, it's very important. Prophet Sallallahu alayhi wasallam told us that the ru'ya, the good visions, from Allah, and bad dream or nightmare is from the shaytan. Then the prophet told us, \"Idha ra'a ahadukum ma yakrah.\" If one of you sees something he dislikes, a bad nightmare, an evil dream, or whatever, you do nafth, which is a form of blowing, or let's say spitting without saliva, three times on your left side, as you turn your face. And then you seek refuge in Allah from the shaitan. You say \"A'udhu billahi min ash-shaitan ir-rajim,\" and from what you saw, three times. Then you switch to the other side. If you do this, it will not harm you. But there is a very important point here. Wala yukhbir ahadan. Not to say to anyone what you saw.", "Now, many people see bad dreams. You wake up, right next to you your husband, and you start telling him what happened. We have the narration of the Prophet Muhammad, who said he saw his head rolling and he was running behind his head. So, Prophet Muhammad told him, do not let one of you speak about the shaitan manipulation of him. If it's a bad dream, do not tell anyone. Why? What is the wisdom? Because the shaitan is manipulating you. He's playing games with you. So, if you go and tell the people he's happy. However, if you don't say, then that is frustrating. Imagine someone is mocking you. You don't speak about it. You ignore it. It's frustrating. That is one of the cures from these things.", "Many of us don't even know that this is a practice that you do if you see something bad. And many of us, even the ones who know, they don't do it.", "And I ask Allah Azza Wajjal to protect all of us, because any of us could be harmed from this world of the jinn that lives with us. Nobody is invincible. Allah is a protector. That's why we're following these measurements that are found in the Quran and Sunnah that protects us. The people who are not believers, they don't have this guidance from Allah. And many of them are suffering. Many of them experience evil things. If only they knew the guidance, they would have been Muslims. And we have the guidance, but we're not implementing it.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “How To Protect Yourself From Jinn, Possession, Magic & The Evil Eye In Islam - Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dDdEEnJpWmI", ((2556, "42:36–43:00"), (2585, "43:05–43:30"), (2613, "43:33–44:02"), (2644, "44:04–44:26"), (2666, "44:26–44:42"), (2688, "44:48–45:22"), (2722, "45:22–46:27"), (2787, "46:27–46:51"), (2820, "47:00–47:27"), (2848, "47:28–48:03"), (2900, "48:20–48:44"), (2925, "48:45–49:09"), (2951, "49:11–49:33"), (2973, "49:33–49:54"), (2996, "49:56–50:42"), (3044, "50:44–50:57"), (3057, "50:57–51:30"), (3098, "51:38–51:47"), (3108, "51:48–52:19"), (3152, "52:32–53:04"), (3191, "53:11–54:14"), (3255, "54:15–55:05"), (3309, "55:09–55:16"), (3343, "55:43–56:15"),), id: 646)

