#passage(("This person here is a popular YouTuber, his name is JiDion. He's got seven or eight million subscribers. He made this video about turning his life to Christ. So, he completely removed all of his YouTube videos from social media.", "سُبْحَانَ ٱللَّٰهِ (SubhanAllah: Glorified is God)! I think some of the Muslims have not asked themselves this question, have not thought for a minute: \"If I were to die right now, where am I going to end?\" SubhanAllah, what made him turn his life, he's saying, is this event of just some Uber driver driving him and asking him this question. Some people might think it's a simple question, but it's not a simple question.", "The Prophetﷺ said أَكْثِرُوا ذِكْرَ هَاذِمِ اللَّذَّاتِ, \"Mention often the Destroyer of Pleasures.\" And the Prophetﷺ did not call it Death; he called it \"the Destroyer of Pleasures\". Why? Because these pleasures in this worldly life make you forget, make you think that you're going to live forever; they make you unaware of the reality, and they distract you of the fact that you're going to die. So the Prophetﷺ called it the Destroyer of pleasures for that reason, because those worldly pleasures around you are the only reason why you think you're OK while you're living your life.", "You're not thinking about this fact that when you die, there's eternal life, and that eternal life is the determination of what actually is a successful person and what is not a successful person. The successful person is the person who is going to end up in Paradise, in eternal life of bliss, not in eternal life of punishment.", "And Allahﷻ says in the Quran (Aljumua62:8) – it's a very profound verse – قُلْ إِنَّ ٱلْمَوْتَ ٱلَّذِى تَفِرُّونَ مِنْهُ (Say that that death that you're running away from), because many people are running away from Death.", "They're trying to escape, like Allah mentioned about certain people (Albaqara2:96): يَوَدُّ أَحَدُهُمْ لَوْ يُعَمَّرُ أَلْفَ سَنَةٍۢ (That he wishes that he lives for 1,000 years), and then Allah says: وَمَا هُوَ بِمُزَحْزِحِهِۦ مِنَ ٱلْعَذَابِ أَن يُعَمَّرَ (It is not going to make him move away or run away or escape the punishment, that he lives a thousand year).", "So, then, Allah says (Aljumua62:8): إِنَّ ٱلْمَوْتَ ٱلَّذِى تَفِرُّونَ مِنْهُ (That death that you're running away from) فَإِنَّهُۥ مُلَـٰقِيكُمْ ۖ (It is going to meet you).", "Then, Allah says ثُمَّ تُرَدُّونَ إِلَىٰ عَـٰلِمِ ٱلْغَيْبِ وَٱلشَّهَـٰدَةِ (Then, you'll be returned to the Knower of the seen and the unseen) فَيُنَبِّئُكُم بِمَا كُنتُمْ تَعْمَلُونَ (Then, Allah will tell you what you used to do). He will inform you of your actions, those things that you're doing that you think no one sees.", "A person like this person here, who is not a Muslim, by the way – he's a Christian – has changed his life, and we know that Christians don't have the Truth – that's a claim we make – and you, a Muslim, you have the Truth and you didn't change your life. This person, he's making hundreds of thousands, millions probably, of dollars, and he's got the fame, he's got everything, and he turned his life. And you, as a Muslim, you have less pleasures around you and you have less desires. Him, death has made him turn his life; and you, death has not made you turn your life.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Popular Youtuber Abandons Money And Fame For Christianity?! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=F3uZK_khCsk", ((0, "0:00–0:11"), (77, "1:17–1:38"), (102, "1:42–2:07"), (132, "2:12–2:27"), (152, "2:32–2:41"), (163, "2:43–2:54"), (182, "3:02–3:06"), (189, "3:09–3:18"), (218, "3:38–4:08"),), id: 648)
