#passage(("SubhanAllah, he's saying very profound things, and they are in the Quran and they are in the Hadith. The Quran (alQalam68:17-33) mentions the story about the three people with their garden, and how they didn't want to give charity, how they kept it to themselves, and then it was all ruined.", "And also, the Prophetﷺ was saying, \"If the child of Adam dies,\" انْقَطَعَ عَمَلُهُ إِلاَّ مِنْ ثَلاَثَةٍ (That his deeds are gone except for 3 things). Everything you're making in this life is not going to benefit you after you die, only a good child who makes supplication for God to forgive you, or good knowledge that you left behind you, or a charity that you left that people are benefiting from. But other than that, all of this money and stocks and wealth that you're stacking on top of your bank account, when you die, they're not going to come with you.", "It's like the ancient Egyptians: when they used to die, they used to put their gold and silver, believing that they'll be resurrected in the same place and then they will enjoy their stuff, and they used to leave food. But no! Today, who's taking their gold and silver? People, today, going into these places and taking their gold and silver. They've not benefited from them. There is nothing that you own once we're in the dirt, once we're gone.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Popular Youtuber Abandons Money And Fame For Christianity?! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=F3uZK_khCsk", ((1076, "17:56–18:06"), (1090, "18:10–18:35"), (1115, "18:35–18:58"),), id: 649)
