#refbox("Reference text: Quran 68:17-33, quran.com (Saheeh International)", (("68:17", "Indeed, We have tried them as We tried the companions of the garden, when they swore to cut its fruit in the [early] morning"), ("68:18", "Without making exception."), ("68:19", "So there came upon it [i.e., the garden] an affliction from your Lord while they were asleep."), ("68:20", "And it became as though reaped."), ("68:21", "And they called one another at morning,"), ("68:22", "[Saying], \"Go early to your crop if you would cut the fruit.\""), ("68:23", "So they set out, while lowering their voices,"), ("68:24", "[Saying], \"There will surely not enter it today upon you [any] poor person.\""), ("68:25", "And they went early in determination, [assuming themselves] able."), ("68:26", "But when they saw it, they said, \"Indeed, we are lost;"), ("68:27", "Rather, we have been deprived.\""), ("68:28", "The most moderate of them said, \"Did I not say to you, 'Why do you not exalt [Allāh]?'\""), ("68:29", "They said, \"Exalted is our Lord! Indeed, we were wrongdoers.\""), ("68:30", "Then they approached one another, blaming each other."), ("68:31", "They said, \"O woe to us; indeed we were transgressors."), ("68:32", "Perhaps our Lord will substitute for us [one] better than it. Indeed, we are toward our Lord desirous.\""), ("68:33", "Such is the punishment [of this world]. And the punishment of the Hereafter is greater, if they only knew."),))
// U ML041:418-447 | The Muslim Lantern | 3
#passage(("Of course, we are not happy that calamities are taking place; trying to do our best. But in the end, we understand, we have this assurance, that this is a part of the test of this life. Nobody is here to remain forever. We're all going to die. So, what matters is if I succeed in the test or not. My test is my life. Have I lived the life in accordance to what the creator wants?", "Some people are like, \"I lived a magnificent great life according to his own desires. I gave charity two times in my life or whatever. I'm a nice guy. I'm a very good person.\" Who determines if you are truly a good person? The one who puts that criteria is the creator, because the one who's going to reward or punish is the creator. It's not me. If you are alone, then you will realize the reality. Because we believe the minute you die, it's either a reward or a punishment.", "When your soul is being taken out of you, the angel of death will come to you. And now the soul will be either taken from your body like a water drop, very easily, very smoothly; or you will run in your body. You try to hide from the angel of death, and you will be grabbed difficultly from you, and you will be hit.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Curious Couple Ask A Muslim To Explain World Suffering! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9AACeXB0A9Q", ((1149, "19:09–19:40"), (1180, "19:40–20:04"), (1206, "20:06–20:31"),), id: 650)
