#passage(("So, the person who hasn't received the Message at all in this life has a different test on the Day of Judgment. They're not going to be punished before they undergo the test. Allah says in the Quran explicitly, in Chapter:17, Verse:15 (alisra17:15): وَمَا كُنَّا مُعَذِّبِینَ حَتَّىٰ نَبۡعَثَ رَسُولࣰا (We weren't going to punish a people until we send them a Messenger). If someone doesn't receive the Message, then that person is not punished.", "When these two angels come, they will question the person. They will say: \"Who is your Lord?\" \"What is your religion?\" \"And what do you say of the man who was sent to you?\" A believer will say: \"My Lord is Allah, and my religion is Islam, and the person who was sent to me would be Prophet Muhammad.\" If he was at the time of Jesus, he would say Jesus. If he was at the time of Moses, he would say Moses, depending on who's the Messenger sent to them. And then, that person will be told not to fear or be frightened.", "Now, the disbeliever, on the other hand, he would say: \"I don't know! I don't know! I don't know!\" The \"I don't know\" is the religion of disbelievers: \"I just don't know!\" They lived in \"I don't know\", and in the grave, it will also be \"I don't know\". And then those angels will have, let's say, a metal hammer, iron hammer – just for a lack of a better way to describe it – and he will be hit, and everything will hear the sound of that strike, except us humans; we don't hear it. But everything in the Creation hears it, from how loud is going to be. And then all of that punishment I'm talking about will take place to that disbeliever. And there's a continuous punishment in the grave for the disbeliever.", "And then, when the Day of Judgment commences, the Day of Resurrection, Allah will resurrect everyone. There's a bridge that will be placed, called الصراط (the Seratt). That's only for the Believers. The Disbelievers are instantly dragged in chains in Hellfire. They will not undergo accountability, because they were disbelievers. They're never going to enter Paradise, so there's no point of God holding them accountable for anything.", "The حساب (Hisab: accountability), which is: you've done this, you've done that, this is the amount of good deeds, this is the amount of bad deeds – that doesn't matter, because the person died as a disbeliever, and therefore they have no chance of entering Paradise anyways.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Shockingly Describes Life After Death Like You Are Witnessing It! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lePF6KO1aZA", ((338, "5:38–6:04"), (367, "6:07–6:30"), (396, "6:36–7:13"), (437, "7:17–7:55"), (479, "7:59–8:06"),), id: 656)
