#passage(("In Islam, this worldly life is a world of testing, and the afterlife is a world of reward. So, it's not about the resurrection. The resurrection is where you move into the next stage. You've been in an exam and a test. You have a piece of paper. You solve, then you move into the stage of either you succeeded or you failed. The afterlife is the conclusion. So you're focusing on the resurrection. You cannot have the resurrection without focusing what you're doing right now, in the moment, in Islam. What you do right now, what you think right now, every action you do right now, is what matters, because it is going to determine what's going to happen in the afterlife. This is just the Islamic worldview.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “The Muslim Lantern, Sneako and Arab Debate Religion! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QiBVA3ZecoI", ((3400, "56:40–57:22"),), id: 658)

