#passage(("Belief in the Last Day, because when you believe in the Last Day and you read the descriptions of Hellfire, and you read the descriptions of Jannah (Paradise), you wouldn't be daring to do the things that you do. You wouldn't dare to transgress against the Maharim of Allahﷻ (against the Boundaries of Allahﷻ), because you understand what are the consequences of doing that.", "There is the example that a friend told me once, and it's a beautiful example, because it fits into this idea. You go to work, you have a boss. If the boss is lenient, you slack on the job, you go here and there for a few hours, you eat and drink, you're not working properly. But if you know your boss is a guy who's like, if he sees anything wrong he's going to fire you, you behave accordingly. So, ولِلّه المَثَلُ الأَعلى (for Allah is the highest of examples), there is no comparison, but what you know of Allah is how you're going to behave.", "So, those people, the only thing they know about Allahﷻ is what? He is Merciful; if your sins reach the sky; all of these things. \"Compassionate\" Imams today that tell compassion every day, day and night, compassion only, nothing else in the Deen (Religion) of Allah. Muslims have absorbed this. And based on that, they think Allah is only Merciful: do whatever you like!", "But Allahﷻ in the Quran, for a حِكمَة, for a عِلَّة, for a reason, in multiple verses, not one, He gathers punishment and reward together: ٱعْلَمُوٓا۟ أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ شَدِيدُ ٱلْعِقَابِ وَأَنَّ ٱللَّهَ غَفُورٌۭ رَّحِيمٌۭ. Just one verse! (alMaida5:98) One verse just telling you these two things together, so you understand: أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ شَدِيدُ ٱلْعِقَابِ (Allah is Severe in punishment), وَأَنَّ ٱللَّهَ غَفُورٌۭ رَّحِيمٌۭ (And Allah is Forgiving and Merciful). Don't take one and leave the other.", "Do what Sheikh alislam Ibn alQayyim said: \"Muslim is like a bird, he has two wings, Hope and Fear; you're in the middle. If you lean too much into one, it's a problem; if you lean too much into the other, it's a problem.\" Of course, not everything is fear. Also, you can not despair from Allah's Mercy: إِنَّهُۥ لَا یَا۟یۡـَٔسُ مِن رَّوۡحِ ٱللَّهِ إِلَّا ٱلۡقَوۡمُ ٱلۡكَـٰفِرُونَ (Yusuf12:87). Only the disobedient, disbelieving people are the ones who despair from Allah's Mercy completely. We don't despair from Allah's Mercy, but at the same time we know that Allah has boundaries, and those boundaries are to be respected, and we have to do our best, and this is how we obtain Allah's Mercy.", "You believe in the Last Day, you understand the Last Day, the حساب (Accountability), the موقف (Standing before Allah). What's going to happen to me when I stand before Allah? The قنطرة (Bridge)? What is this قنطرة? What is the صراط (Path)? What is going to happen when I walk there? These things, when you visualise it, when you put in your mind as a Muslim, your behavior becomes in accordance to what you know.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “The Situation Of The Ummah, The Disease & The Cure | Al Muwahiddeen Mosque - The Netherlands |”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0ycNKKOx2jg", ((3284, "54:44–55:01"), (3304, "55:04–55:34"), (3338, "55:38–55:53"), (3359, "55:59–56:23"), (3386, "56:26–56:53"), (3420, "57:00–57:12"),), id: 659)
