#passage(("Why do you say this system of life is a perfect system? Of course, there's many things that are not perfect within the world. For instance, there are people who exist in this life who can commit terrible atrocities, and they can die without being punished for these atrocities.", "We have a clear example today. We have Satanyahu of the Zionist movement today, and that Satan of a human being exists today. And he hasn't begun on October the 7th or something. For 20, 30, 40 years – the invasion of Iraq, everything you can think about, evil that happened – he had some hand in that evil that took place. And until today he lives as a prime minister, he has private jets, he eats what he wants, he drinks what he wants, and he continues this genocide. Now, let's assume, like other presidents, which we had this happening in history, he dies on his deathbed of old age or whatever. Now, how is that a perfect system in your worldview?", "Even if we assume my position is irrational, that doesn't answer or account for your position, because I'm not the one who's making a point of \"Life right now is a perfect system\". You are the one who's making that claim. I'm critiquing your claim right now on your worldview. Any rational person would agree that this is not a perfect system.", "We're not discussing the existence of Heaven and Hell. We are asking the question: in your worldview, if we were to subtract this idea and take it away, does that claim that the system right now is perfect, is it actually perfect? Then you went on: I'm not talking about this pixel, I'm talking about the bigger picture. That doesn't answer my question.", "Yes, he did influence other people negatively, he killed people, he slaughtered people. So now we are asking for justice for those people. Number one, how can they get their justice? Because right now they're dead. They're done. They lived a life of torture, a life of evil, a life of being destroyed, a life of being tortured in prison until they're killed. And that person lived a life of afflicting those punishments. Therefore, the answer is that that's not a perfect system, because, number one, you cannot give justice to the people who were wronged, and you cannot give justice to the person who's doing evil.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Omnist Left Speechless After Hearing This Muslim's Answer! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yVHQD2W5S0c", ((315, "5:15–6:35"), (406, "6:46–7:32"), (496, "8:16–8:41"), (630, "10:30–10:52"), (654, "10:54–11:54"),), id: 660)
