#passage(("Now, on the other hand, let's assume Satanyaho, instead of saying on his deathbed, let's say a few years before his death, he's still healthy and everything, and then he comes back and repents. Now, of course, the first thing he needs to do is to try his best to rectify what he can for what he did, admit to the evil that he did, rectify as much as he can. But still, there's other elements here which are missing: the people who were harmed, or got killed, or the people that whatever happened to them, they will be getting their justice in the Afterlife.", "Here is where the Afterlife fixes the picture. It's not only the punishment of the evildoer, it's also the mercy given to the people who injustice happened to. Those people go to heaven. There's good deeds and bad deeds in the Afterlife, and your good deeds need to outweigh your bad deeds in order for you to enter Paradise.", "So when someone's done evil, there are ways to get your retribution from them. One way is, for instance, that you take from their good deeds, if they have any, to increase your good deeds. Or you would give them from your bad deeds, if they have no good deeds to give you. So it'll be upon them more and more, so more punishment for them. But you can get your justice in the Afterlife.", "So that system of the Afterlife that we talk about completes this gap, this moral gap which you cannot explain, which nobody can explain, because this world will just be an evil void of suffering and hatred and no accountability, if you don't have that in the end, the justice system that takes place. And that justice system, what even perfects it more is that The One Who will do the judging is The Creator: it's Allah, it's God.", "And if God is The One Who's going to do the judging, He knows every detail of your life: your intention, what you wanted to do, why you didn't want to do. So your idea of a small picture and pixel and whatever: God knows everything (alImran3:29). And that is why Allah is The Judge. That is why one of His Names is الحَكَم alHakam. He's The One Who's going to deliver the justice to the people, and He's The One Who's going to give mercy to people who deserve mercy.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Omnist Left Speechless After Hearing This Muslim's Answer! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yVHQD2W5S0c", ((818, "13:38–14:01"), (851, "14:11–14:32"), (876, "14:36–14:55"), (898, "14:58–15:22"), (927, "15:27–15:52"),), id: 661)
