#passage(("I know the verse you're referring to, (Muhammad47:9): \"Because they hate what Allah has revealed, so He nullified their deeds.\" Are you going to be accountable if you do something wrong to someone who is not a Muslim? As a Muslim, you're accountable for your deeds. If you wrong a Muslim or a non-Muslim, you'll be accountable for that.", "But the thing is that if someone dies a disbeliever, he cannot benefit from taking from your deeds and go to Paradise, for example. He's not going to benefit, because now his destination is The Fire. So it does not matter if he gets deeds or he doesn't get deeds. There will be no process in which he will get deeds from the believer, but the believer will be accountable. So that is a sin upon the believer that he will be accountable and responsible for, that he will have to account for with God.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Sister Cries After Realising Islam Is The Truth! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PtJpInP1jl8", ((703, "11:43–13:26"), (812, "13:32–13:56"),), id: 662)
