#passage(("We believe humans can also judge as a representation of God. Allah says in the Quran about Prophet Muhammad (anNisa4:65): فَلَا وَرَبِّكَ لَا یُؤۡمِنُونَ حَتَّىٰ یُـــحَـــكِّـــمُـــوكَ فِیمَا شَجَرَ بَیۡنَهُمۡ ثُمَّ لَا یَجِدُوا۟ فِیۤ أَنفُسِهِمۡ حَرَجࣰا مِّمَّا قَضَیۡتَ وَیُسَلِّمُوا۟ تَسۡلِیمࣰا (By your Lord they will not believe until they make you a judge over their affairs) (then they don't find any displeasure in your decision and completely submit to your decision). This is about Prophet Muhammad. We don't have a problem in someone judging. The one who is judging in the end of days is Allah. Allah says in the Quran (alAnaam6:62) that the Judgment on that Day is only for Allah.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Arab Christian Attempts To Convert A Muslim But This Happens! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J1fLxzg-AgY", ((1900, "31:40–32:29"),), id: 663)
