#passage(("Some Muslims will be punished. So if their bad deeds outweigh their good deeds, that means they still are going to be punished before they enter Paradise, because they didn't do as best as they could in this life. No one is going to be perfect. Allah doesn't ask you to be perfect, but he asks you to do as much as you can. And Allah makes it super easy for you, actually! One good deed, you get 10 times the reward in Islam, to 700, to an unlimited amount, if Allah wants to increase you, depending on your intention.", "Maybe Allah see you one day: one person, he had only two pounds, and he was hungry, and he brought bread, and he gave it to someone else! And he has no money, as he has only that two pounds! For that very small deed – that if I were to do, and I have millions, I'm not going to get the same reward, because of the situation, because of the circumstances – Allah can give him a reward that we cannot even imagine, because of that simple action.", "That's why in Islam, you have an example of a woman who was a prostitute, and there was a thirsty dog in the desert, and she was going by a well, and his tongue was out because he was thirsty; he's going to die from thirst. And then she went in, she used her shoes, and she gave him water, and then Allah forgave her for that. She lived a sinful life – if you can use the term \"Sinful life\" – but still, she was forgiven because of that specific action she did.", "In Islam, there are Minor Sins and Major Sins. For the Major Sins, you have to seek repentance, but for the Minor Sins, if you do good deeds, Allah forgives them. Allah says (Hud11:114) إِنَّ ٱلْحَسَنَـٰتِ يُذْهِبْنَ ٱلسَّيِّـَٔاتِ: Good deeds remove bad deeds. Without you even asking for anything, you just do good deeds and Allah removes from the bad deeds that you have. Allah gives you chances and opportunities: when you go to Hajj حج (Pilgrimage), and then he forgives all these sins if you do a correct Pilgrimage. He gives you Ramadan; he forgives all your past sins if you fast Ramadan correctly, or you pray in Ramadan.", "But still, there will be some Muslims, some of us, who are not good, not taking that, even though it's so easy. We're not taking this handout – if you use that term – from Allahﷻ, we're still living a bad life, and in the end, our bad deeds will outweigh our good deeds, and we'll be punished for a period of time, if we're Muslims. Then you're going to enter Paradise. Because accountability is not for disbelievers anyway: if you are a disbeliever, you go to Hellfire straight away; there is no point of accountability. This accountability is for the Muslims.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Surprises Muslim With Unusual Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cluCTYA-UgM", ((371, "6:11–6:37"), (401, "6:41–7:02"), (426, "7:06–7:30"), (456, "7:36–8:04"), (488, "8:08–8:37"),), id: 665)
