#passage(("I think you should be more worried about where you're going to end up. We can ask all of these questions: \"Where's my uncle going?\" \"Where is my nephew going?\" \"Where is my niece going?\" I don't even know where I'm going! None of us in this life has a guarantee where are they going to end up, because none of these questions matter unless you are in Paradise. And asking them gives the impression that someone thinks: \"I'm going to be in Paradise.\" But you don't know! Do you deserve to be in Paradise? I'm not accusing you of that intention. Only God knows the intentions. But when you ask a question that way, it removes the most important question, which is: where are you ending up?", "Because Allah tells us in the Quran (Abasa80:33-34) (on that Day), the Day of Judgment, یَوۡمَ یَفِرُّ ٱلۡمَرۡءُ مِنۡ أَخِیهِ (You run away from your brother, your mother, your father) (your wife, and your children). Everyone will say, \"myself!\" Even Narrations about the Prophets of God: people will come to them on the Day of Judgment, and they will say: \"Intercede for us with God,\" and the Prophet will say: نَفْسي (myself). If the Prophet of God is saying \"myself\" – because it's done! The time of this life is over, that's it! You've done what you can. You had all the chances – if they will say that, imagine us! Nobody is going to be worried about someone else.", "Allah says (alHajj22:2) تَذۡهَلُ كُلُّ مُرۡضِعَةٍ عَمَّاۤ أَرۡضَعَتۡ (when every breastfeeding woman will be completely blown away from the fact that she needs to breastfeed her child) on that Day! وَتَضَعُ كُلُّ ذَاتِ حَمْلٍ حَمْلَهَا (And every pregnant woman will give birth) وَتَرَى النَّاسَ سُكَارَىٰ وَمَا هُم بِسُكَارَىٰ (You see the people, you think they're drunk!) They're not drunk, but because of the severity of that Day!", "And now, of course, after that, Allah says in the Quran (atTahrim66:6) (O you who believe, protect yourself, then your family). We're not saying forget about your family, but your family comes after you. First, know where you are going. Have you done what is necessarily needed for you to end up in the right place? And then after that, you should worry about your family. You should want good for them. You should try to invite them to the Message of Islam. You should try to show them proofs and evidences. But in the end, you should know that you are not more merciful than Allah.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Shockingly Describes Life After Death Like You Are Witnessing It! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lePF6KO1aZA", ((656, "10:56–11:50"), (712, "11:52–12:23"), (748, "12:28–12:45"), (789, "13:09–13:36"),), id: 670)
