#passage(("The entirety of Heaven is sexualized? At least you're coming to a Muslim to ask the question. I'll tell you that is the best source: the best would be the people who actually believe the thing.", "So we wouldn't say food is sexual, for example. Jannah (Paradise) is where you have whatever your heart desires. So of course everything in Jannah is the desires of a Human being, because it's a Reward and you're rewarded by what you desire. That's the definition of a Reward. If I give you something you don't desire, that is not a reward.", "So Paradise from an Islamic perspective is a Reward: you have gardens in Jannah, you have Rivers. You have drinks that are not like the drinks of this life. For example, you have alcohol that is not like the alcohol of this life. It's not sour like the alcohol in this life, that does not give you a hangover, complete different type of alcohol. You have milk that does not go off, you've honey that is 100% pure, which you don't have in this life, cannot have a 100% pure honey. These types of things would be in Paradise. Fruits, different fruits etc., you'll have in Paradise as the Quran describes.", "You have حور العين “Hoor Al-'Ain”, which is a Creation of God, a Feminine Creation of God that is given to men. You have palaces, gold, you have silver, you have beds, you have everything that your heart desires. So the things that human beings would desire, and anything they can desire or ask for, in Paradise they can be given, according to the Quran.", "And Paradise has different levels, and the Highest Reward in Paradise that is mentioned in the Hadith is where Allahﷻ will speak to the Believers. And He will say to the Believers (are you satisfied?), with all of these things that I mentioned. And then they will say: (Yes). So Allah says He will increase them, and they will see Allah! This is the Highest Reward we will have in Paradise.", "The people who will be in Paradise will see Allah. The people who are not in Paradise, they're not going to see Allah. In fact Allah explicitly says in the (Quran83:15) that (they would be veiled away from Allah). The Disbelievers, they are not going to see, because it’s a Reward. It's not just \"A reward\". When you see something beautiful, that's a reward. Allah is the Source of Beauty. Allah is the Most Beautiful, and one of the Names of Allah is Al-Jameel, so the most beautiful is Allah and beauty comes from Allah. So seeing Allah is the Highest Reward that Believers will have in Paradise.", "But as I said, it's a place of reward. In this life, if you know a bit about Islam, you might know some of these rules of Muslims: they don't have intercourse before marriage, for example. Muslims don't drink alcohol, they don't eat pork. So you hear about prohibitions in this life, things that Allah prohibits you; you stop them, you don't do them in this life, because Allah prohibited you from doing them in this life, and Allah rewards you in the afterlife by giving you what your heart desires. So Paradise is a place of reward, and if you agree that paradise is a place of reward, then it would make sense for you to have your desires there.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Lady Enquires About Heaven In Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NyrpGRsef5I", ((16, "0:16–0:59"), (62, "1:02–1:20"), (83, "1:23–1:47"), (113, "1:53–2:03"), (131, "2:11–2:23"), (149, "2:29–2:56"), (188, "3:08–3:35"),), id: 679)
