#passage(("I don't think they say you \"do\" anything, they say you \"get\" anything. I think it's the difference between the two. Allah says in the Quran (Fussilat41:31) (that you get what your heart desires from the good things). So the thing is that Allah takes away any evil things from the hearts of the people in the Paradise, so they do not desire anything which is evil. For example Allah says in the Quran(AlHjir15:47) “وَنَزَعۡنَا مَا فِي صُدُورِهِم مِّنۡ غِلٍّ” (and we have stripped away any enmity and hatred from their hearts) إِخۡوَٰنًا عَلَىٰ سُرُرٖ مُّتَقَٰبِلِينَ (then they are brothers). So that means that everyone in Brotherhood, there is no hatred and enmity that one person has towards the other person.", "So Allah takes away any desire for something which is not good from the heart of a person. You wouldn't desire something bad in Paradise. To put it simply, you desire things which are good, because we are born upon what we call the Fitra. Fitra is an innate disposition that Allah created us with. It's a pure disposition. So Prophetﷺ said “كلُّ مولودٍ يولَدُ على الفطرةِ” (Every child is born upon this innate natural disposition) to recognize the Truth or to be upon goodness. \"فأبواه يُهوِّدانِه أو يُنصِّرانِه أو يُمجِّسانِه\" Then his parents they change him into Christian, Jew, Atheist and any of that. So naturally we are upon this natural position of Fitra; we don't desire this nonsense. Innately we don't. Therefore in Jannah, in our purest form, we don't desire this rubbish as well. These things are not going to be in Paradise.", "Reincarnation necessitates death. But there is no planet Earth and all of these things in that time. You're in Paradise; Paradise is an actual place. So you'll be abiding in Paradise, and the Quran (Al-Kahf18:108) says: ”خَٰلِدِينَ فِيهَا لَا يَبۡغُونَ عَنۡهَا حِوَلٗا” (They will not wish to be removed to any other place). They will not wish to be changed in their reality because they are pleased. They are ultimately happy.", "Imagine you are in a place where you have whatever you like, whatever you desire, you become more beautiful every day. Everything you desire is there; no one wants to “let me reincarnate to a monkey and just do whatever monkeys do”. You would not desire anything other than that. You cannot even imagine what you will have in Paradise. That's the thing Prophetﷺ told us, that Allah said: (What no eyes have seen, what no ear have heard and no mind can imagine). What you have there, you wouldn't even be thinking about anywhere else.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Intelligent Man Examines The Evidences For Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CyXdIF4BXok", ((419, "6:59–7:26"), (452, "7:32–8:11"), (494, "8:14–8:47"), (533, "8:53–9:21"),), id: 683)
