#passage(("There's one paradise. There's different levels, but not seven. The Quran says seven Heavens. Seven Heavens there is not referring to Paradise. There's different levels in Paradise, and these levels are based on the deeds that you do. There's also different levels, grades, in hellfire; it's not even one place, you go down and down and down based on the evil that you've done in the world as well. Punishment is not equal and also reward is not equal. So in جنة (Jannah: Paradise) there is different levels, and the highest level is called فردوس (Firdaous), which can be translated into Paradise. So Firdaous is the highest level and it is under the Throne of Allahﷻ. It is the highest level of Paradise and the highest level of reward, and there will be the Prophets and the most righteous individuals. So based on the deeds that you make, you will reach a specific level in Paradise.", "Allahﷻ says in the Quran (Qaf50:35) لَهُم مَّا یَشَاۤءُونَ فِیهَا (for them whatever they will or wish for in there). In paradise, there are certain things that you're not going to wish for. You're not going to wish for evil things, for example, towards other individuals.", "So you're not going to wish for something evil; injustice is one of these things, because you know you're justly in that position. But you're not going to only know you're justly in that position, you will be pleased to be where you are. You'll be so much pleased with whatever you have. And there's always increasing of pleasure and reward from Allah, to the extent that you would not wish to be anywhere else. So you'd be completely pleased to the maximum level that you can be; Allah is going to give you that.", "If he's a Believer, there's a chance for this to take place, because there is a Hadith where the Prophetﷺ told us that a believer in Paradise would be saying to Allah: \"Ô Allah my joy is not complete without my friend being with me\", but he's a Muslim. It is impossible for any non-Muslim to enter Paradise. This has been decreed by Allah. Allahﷻ says in the Quran (Almaida5:72) مَن یُشۡرِكۡ بِٱللَّهِ فَقَدۡ حَرَّمَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَیۡهِ ٱلۡجَنَّةَ (whoever disbelieves in Allah or associates with Allah, Allah has made Janna Haram, prohibited, forbidden, he's not allowed to enter that place).", "So, if you are a Believer, there is a chance, because Believers will go to Hellfire for a period of time. The ones that were disobedient, that did not repent and died with Major Sins, they don't get a free pass, they're still punished for the evil that they did. Then the Prophetﷺ told us that this is the benefit of having good friends that are righteous friends. So that person will be taken to be joined with his friend just because of the wish of that friend. So this is a possibility if the person is a Believer, and you are a righteous person that entered Paradise.", "But Allah has to be pleased. This is something called شفاعة (Shafa'a), which is Intercession, the act of intercession, and it is based on Allah being pleased with you, being pleased with that person that he's going to allow you to be with, and permission of Allah. These are three conditions. If these conditions are fulfilled, then that can take place. This is the importance of having righteous friends around you, people who are actually good friends.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Popular Youtuber Asks Muslim Difficult Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S7bA8bsNs20", ((1587, "26:27–27:25"), (1661, "27:41–27:55"), (1699, "28:19–28:58"), (1751, "29:11–29:39"), (1784, "29:44–30:18"), (1823, "30:23–30:41"),), id: 684)
