#passage(("Allah عز وجل says in the Quran7:43: We removed any enmity from their hearts. So no one is gonna say I don't wanna see you. People will be visiting one another, and the Hadith mentions that when you visit them, you will increase in beauty and they will increase beauty. The next time you visit them, they will increase more in beauty, and they will say to each other: you've increased in beauty and goodness since the last time we saw you.", "Of course the way you think will change, because of what you will see. It's not that you will be pre-programmed to want something different. That's not what is going to happen to you. You will be you, and even people will recognize you, because there are Narrations about people in Paradise and Hellfire, they're recognized by other people, which means you will be recognizable. People will know your identity, who you are, and you will be yourself.", "But the point is this. When the world of the Unseen is unveiled for you to see, of course your perception of things will be different, because now you've seen so many other information that you didn't know before. So the petty things probably that you want, it might change based on what you've seen. This is what will change in your mentality: your mentality will change based on the information that you will absorb. But you will be the same person, the same human being. You'll have a different body, but you'll be the same human being, and you'll be recognizable by other people as well. So it will be YOU. Otherwise it wouldn't make any sense for it to be a reward for you to begin with. How is it going to be a reward for YOU, or a punishment for YOU, if it's not YOU being punished or rewarded? It will be YOU, the same individual.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Challenges Muslim On God Then This Happens! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MSk1AiEaXH8", ((888, "14:48–15:16"), (939, "15:39–16:02"), (967, "16:07–16:42"),), id: 686)
