#passage(("We don't know that actually. atTabari, which is one of the classical exegetes, he talked about this. Because even for us time is relative. If you exist right now on the moon, time works for you differently than it worked when you're on planet Earth, if you're measuring it with the Sun and the Sun's movement; it's a relative thing. So, \"how does it work in Paradise?\" We do not know exactly how it works. You have to be there to understand. But it's eternal life anyways! So it would be irrelevant how time is functioning in that way, because it is an eternal existence to the end. It's not something that stops, but how exactly time works there is not something that we know.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Attempts To Explain The Concept Of God! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Y0EuiG8SUZM", ((1468, "24:28–25:09"),), id: 687)
