#passage(("Talking about Sikhism: you can enter Heaven just by being a devout person in your own religion, you don't necessarily need to become Sikh, which is completely false.", "There's the difference between post Eternal and Pre-Eternal. Pre-Eternal is being eternal in the past, and post Eternal is being Eternal in the future. So God is the only one who's Post and Pre-Eternal.", "God can logically create something that remains in the future and does not perish, but it's remaining is based on God. Because God is preserving it, it is there, and God is Eternal, so he can keep that thing eternally. Logically what is the problem there? It's not equal to Him because it's not Eternal in the past, so how is it equal to Him? First, it's created, number one. Number two, it is not Eternal in the past. Number three, its existence and eternality is dependent on God, while God's Existence and Eternality is dependent on no one. So to claim they are equal is logically false.", "Do you speak? Can you love and hate? Can God have similar attributes to these things? Can God also speak, can God hate, and can God love, reward, punish, and all of these things that we can do, can God do them or not? Does that mean we're equal now? Because we've got an attribute that God has, does that mean we're equal with God? God's Eternality is perfect and a Creation post eternality is not perfect, so it's not the same, just like your attribute is not the same with God's attributes.", "I can have an attribute of knowledge, love, hatred, this and this and that, and God can have these attributes as well. But He has this attributes maximally perfect, while I have a limited version of those attributes. And just because both of us have a similar attribute, or the same attribute in a different level, does not mean we're equal to God. The same thing when it comes to eternality: if a Creation was to be a post Eternal, this attribute of eternality is a limited attribute of a eternality, while God's Eternality is perfect. So just because we share an attribute does not mean that we're equal to God, and that was your premise, which is a false premise.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Sikh Challenges Muslim On The Preservation Of The Quran! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3FaWv_XB4Eo", ((1161, "19:21–19:50"), (1194, "19:54–19:58"), (1209, "20:09–20:57"), (1270, "21:10–21:40"), (1320, "22:00–22:31"),), id: 691)

