#passage(("It's not limited to 72. Paradise is a reward, a place of reward, and Allahﷻ says you can have what you want in there (alFurqan25:16). Men have desires and women have desires. For the man, the number one desire is women, always. Therefore, it's natural that Allah will mention women as a reward for the man, because this is the first thing that he desires. You want to have a million women, you can have a million women, 2, 3, 4, 11. So the women in paradise, for example, if they're married, they're going to be with their husbands.", "The way you're thinking about it right now, you're thinking from a worldly perspective, meaning you're thinking if things were happening in this world, I'd be thinking about it that way. First, the women in paradise, if you want to use the term women for them, are حور العين, and they're not like the women of this life. They're a specific creation made by Allahﷻ. Now, no one is saying the woman is going to sit around and do this. This is not the description of how things are happening in paradise.", "Allahﷻ says in the Quran (alHaqqa69:21-22) (Whoever is in paradise, whether it is the man or the woman, they will be CONTENT with their position). You're not going to be upset and jealous and fighting, the things that happen in this life between women, one another. It does not happen. Allah removes any enmity, any hatred, any of these things, any jealousy (alHijr15:47). All of these things that cause issues in this life, Allahﷻ completely removes them in paradise, because paradise, as I said, is a place of reward.", "Also, the woman, when we say she's the wife of the man, that doesn't mean she's sitting around for him. She's also having her rewards. If she thinks about something or desires something, food, anything, you can have it in paradise. So, Paradise is a reward for both men and women. It's not like the woman is going to be there just for the man, for the husband, or whatever it is.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Lady Questions Muslim On Evidence Of God! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Nk4EM0u0VNs", ((968, "16:08–16:47"), (1020, "17:00–17:20"), (1046, "17:26–17:56"), (1076, "17:56–18:12"),), id: 692)
