#passage(("The description of paradise is genderless in the Quran; there's no description for men and description for women. So the Quran does not differentiate in the description on Paradise for men and women. Everything I mentioned, food and all of these things and seeing Allah, that’s all for men and women in Paradise. Allahﷻ says in the (Quran4:124) (and whoever believes in Allah and does righteous deeds, whether believing men or women -MEN OR WOMEN- Allah will reward them).", "حور العين Hoor Al'ain, that's gendered. Paradise is not about Hoor Al'ain; Paradise is about what your heart desires. And Allah created men and women differently. The physiology of men and women are different. For example most women, they would desire to be with one man that they love and admire and they respect. But the nature of most men, that they want multiple women, is the nature of men. So when you talk about the types of reward, this specific reward that you ask about, Hoor Al'ain, it will be in accordance to the physiology of men and women. But that's the only example that you can mention.", "So if a women do not want multiple men, why is it a problem for them not to get multiple men? This is a claim that a lot of people make. For me it's just ridiculous for someone to say that \"they don't get this!\" but they don't want this! So why would they get something that they do not want? But they get what they want, that's the thing that Allah says in the Quran. Man or a woman, you get what you want, and everything else I mentioned is for both men and women.", "I’ll tell you something interesting. Pew Research, it's one of the biggest Research Centers in America. So according to Pew Research Institute, by conversion, the biggest growing religion in the world is Islam, conversion rate not birth rate. 3 out of every 4 people that accept Islam are women. Imagine 3 out of 4 people who accept Islam are women and there's nothing for them in Paradise!", "But get to Paradise first! That's the point! When you get to Paradise you can ask these questions, like which specific type of reward you will get. And Allahﷻ says that the people will not want to move away from Paradise, which means all of their desires will be fulfilled. Allah says at the end of chapter 18 of the (Quran18:108) لَا يَبْغُونَ عَنْهَا حِوَلًا (they do not desire to turn away from their current state).",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Lady Enquires About Heaven In Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NyrpGRsef5I", ((253, "4:13–4:28"), (276, "4:36–5:24"), (332, "5:32–5:59"), (372, "6:12–6:39"), (421, "7:01–7:15"),), id: 697)
