#passage(("God did not make Hell for that reason. يَوْمَ نَقُولُ لِجَهَنَّمَ هَلِ امْتَلَأْتِ وَتَقُولُ هَلْ مِن مَّزِيدٍ: This is a statement of a question that will be in the Future. But where does Allah say in the verse جعلنا جهنم لتملأ بالكافرين (we made Hellfire to be filled with disbelievers)? Allah doesn't say that. Allah says a fact, that Allah will ask Jahannam (Hellfire) on The Day Of Judgment: Are You full or not yet? And then Jahannam will ask: is there more people to be put in Hellfire?", "Why did Allah make Hellfire? Allah made Hellfire for the people who will choose to go to Hellfire by disbelief in Allah. So Allah did not make Hellfire so he can necessarily force some people inside there to burn. Allah made Hellfire for the people who deserve to be punished, for the people who will be unjust in this life, for the people who do evil to other individuals, for the people who will do things in this life in which they can maybe get away with them in this life. Hellfire will balance out that scale. So those people will be punished for the things that they did in this life. And for example, you see someone who's an evil person, who goes to the park and then he does things with little children. Where do you think that person should go? And no one caught him all his life? Hell makes sense because it's for the people who do evil.", "You do not go to eternal Hellfire for drinking alcohol. It's a sin, but Allah doesn't say that you go to Hellfire forever for drinking alcohol. The only sin that keeps someone in Eternal Hellfire is disbelieving in Allah or associating partners with Him, i.e. الكفر والشرك (Disbelief and polytheism). These are the two only sins that can allow someone to be in eternal Hellfire.", "And why? Because they denied The Maker of the universe, they denied The One Who made them, Who gave them all the blessings that they have, Who gave them everyone around them, Who provides for them on a daily basis even though they disbelieved in Him, Who is The One Who allowed them to breath air. When they go to sleep their heart keeps pumping, because He created them with that heart. The eyesight that they have, that they choose to disobey Him with, to deny His existence with, He gave it to them. Those are the people who spend Eternality in Hellfire, because they made the biggest sin, which is to completely deny the existence of The Creator as if He's not there. And still Allah leaves them in this life until they die; they have a chance to come back.", "So drinking alcohol is a sin, but there is repentance, and if you don't repent you can be punished for a while, but you're not punished forever in Hellfire.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Tunisian Girl Questions Muslim On Women's Rights! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l68vK6nDhbA", ((456, "7:36–8:04"), (488, "8:08–9:01"), (543, "9:03–9:23"), (563, "9:23–9:57"), (602, "10:02"),), id: 701)
