#passage(("Allah doesn't threaten people with hellfire to join the congregation! That's not the case. Allah says in the Quran (alKahf18:29) فَمَن شَآءَ فَلْيُؤْمِن وَمَن شَآءَ فَلْيَكْفُرْ (Whoever wishes to believe, let him believe, whoever wishes to disbelieve, let him disbelieve). But then it says there's consequences to [disbelief]. It's a very simple thing. It says to you, if you do the wrong thing, there are consequences to that wrong thing. It's not threatening, that's warning. Warning and threatening is not the same thing. Telling someone that if you do something wrong, there will be consequences for that, that's not threatening them to join the faith, because Allah tells us in the Quran (alBaqara2:256), لَآ إِكْرَاهَ فِى ٱلدِّينِ (There's no compulsion in acceptance of the religion). Explicitly, you cannot compel anyone to accept the religion.", "But of course, it's a moral responsibility on you to tell people that if you do this specific action, there will be this consequence. Because when they're punished, they cannot come and say: \"I was ignorant, I didn't know that this will happen to me.\" No! You've been warned. You've been told examples. You've been told verses. And you chose to still do the wrong thing, and this is the consequences of your actions. So this very simple common sense is what the Quran is teaching, and what the Quran is talking about.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| Atheist Disproves The Quran?! Is Ezra The Son Of God? Islam Predates Judaism|”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0_RrmYKq0qU", ((1140, "19:00–19:37"), (1180, "19:40–20:10"),), id: 702)
