#passage(("So if I were to put it that way, just put it very crudely or simply, as they say: God created you. We have the saying in Islam, inna lillahi wa inna ilayhi rajioon: We belong to Allah and to him we shall return. And if I create something, I have complete control of what I want to do with that thing that I've created. It's a simple creation. It didn't even exist unless I willed it into existence.", "Now, I gave certain conditions to that created thing. I'm merciful with it. I give it a very easy test. I even allowed it to cheat in so many ways: do one good thing, you get 10 points, to an unlimited amount. Do one bad thing, it's only one bad thing. If you do good things, they will remove your bad things. If you have a thought of doing a bad thing and you stop, I'll give you a good point. I can go on and on and talk about how easy the test is.", "So God creates a creation that belongs to him, of course. He gives it a very easy criteria, very easy test. All you have to do is this very simple things. Don't be perfect. You will fall, but just repent. Just stick to these very simple things. Do them and you will attain paradise. And then, one after the other, keeps sending you warnings. Warnings through messengers, warning through verses, warning through signs in your life, warning through people talking about you. Once and once again: if you don't do these simple things and you choose to live a sinful life and disbelieve in God, you are going to be punished for eternity. Over and over again, this warning, warning, warning.", "And then, after this very easy test and very easy requirement, and God has been so merciful with you, allowing you all of these chances and opportunities, you still end up to disbelieve in that God. You still end up to die in disbelieve, even though you will know in your heart it's a truth, cuz you have a fitra. You have an innate position to recognize the truth, and you will die upon that rejection.", "Then God says, \"I've given you this opportunity. I've created you. I've been merciful with you. And in fact, I was so merciful with you that I allowed you to live while you curse me, you disbelieve in me, you insult me, you do all of these things, and I give you food, I give you sustenance, I allow you to live, to laugh, to enjoy, to travel, to do whatever you want. And I warned you that if you continue upon this and you die, this will be your outcome.\" Then he gets that outcome. I want to understand what's the problematic thing when you put it that way, which is the Islamic perspective. Where is the issue there?",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Claims That Pantheism Is More Rational Than Monotheism! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=C3BXt0zJr3o", ((288, "4:48–5:10"), (312, "5:12–5:40"), (340, "5:40–6:14"), (381, "6:21–6:40"), (401, "6:41–7:15"),), id: 705)
