#passage(("I'll say that, yes, God doesn't burn His children. No human would burn his children. But God does not have children. God has creation. He created us. And God doesn't burn us. We chose hellfire by disobeying God and by harming other people in our existence and in our life. The Prophet, he told us: \"everyone enters paradise except those who refuse\". So the people asked the Prophet: \"Who would refuse going to paradise?\" The Prophet said: \"who obeys the Creator's command, who obeys the Prophet, then he will go to paradise\". Who disobeys God and the Prophet's command, then he has refused! Because it's your choice to obey and disobey God.", "Of course, the Quran talks about Hell. The Quran is the Message that Prophet Muhammad brought. The Prophet expounded on the Quran. Of course, Hellfire exists.", "What is your position on what's happening in Palestine? Do you believe that what you see in the videos and the pictures, there are people who are worth being punished in the most hideous ways, because of what they do to innocent children and women? And they're using these Bible verses, \"the Amalekites\"; they're using the verses in the Bible to justify it.", "Hellfire exists as a form of justice for the people who were wronged, and as a form of justice, as punishment for people who do evil. Rationally, I can never accept a world with no Hellfire. That means every person who did evil in his life and died without getting punished, they're getting away with it. And there's millions of people, examples of that. I'd never accept that this is a just worldview at all. Hellfire, from my point of view, is a necessity, and it must exist for anything to be just and rational.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Grills Muslim With Difficult And Inquisitive Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eOPafAukvyc", ((608, "10:08–10:42"), (663, "11:03–11:29"), (706, "11:46–11:59"), (741, "12:21–12:54"),), id: 706)
