#passage(("Islam is wrong because God sends people to Hell and He doesn't give freedom of choice, according to you. How do you go to Hellfire in Islam? There's only one thing you can do for that punishment, which is Shirk (association) and Kufr (disbelief).", "This eternal punishment, if someone does Shirk and Kufr, is it for everyone, or is it for specific people that hear the Message and evidences of Islam first? It's for people who hear the Message and evidence of Islam. Number one. Number two: is it for people who heard the Message and straight away they go to eternal punishment? Or is it they're given the chance until they die, to accept the Truth or not? That's what giving the chance means.", "It's not about point of view. We're talking about facts. Can anyone come and say \"I'm going to become a Muslim\"? \"I testify there's nothing worthy of worship except Allah and Prophet Muhammad is His Messenger\"? Can anyone do this, if they wanted to? And would that mean that they're Muslims? So anyone has the chance to become a Muslim by saying that Testimony of Faith and entering into the fold of Islam. They will all hear the Message of Islam and evidences of Islam first, and they will have until they die, until whether they're punished or not punished. And that is the definition of choice. But what's the problem? What we just established now, that people who go to Hellfire is through their own decision making, i.e. their own choice.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Fake \"Ex-Muslim\" Gets Examined Live On Stream! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=snbioso3vGg", ((692, "11:32–12:06"), (742, "12:22–13:03"), (818, "13:38–14:26"),), id: 712)
