#passage(("Our problem with Christians or with Christianity is to claim that there is more than one God. How do you claim more than one God? You attribute divinity (divinity means any type of deity) to Jesus. Whether you say he's equal, he's not equal, he's lesser, his son, his daughter, whatever term you want to give, there's only one God in every sense. Nothing else is God or has the nature of God, because God is one and uniquely one. Everybody else is a prophet of God.", "Prophet Muhammad is a humble servant and a slave of God. I'm a humble servant and a slave of God. He's a messenger, so he's better than me there, just like Moses is a messenger who's better than me there. However, he's also a servant of God. No human being is ever God. No human being is ever anywhere near the creator. And Jesus himself says that, by the way, and I'm going to give you now the evidences from this verses that Jesus isn't God and cannot be God.", "So, our problem when we say that Christians are not going to heaven is a few things. First, they believe in the trinity, so they believe there's more than one God. They attribute divinity to other than God, like I said, to Jesus, and they reject the last and final messenger of God, which is prophet Muhammad. Now, if I reject Moses, I go to hellfire in Islam. If I reject Jesus, I go to hellfire in Islam. Abraham, if I reject him, I go to hellfire. You cannot reject any of the messengers of God, because rejecting one is equal to rejecting all.", "So when we say that, that's what we mean. We mean that you have to worship one God alone, obey one God alone and believe in one God alone in every sense. Then you have to believe in all the messengers of God. Without these two things, you cannot have eternal life. And who said that? It was Jesus. Where did Jesus say that? John 17:3. If you read from verse one, it says he, Jesus, raises up his eyes up to heaven and he says, Father. So he's speaking to God the father, who you call God the father, who's the only God.", "Then in verse three he says, this is eternal life, which is what we're talking about, salvation. What is eternal life according to Jesus? Does he say, this is eternal life, that you believe in I died for your sins? No, he never says that. He says this is eternal life, to believe in you, the only true God. According to Jesus, there's only one true God, like I was telling you, and Jesus, who sent by the only true God. So you have to believe in God alone and his messenger.", "So at the time of Jesus, you cannot go to heaven without believing in only one true God, like Jesus says, and then to believe that he's a messenger. Today, when God sent another messenger, which is the future from this verse, you have to believe there's only one true God (again, same belief) and that person is a messenger who sent you, whoever that person is. If you lived at the time of Moses, it has to be Moses. If you lived at the time of Abraham, it has to be Abraham. God assigns to each people a prophet. Now in this time we have a prophet sent by God. You are not going to have eternal life, according to Jesus, if you do not believe in that messenger that was sent.", "This is how you attain eternal life: believing in one true monotheism, one true God, and in believing in the messenger that is sent to you by God. Without that, you're not going to attain salvation at all, according to the Bible and according to the Quran.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Passionate Christian Challenges Muslim On Jesus & Salvation! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X5mvbKQDRZI", ((1729, "28:49–29:15"), (1755, "29:15–29:37"), (1779, "29:39–30:06"), (1808, "30:08–30:44"), (1845, "30:45–31:21"), (1881, "31:21–31:54"), (1916, "31:56–32:09"),), id: 717)
