#passage(("We have something called Faith, \"Iman\", the faith in the heart. We believe that Iman, that Faith, increases with good deeds. So when you become Muslim and you start to pray (prayer every day for us, every day five times), you connect to Allah, your faith increases in God, when you start doing righteous acts, always having God in your mind.", "These deeds bring you closer to God, increase your faith, and ultimately you enter Paradise by the Mercy of God, because God sees you trying your best, you're doing good and you're increasing your faith.", "So when you accept Islam and you start practising and your faith increases, following the commands become easier, because you have a stronger faith. It is much easier for you to wear the Hijab, because many sisters accept Islam and it takes them gradually some time to wear the Hijab, not necessarily in the beginning. When you start incorporating Islam in your life and practising it step by step, then wearing the hijab does not become as difficult as you're perceiving it right now.", "So what I would say is not to worry about the Hijab right now; worry about the most important thing, which is dying upon not rejecting the Messenger of God, which is Prophet Muhammad, accepting Prophet Muhammedﷺ, following the commands of God as much as possible, which is all good commands for you: give charity, be good to your parents, be good to your neighbours, all of the commands, many of which you will be already practising. And then when you would be praying to Allahﷻ five times a day, getting closer to Him, then you yourself would want to wear the Hijab. And my advice to your husband is to leave you step-by-step.", "But the point is this: he's not accountable if he gives you advice. But he has to leave you step by step until you start practising Islam and then you are a little bit more into Islam, and then maybe he reminds you with the Hijab. If he reminds you, then there is no sin on him, because everyone is responsible for 