#passage(("The first thing is, what you've based your understanding upon is incorrect. If you base your understanding on something which the premises are not correct, then everything falls apart. And that's the problem. Islam's Message was never that you have good deeds and bad deeds and good deeds will qualify to go to paradise by themselves. This was never the Message of Islam. In fact, the Prophet Muhammadﷺ, we believe, is the best of human beings. Now, Prophet Muhammadﷺ, he said to us, “None of you will enter paradise with your deeds.” Now, that completely shatters the point.", "In the Hadith, in Saheeh alBukhari, because Prophet Muhammadﷺ doesn't speak in the Quran, unlike the Bible, where you have other people speaking other than God, like Mark speaking or Luke speaking, or John speaking. We have the Quran, strictly God's word. No one else speaks in the Quran; Prophet Muhammadﷺ does not speak there. So whatever Prophet Muhammadﷺ says is in the Hadith.", "There are many hadiths, but I'll give you one. Allah's Apostle said, “Do good deeds properly, sincerely and moderately, and know that your deeds will not make you enter Paradise, and the most beloved deed to Allahﷻ is that which is regular and consistent, even if it were a little.” This is (Bukhari:6464). Bukhari is very well known. There are other ones; the one I was saying was even different. The Prophetﷺ said, “None will enter Paradise.” They said to the Prophetﷺ, “Even you?” He said, “Even me, unless Allahﷻ gives me from His mercy, I'll never enter Paradise.” (Muslim:2816c)", "The people who enter Paradise need two things: they need to do good in their life, and Allahﷻ chooses them from His mercy to give them Paradise. These are two things. But they don't enter Paradise because of their deeds. They enter it because of the Mercy. Why? Because it doesn't matter what we do in our life, we can never thank Allah enough for the blessings that He's given us: my heart is beating with every breath I'm taking, every second; my eyesight.", "It's not selective. If I'm hiring (this example I give often), say, I want a secretary, and I say I'm only going to hire a woman. Does that mean any woman that will come, I'm going to hire her? No, I'm still going to look at the qualifications that I need in order for me to hire the woman. So, I can say I need a woman, but this is not whom I'm going to hire. That's one of the criteria. So, a criteria to enter Paradise is to be good. But you said that it is why you enter Paradise, and we do not believe that's why we enter Paradise. We enter Paradise because of Allahﷻ's mercy. And even the eyesight alone is more of a blessing than anything you can do in your life. So we don't think that good deeds are that which take you, but you have to do it.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Inquisitive Christian Learns About Islam P1! Muhammed Ali - Speakers Corner”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bJOB7cYkp-I", ((862, "14:22–15:14"), (917, "15:17–15:50"), (1009, "16:49–17:24"), (1064, "17:44–18:01"), (1089, "18:09–20:25"),), id: 727)
