#passage(("There's one more important thing I want to say about this idea of martyr, being a martyr. We as Muslims cannot know at all who is a martyr and who isn't a martyr. We cannot say, therefore, that this person died as a martyr, unless Allah tells us or the prophet tells us.", "There's a great example the [prophet] himself gave us. There was a person; in reality (by the way, a lot of people don't know this), he was a hypocrite, but people don't know, because hypocrisy is in the heart. You're pretending: you are in your heart a disbeliever, but you're showing belief. That person was with the companions. His name is irrelevant. He was one of the hypocrites in Medina. Even the narrations don't mention the name, because it doesn't matter. The idea is what matters. One of the scholars mention him.", "In the battle, he didn't go to fight. So people called him a woman: You're like women, sitting with the women. Why wouldn't you go fight? Because he was a hypocrite. He was afraid. Then one of the other battlefields, he went with the Muslims. Remember, he's a hypocrite, so people think he's a believer. And now we're talking about what? Fighting. Because everything happening today is in the idea of fighting: this guy is fighting for the sake of Allah, therefore he must be a shahid; this guy's fighting for the sake of Allah, he must be a good person.", "This person was doing the same thing. He went to the companions, but he was a hypocrite in his heart. He was slaying left and right. I'm talking about chopping left and right. The Sahabah, who are the most courageous people, they were saying, “Look at this person. Nobody today did like this person did.” Then the [prophet] said, “He's in the hellfire.” Everyone got confused: this person was with us on the battlefield. He was destroying everyone. Then said, “I will follow him.” He followed him. He saw he's killing 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, seven. But he got so many wounds in the battlefield. Then the pain was so strong that he got a weapon and he stabbed himself and he killed himself. He couldn't bear it. So he killed himself. Then that man came and reported to the Sahaba.", "If you kill yourself, you go to hellfire straight away in Islam. You're not allowed to do that under any condition. No matter what happens, you're not allowed to kill yourself. So he went and he did that. And then the prophet said that by Allah [I'm] the messenger of God. So he's telling him, this is the fulfillment of what I told you. You saw him. You thought this person is fighting disbelievers in the battlefield, he's slaying the enemies, therefore he's a holy person, a person who's going to go to paradise. But no.", "Then the prophet said that someone will live and he will be doing the work of the people of [Jannah]; people will think this person is a righteous person, in the eyes of the people. Then he will do the work of hellfire, and he will go to hellfire. And someone will be doing the work of hellfire in the eyes of the people; they think this guy is going to hellfire. But he will do the work of paradise in the end, and he will go to paradise.", "Prophet is teaching us you cannot judge. You cannot know what's in someone's heart. He could be in the battlefield destroying, killing, fighting the enemy, whatever. But what is in his heart only Allah knows. I'm not going to say this person is a martyr, this person is not a martyr. We can say we hope that he died as a martyr. It's not me and you who put people in paradise. I can say this guy is shahid, this guy, this guy, this guy. But I'm not going to put him in paradise in the end. Allah is the one who's going to put people in paradise. And Allah knows how he lived his life. Allah knows the history, the past, what this person did, and what he died upon in the end.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Sneako Questions The Muslim Lantern On Shia & Sunni Unity | The Iran War And More | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kdFNc6Jr6OQ", ((2092, "34:52–35:08"), (2110, "35:1