#passage(("There were people who were created and they never heard about the Quran or the Bible. In Islam there's a very simple response to that. There's a group of people in Islam called (Ahl alFatrah: People between Prophetic intervals); those are the people who the Message does not reach. They're not punish in the afterlife; they have a different test on the day of judgment.", "The same test that you have: a prophet will be sent to them, but on the day of judgment, and then if they obey that prophet, they will go to Paradise; if they don't, they go to Hellfire. The same idea that happened to you in this life will happen, but that will be delayed into the Afterlife. It's not going to be in this life, because the message did not reach them.", "But the people who need to look at what's going on are the people who the Message has reached, which is the overwhelming majority of people. In the past, when things were not globalized like internet and today, Allah sent to every nation a Messenger, but now Allah sent the last and final Messenger, which is Prophet Muhammadﷺ, and he brought this message because our time has become globalized. People can hear you. You're in France right now and I'm somewhere else in the world, and we're easily communicating right now. The reason we are able to do that and we're doing that is this globalization that we are in.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist Asks Muslim To Explain Why God Allows Suffering! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5-bfwhR0lSM", ((1479, "24:39–24:57"), (1504, "25:04–25:17"), (1520, "25:20–25:51"),), id: 761)
