#passage(("How does a deaf man hear God? Can he see? You can read through seeing. Why does he need to hear? You read with touching. A blind man can hear. One of the greatest scholars in modern times is called [Ibn Baz], and he couldn't see, but he accumulated all his knowledge through learning, listening.", "My answer is: if you cannot see, hear or access the truth, then that is why in Islam we have something called a different test on the day of judgment. You're not responsible in this life. You're only held accountable if you can access the truth.", "The afterlife is after you're resurrected. Then we have something called heaven, and then we have something called hellfire. And then you're eternally either in that place or this place.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “The Muslim Lantern, Sneako and Arab Debate Religion! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QiBVA3ZecoI", ((3215, "53:35–54:14"), (3261, "54:21–54:36"), (3302, "55:02–55:12"),), id: 762)
