#passage(("What is not correct is that we say that everyone knows the truth inherently. We don't say that.", "But what we say in Islam: you have something called the Fitrah, which is an innate thing. But this can only tell you that there is a Creator. You will know in your heart there is a Creator. 2nd thing, you will know basic good and bad. You will not know everything. That's why you require revelation in order to expound upon the things in life that are bad and the things in life that are good. So it's not everything.", "If an atheist is born in a country, is born in Amazon, and no one came to him with the Message of Islam, that person doesn't go to Hellfire. That person has a separate test on the Day of Judgment, because the Message did not reach him. Unlike Christianity, where you don't have that. In Christianity, there is not a single verse in the Bible which I have read that says if you have not heard the Message and you don't believe in Jesus, you're going to go to paradise. You still have to believe in Jesus. It doesn't matter whether the Message reached you or not.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Inquisitive Christian Learns About Islam P1! Muhammed Ali - Speakers Corner”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bJOB7cYkp-I", ((1281, "21:21–21:25"), (1311, "21:51–22:12"), (1332, "22:12–22:37"),), id: 763)
