#passage(("I would say this is something a lot of people think: if I were to tell someone the message of Islam, does that put them now at a point of disadvantage? If I would not tell them, would they end up better? No. And the reason why is because, if they were sincere and they were to accept the message, they would do in this life, and if they were not going to do it in this life, they're not going to do it in the afterlife. You've not really changed anything, and the punishment is in the afterlife anyways, so it's not like you hasten punishment, if in this life they reject.", "So if they reject in this life, they will also reject in the afterlife, and the reason being is that it's the same person. The person who will have the test on the Day of Judgment is the same person who will have the test in this life. Allah is not going to bring someone else to be tested on the Day of Judgment, or there'd be different [variables], or else it wouldn't be a fair test. It's the same test that you would have in this life, and this life is the same test that these people will have in the afterlife, as the same individual.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Compares Islam And Christianity! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Igzqbqr2Pew", ((949, "15:49–16:07"), (973, "16:13–16:33"),), id: 764)
