#passage(("Allah, one of his names is: he's the judge, the most just. He has these attributes and names for a reason. Allah says in the Quran: we will show them our signs within the horizon and within themselves until it's clear to them it's the truth. So he can live in India, can live under a rock, it doesn't matter: Allah can put opportunities and chances in front of you that you get the message somehow delivered to you.", "People now get to know Islam in the most random ways, especially in the age of internet. In the age of internet you can just come upon a video, a short, whatever. People think it's random. We don't believe in randomness: Allah has put a chance in front of you. Okay, here's the message. Then the person now will make the decision.", "You're not going to be more just than Allah. You're not going to have, okay, I figured out a problem, logical problem with Islam, there's a hole here. You're not going to do that, because Allah is the most just, and anything you can think about, Allah will already have an answer for it that you have not considered.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Doubtful Muslim Learns the Secret to Overcoming Doubts! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XG-z1myMY7I", ((666, "11:06–11:43"), (705, "11:45–12:06"), (732, "12:12–12:27"),), id: 767)
