#passage(("The Creator judges us based on our surroundings. So The Creator, Allahﷻ, tells us that: \"You'll only be held accountable for what your capacity can do\" (Albaqarah2:286). Allahﷻ does not ask you to be a superhero. So, for example, there are punishments in Islam. The punishment was suspended at the time of Umar because there was a famine and people were stealing, because they were stealing to survive. So there was no punishment for them, and there is no sin for them for doing that. So in these situations in which you're forced to do a specific thing, there is no longer harm on you. The Quran (Alanaam6:119) says: إِلَّا مَا اضْطُرِرْتُمْ إِلَيْهِ (except that which you have to do by necessity), then it's OK. So there are things that are not permissible, but if it's by necessity, if you have no choice, then there is no sin on you.", "But the person goes to Paradise or Hellfire based on him believing in a Creator or not. And him believing in a Creator: he's born knowing in his heart there has to be something that brought this universe into existence. If he then chooses to reject The Creator, this is how the person ends up in Hellfire. So Allahﷻ is completely just, but Allahﷻ will show you the signs. Like today, Allahﷻ has given you the message, answering your question, showing you the sign. But then it is your choice to accept the Truth and reject the Truth.", "So right now, is anyone forcing you not to accept Islam? Khalas! خلاص (that's it!), what is stopping you? We don't force Islam on anyone. We believe Islam is a valuable thing. You should want to be a Muslim, not me trying to force you to be. So this is our position: it's completely your choice.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Future Priest Attempts To Rescue A Christian Part1! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e7Uqvu7Sdjs", ((175, "2:55–3:29"), (213, "3:33–4:04"), (244, "4:04–4:26"),), id: 768)
