#passage(("The Muslims will end up going to Paradise. Allah quotes Jesus 'Alayhi salam (Peace be upon him) as saying: “Oh! My people, worship Allah alone. Whoever associates with Allah, then Jannah is Haram for him (Paradise is forbidden for him), وَمَاۡوٰٮهُ النَّارُ ؕ and his abide is Hellfire, وَمَا لِلظّٰلِمِيۡنَ مِنۡ اَنۡصَارٍ and they will not have any supporters (the wrongdoers)”. So it’s crystal clear in the Quran.", "People who did not get the Message delivered to them, those have a different test on the Day of Judgment, because not everyone necessarily heard the true Message of Islam. That's based on the Quran as well, chapter 17 of the Quran verse 15. Allah says: “We’re not going to punish a people, until we send them a Messenger”.", "But the point is marrying a Christian: yes, you marry a Christian, but you marry a Christian for what purpose? You marry a Christian for the purpose of trying to bring her closer to Islam, because the man is the leader in the relationship. The man is the leader in the marriage. Of course, Women generally follow the lead of the man. That's why women, it's not permissible for them to marry a non-Muslim man. So that is one of the purposes for an individual to marry. It's not for their beauty and all of what certain people do. It's not for that. So yes, you can marry her and call her to Islam, and no problem, Allah has allowed you to do that, and the children will listen to you. They will take your religion, as they do most of the time take the religion of the father.", "But none of that is related to you now! Taking that step and dying upon the Truth now. No religion will be accepted from you except Islam, and you have to testify with the Truth. You have to say the Shahada. Allah says (Quran43:86) إِلَّا مَن شَهِدَ بِالْحَقِّ وَهُمْ يَعْلَمُونَ “Except those who testify with the Truth knowingly\".", "So you have to testify with the Truth, u have to say what u believe in your heart; because the Deeds you're doing, I don't want them to go to waste, and I don't want you to say \"in the next year\" and you're not alive in the next month, and you're not alive in the month after the next month. Allahﷻ knows. But it has to come from you.", "If you are someone who do not know about Islam, I will not tell you to take the Shahada. But you're not only someone who knows about Islam, believes in the pillars of Islam; you're someone who's practicing the pillars of Islam every day. You're doing probably more than some Muslims. So it would not make any sense for you to be praying, be doing all of the [du'as], be believing in Allah, He's the Only True God, Jesus is only a Prophet of God, believe in the Quran, believe in everything, but not taking that step and saying \"OK, I'm going to do that next year\"! No!", "My advice is you do it for yourself, is to guarantee if you die, at least you died upon the Truth. And no one is saying don't go with your friends. Go, no problem, go again with your friends, if you want to do it again in a Masjid where people are around you. No problem, you can do that, but you have to do it before as well, if you know it's the Truth.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Sincere Man Realises The Contradictions In Christianity! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CR6_RG9qdVM", ((1404, "23:24–24:24"), (1487, "24:47–24:54"), (1499, "24:59–25:29"), (1536, "25:36–25:52"), (1556, "25:56–26:09"), (1569, "26:09–26:27"), (1596, "26:36–26:48"),), id: 773)
