#passage(("In our belief the Christians do not fulfil the condition. So, for example, the Christians would reject the Messenger of God, who we believe is Prophet Muhammad. We believe that Christians associate partners with God. The biggest sin you could do is to associate with God. So we would say that you cannot enter Paradise if you associate partners with God, because you worship other than God. And it's the same in the Bible; it says: \"do not take any other gods beside me\" (Exodus20:3; Deuteronomy5:7). The Old Testament is very clear: do not take any image, anything that you pray to other than me. So it is the same concept that we have: do not take anything other than God, make equal with God; this is the sin, the unforgivable sin, in Islam. Other sins can be forgiven: if you repent from this in this life, you're forgiven. But if you die associating partners with God, you cannot enter Paradise.", "And this is a similar belief: Paul says that you could only enter paradise by believing in Jesus Christ. The same concept is in other religions, and some people don't know that, but it's in Christianity and other religions as well. But Jews, for example, will believe we will enter Paradise but you won't. Something which might be surprising. Because they say we worship God Alone, we don't associate partners, and they would say you worship other than God. So, if you look at the Rabbis, they will say to you the Muslims will enter. That's why a Jew can pray in a Mosque, but they're not even allowed to enter a Church, let alone pray there.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Australian Couple Defend Their Beliefs! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cWb2t094YMc", ((1572, "26:12–26:49"), (1619, "26:59–27:22"),), id: 775)
