#passage(("A lot of people think that way. I'm not going to say to them they'll be okay. We cannot trick God. God knows everything in everyone. He's the one who will judge, and these rules, he's the one who put – can never outsmart God – and what we can do, what we cannot do.", "Understand one very, very important thing: our family members are not more dear to us than the family of the prophets. Abraham: his father was his enemy; he said to him, if you don't stop, I'm going to kill you. The uncle of the Prophet Muhammad, who protected him all his life, who was dying on his death bed, and the prophet was saying: just say the words, say the words, so I can use them as an excuse in day of judgment. And then the other say: die upon the religion of your forefathers. And he died that way.", "And I'll tell you something very important. That's not just for [reverts], that's for Muslims: many Muslims who have family members – don't pray, don't fast, don't do anything – and they will end up in Hellfire if they die that way. It's the same thing. There's always a level – this life is a test – always a level of advice that you can give, but then it ends there. You cannot do anything else.", "So always know that Allah is a merciful god, and he's more merciful than you. And if that person deserves guidance, They will receive guidance, and you never know: is that today, tomorrow, next year, next month? Nobody knows. Only Allah knows that.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim and Christian Sisters Enquire About Hellfire In Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7sdgLSIwzHQ", ((1635, "27:15–27:28"), (1650, "27:30–28:16"), (1696, "28:16–28:52"), (1745, "29:05–29:29"),), id: 783)
// U ML099:278-313 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("Prophet Muhammad told us that Allah is more Merciful to us than our own mothers. So, I'll ask you this question: would your mother throw you in the Hellfire? No, your mother is not going to throw you! I understand the arguments of self-preservation. Even if I were to say, \"Would a stranger throw you in the Hellfire?\", if he's a normal human being, decent human being, probably he wouldn't do it, because the minute you see Hellfire, it's an infinite eternal life. He wouldn't throw you there. And we're not more merciful than Allah! So, if Allah is more Merciful to us than our own mothers, and our own mother is not going to throw us in Hellfire, then we should have hope in the Mercy of Allah.", "Allah in the end is Loving and Just, and He wouldn't punish someone who doesn't deserve to be punished. And I'm saying this: if Allah puts my own family, whoever that family member is, in Hellfire, I will be content with it, because I know that Allah would not place that person except that he deserves to be there, whoever that person is.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Shockingly Describes Life After Death Like You Are Witnessing It! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lePF6KO1aZA", ((822, "13:42–14:36"), (902, "15:02–15:23"),), id: 784)
