#passage(("It's not something silly. We would NEVER call something like that \"silly\". It is very important. Everyone cares about their own family, and wants their family to be in a good place in the end. And what I can tell you is that there is no one more just than Allahﷻ. I'm not the judge. No one can ever guarantee you that a specific person is in paradise or hellfire. A part of the Islamic belief and creed is that we don't declare a specific individual to be in Hellfire or Heaven, except if Allahﷻ tells us, because nobody knows what's in someone's heart. Nobody knows what the person did before their death, in the last few minutes. Nobody knows what they came across, the amount of information they came across. Nobody knows any of these elements. Only Allahﷻ knows.", "All we can say is what Allahﷻ told us: generally, unless someone fully receives the Message and know deep down that it is the Truth, and then just say: \"I'm not going to accept the Message. I'm going to continue in disbelief\", \"even though I know that it is the Truth\", and then died, this someone is going to go to the Hellfire. But who fully received the Message? Who rejected it out of arrogance and died upon Rejection? NONE of us knows! So, the answer to your question is that the only one who knows this is Allah, because He's the Judge. Allah knows what we have, what we conceal in our hearts, what we think at every moment, and even each decision we take.", "The Prophet Muhammadﷺ wanted to go and seek forgiveness for his mother, the same thing that you're saying, and Allah forbade him from doing it. Unless someone, in our eyes (which doesn't always have to be the case) and in our perception, unless they die on Islam, then there are certain rulings that we cannot apply to them. Like I said, that doesn't mean that this person is necessarily in Hellfire or Heaven. But when it comes to the practises of Islam, unless we know for certainty they died upon Islam, we are NOT allowed to do that. We are not allowed to seek forgiveness for them, for example; one of the things we are not allowed to do. Allah tells us that in the Quran (atTawba9:113).", "So, like I told you, you're asking God to forgive her. That's what a prayer is. But I'm telling you that God is more Merciful than you and me. If there is any chance that she is forgiven, Allah will forgive her even without you saying it, because Allah told us that (He's more Merciful to us than our own mothers).", "And Allahﷻ said that He created a hundred different Mercies, 100 ones, and He sent only ONE here in this life. And this one, out of 99 that He created, is what all of the Creation is using to be merciful with one another. All of the mercy that we show to each other, that mothers and fathers show to their children, animals: all of this is ONE of those Mercies. And Allahﷻ kept and maintained 99 of those for the Day of Judgement, because it will be a SEVERE Day. So when it comes to mercy, you can't even comprehend Allah's Mercy.", "So, don't worry. Allah is a Merciful Creator. And what's important is that we do what we can, and we have good assumptions about Allah. Allahﷻ tells us: أَنَا عِنْدَ ظَنِّ عَبْدِي بِي. It's hard to translate this, but it means that if you think good of Allah, Allah will be as you think of Him. If you think badly of Allahﷻ, then it will be bad for you.", "Allahﷻ is the only God and Muhammadﷺ is His Messenger: that's what the Shahada is. The Shahada doesn't need to be said in the Arabic language, by the way. It's good to say it, but it doesn't have to. So, saying it in your language, as long as you believe in its meaning, that's what the Shahada is.", "That's why I'm telling you, none of us can judge. This is the thing: someone might say, oh, she died as a Catholic. But in the end, in her heart, she believed Prophet Muhammadﷺ was a Messenger, that there is only One God; she didn't believe that Jesus was another God. So, essentially, she believed what Muslims believe. \"Catholic\" is just a name. It's just a thing that people say. But in reality, her beliefs are not in accordance with that. When you go to Christians today, they don't believe in that. They don't believe that Prophet Muhammadﷺ is a Messenger of God and that there is One God only. Nobody knows this person is ending here or there, because nobody knows what they really died upon. But this, what you said, should give you a lot of hope towards her position. It would make me personally very hopeful that this is the case, that she was saying that.", "Prophet Muhammadﷺ was trying to get his own uncle to just say these words! That's it! Say that there's only Allah worthy of worship and that I'm His Messenger. Just say them. And he didn't say them! But your mother was telling you to say them every day. SubhanAllah (Glorified is God).",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Emotional Shahada | Peruvian Sister Discovers The Truth Of Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PZDTz4a-nZA", ((741, "12:21–13:15"), (805, "13:25–14:00"), (859, "14:19–14:59"), (903, "15:03–15:25"), (931, "15:31–16:08"), (972, "16:12–16:35"), (1040, "17:20–17:45"), (1070, "17:50–18:39"), (1126, "18:46–19:02"),), id: 785)
