#passage(("They have to be Muslim, because intercession, which is what you're referring to, has three conditions. First, that Allah is pleased with you; then Allah is pleased with the person you are going to do intercession for, so he has to be a Muslim. And Allah says in the Quran about these: the intercession is not going to benefit them, the disbelievers. Because if I die disbelieving in God, I deny God or I associate partners with him, I cannot expect something from God in the afterlife, or there's no difference between a Believer and disbeliever. Why do I have to be a Muslim?", "The thing is, if this was the case, why would Allah address the people of the book and say: oh the people of the book, Come To Worship in one God; oh people of the book, do not transgress in your religions? People of the book: Allah is talking to them because what they're doing is wrong. If what doing is okay, would make no sense for Allah to talk to them. Allah would say: okay, be the way you are.", "And I understand, what I'm telling you might be difficult; the idea itself may be difficult. It's nice to think that everyone will be okay, but this life is a test, and we're not the judge. Allah is the judge, and the Allah is a just God, so he will always make a differentiation between the person who does his best and obeys him and the person who doesn't obey him. Allah cannot make them equal.", "Remember, what you ask for does not transgress to other people. What I ask for, for me, I will get, but that's me; my asking cannot transgress to other people. Let me give you a hypothetical example: I go to paradise and I say, I'm not happy until everyone in Hell Fire is in paradise. It make no sense that God will put everyone in. What we can demand is us. You cannot transgress against God. God has put conditions and rules, because he's just.", "Prophet Muhammad said something very beautiful. He said: everyone will enter Paradise except those who refuse. Then the companion said: who would refuse