#passage(("Why do you have a negative connotation when you hear the word command? I get commanded by God. You get commanded by the law, by this police officer. He's like, do this, and you get commanded and you follow. Why you not commanded from God, when you follow another human being like yourself, and you bow your head if he tells you bow your head; get on the floor, you get on the floor? So why is the problem to obey the creator, his command, when I can obey another human being just because he has a weapon? God doesn't need a weapon, cuz he's the all powerful. He can take your life if he wanted, right now, in this moment, as we speak. So he's more powerful than this police officer. So he's more worthy of being obeyed.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Buddhist Gets Defensive After A Muslim Highlights The Problems With Buddhism! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cCyN0gL4kEI", ((2461, "41:01–41:43"),), id: 794)
