#passage(("Do you speak the language of birds? Do you speak the language of ants? Spiders? Tigers? You understand how they hunt from National Geographic, but that's not what I'm asking. I'm asking: do you speak the language? So how can you know, as you just stated, that they don't worship anything?", "I'll mention to you an observation that I saw personally. First, I'll mention to you a verse of The Quran. Allahﷻ says in (The Quran17:44) وَإِن مِّن شَيْءٍ إِلَّا يُسَبِّحُ بِحَمْدِهِ. And وَإِن مِّن شَيْء here, in The Arabic Language, it includes EVERYONE. So literally, if you want to translate it: (and there isn't ANYTHING except that glorifies Him) وَلَٰكِن لَّا تَفْقَهُونَ تَسْبِيحَهُمْ (but you do not understand, comprehend their ways of praising Allah, worshipping Allah) Etc. So all of these things that you mentioned, all of these ants, animals, insects Etc.: everything glorifies Allah in its own way, in the way that Allah created it to glorify Him in. We, as humans, we do not speak that language of these animals, so it would make perfect sense that we don't understand how these animals worship.", "Now the observation I wanted to mention, which is this, the following: there is a specific time which is after Dawn, from Dawn Prayer until Sunrise, and just the time before Sunset, the one or two hours before Sunset. These two periods of time, in Islam we have certain prescribed Reminders that we say. We call them Day and Night Reminders (Adhkar AsSabah wal Massa'), which are certain supplications that we say in these two times of the day, that the Prophetﷺ used to say. So the Prophet taught us when these two times come, there are certain reminders that you say, certain supplications, certain things that you say to glorify and worship Allah.", "The observation that I found is that birds are always making noise in these two times of the day. You want to call it singing or whatever term you want to use, but specifically these two times of the day, you will hear them making the most. That is an observation that I've seen, because when I used to go to The Mosque and walk to The Mosque and come back from The Mosque in these specific times, I always heard them singing in these specific time. And if I go to the prayer and the Mosque in the other times of the day, they're not making noise! But they are making noise, they're singing, they're making that noise specifically in these times, which are prescribed times for us to glorify Allahﷻ.", "The point I want to make is this: you have no idea what these animals are doing, because you do not speak the language. So you cannot then come and say that animals do not glorify Allah. I would say them following the Laws that Allah has prescribed for them – what people call the Laws of Nature; there's no such thing as \"Nature\", it's just taking God from the equation and replacing it with a word, calling it \"Nature\" – so the Laws of Allah, that Allah has created this creation with, I would say, it's just them following that Law of Allah, is worship to Allah, because it's submission to His Laws. And a \"Muslim\" by definition is someone who submits his will to The Creator, which is Allahﷻ.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Why Does God Not Communicate With Humans? Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1c92faSXNec", ((73, "1:13–1:35"), (95, "1:35–2:18"), (143, "2:23–2:51"), (179, "2:59–3:30"), (217, "3:37–4:05"),), id: 795)
