#passage(("You see this individual, and you see how ridiculous these claims are. He's going to completely ignore what is the meaning of the word Allah Akbar, and he's going to pretend as if this has no meaning. And he's going to go on to say: oh, you don't see this and you don't see that. What does the word even mean? It means God is Greater. God is greater than everything, God is greater than anything. That's essentially what it means.", "And he's here saying you never hear that word and see something peaceful. This is clear evidence that you have no clue about Muslims. You've got no idea what these people do. Every day, Muslims pray five times, and during each prayer, from each movement, they move from one to the other movement, they say that word Allahu Akbar. Whenever there is a call of prayer, and there's always five calls of prayers during the day in each mosque, you repeatedly hear this word as a Muslim, because it means God is Greater.", "So this is what the word means, and you hear it every day almost as a Muslim, and anyone who's been around any Muslims, or been in any Muslim countries, would hear it every day, and he's not going to see any of this nonsense that this guy is saying. This just shows us how much illiterate these people are when it comes to the teachings of Islam.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Responding To @PBDPodcast Absurd Comments On The Bishop Incident! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=je-cOqAbR8c", ((425, "7:05–7:24"), (449, "7:29–7:55"), (479, "7:59–8:12"),), id: 796)

