#passage(("If we pray five times a day or we pray towards the direction of Meca, how does that correlate with the attributes of God?", "Because God commands us to pray as an act of worship first, meaning it's a form of submission; it's not [related] to that, the knowledge of God. Number one. Number two, it is because it's good for us. So it does not benefit God that we pray. But why do we pray? Prayer is for us. So if prayer is beneficial for us, then we will do it five times a day. You're thinking of it as it is a benefit for God, which is not.", "We have a soul; we don't just have the bodies. I have a body; I can feed the body food, but the soul also requires nourishment. And that's why a lot of people have a lot of money but they are the most miserable people on Earth. Richest people commit suicide all the time, because materialistic things do not give you fulfillment internally.", "We say that prayer is a connection between us and God. So first, it gives us this fulfillment, number one. Number two, it reminds us of God. So when we're living our lives, we get reminders; we do not commit evil deeds, because this life is a test. And there's many, of course, other things as well: gives us relief from all of the tiredness that we have in life. We just focusing between us and God, the conversation that you have with the most beloved to you, which is the [Creator]. So there's many things that we do for ourselves. So these prayers, we don't look at them as a burden.", "If God is the one who commands you how to pray, then prayer has to be done in the way that he likes. Like if you buy a gift for your friend, you buy a gift that he likes, or the gift that you like? If we're going to pray to the Creator, we have to [pray] to the Creator the way that he likes, He commands us, because it's a form of submission; not the way that we determine. We start innovating: one guy says, I'm going to do this at the prayer. We say okay, then everyone will do his own thing and we refer to it as a prayer. But the one who determines how he would like you pray to him is the one who asks you to pray to him to begin with, which is the creator.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Man Grills Muslim With Difficult Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-rSkeAMTyK0", ((8, "0:08–0:14"), (31, "0:31–1:06"), (70, "1:10–1:29"), (89, "1:29–2:01"), (141, "2:21–2:51"),), id: 797)
