#passage(("There is many commandments of Allah that we would say are ta'abbudi, are done as an act of worship. For example, if the prayer were 10, someone would say, why are they 10? If they were seven, they'd say, why are they seven?", "The prayers in the beginning were actually commanded as 50. And then Prophet Muhammad, when he went in the night journey, he went up to the heaven. He went up and he had a discussion with one of the prophets, Moses, and then he told him that: I experienced people. I've been a prophet. They're not going to handle 50 prayers. It's too much. So go back to your Lord. So he went to Allah, and then Allah decrease the prayers. He keeps going back. Moses: no, keep going back. Until they were five, and Moses: no, that's too much. But the prophet said, I feel shy now, I went so many times to Allah. So then it was five prayers ordained upon us to pray.", "The number itself, we're not told anything significant to do with the number. It's a command that Allah commands us to do.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “New Convert Questions Muslim On Lack Of Connection With God In Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pwUuzBBM4o8", ((203, "3:23–3:32"), (217, "3:37–4:17"), (265, "4:25–4:32"),), id: 798)
// U ML091:334-424 | The Muslim Lantern | 7
#passage(("Now, what do we benefit from prayer? There's many things that we can highlight. We can see many wisdoms as human beings looking at the prayer times. What does it teach us? It teaches us many things. First, it teaches us discipline, consistency, remaining upon doing the same thing and sticking to doing that thing. What do most humans lack? That is what most humans lack. That's what makes most humans not succeed in life. What makes a good business, what makes a successful person, is his consistency, is his discipline.", "Now you connect with God. So it teaches you that you need to dedicate a time in your day and in your life to God. Not everything is just about the world, but there are times and instances that should be given to the Creator, and within that time, it's only for God. When we enter the Mosque, we leave the worldly life there, outside, before entering the mosque. And when we pray, then we just focus on that Creator alone; we connect with Him.", "Now you say, \"whenever I remember to thank God\", but this world is full of distractions! That's why this world exists. That's why you need reminders. When you want to do something important, you put reminders on your phone. You don't just say, \"if I remember that important thing\". No! You need reminders. As a human being, you forget, you're forgetful. Not only are you forgetful, but this world is full of distractions. You start getting distracted with music, you start getting distracted with parties, you start getting distracted with women, with food, with money, with everything, and you forget God! And that's the reality of the most people upon the earth. And without a constant reminder that brings you back to the Creator, you cannot have that.", "Go look at the studies for people, for instance, who pray, and their mental health and mental well-being, versus people who don't; religious people versus people who aren't. And you will see that it's your own benefit, because you take that time to focus on something spiritual, on God, not just worldly materialistic aspects of life that gives you anxiety and pain, but things that even help you. Even in the prayer, if you look at the least amount of things, you do physical movements. These are by definition helping your body, helping you stay in a functioning state, not just sitting in your mother's basement, 24-7, gaining weight or something.", "Now, the prayer is done where? Prayer is done in a mosque. So what happens in a mosque? You go and you stand. You stand next to the person, and the Prophet told us: \"Your feet next to the feet, your shoulder next to the shoulder.\" Now, that person might be black, that person might be white, that person might be Chinese, that person might be from any place.", "Now, that's what the prayer does. It removes anything. It doesn't matter if you're Bill Gates, it doesn't matter if you're Elon Musk, you will stand next to the person who is the janitor of the house, the cleaner. You're not going to say: that person is not clean enough. You're going to stand next to them, you put shoulder to shoulder and feet to feet, and you will learn to humble yourself and put your face on the floor and humble yourself in front of The Creator as a form of submission.", "And the person who will lead the prayer is not the most rich person! It's not the most educated person! It is the person who is most pious and memorises most of God's Words and practices most. That's the person who's going to lead the prayer. He's better than you in the eyes of God, and you're going to learn that. Also, the community sense. You have your own community; you get to know people, your brothers and sisters in the Faith. I can give you a never ending list of the benefits of prayer.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Omnist Left Speechless After Hearing This Muslim's Answer! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yVHQD2W5S0c", ((1294, "21:34–22:13"), (1350, "22:30–22:50"), (1374, "22:54–23:30"), (1414, "23:34–24:06"), (1450, "24:10–24:27"), (1471, "24:31–25:12"), (1515, "25:15–25:36"),), id: 799)
