#passage(("If this is the Truth, then it has objective morality, which would mean that whatever it says, it is good for us. If Allah says do this, or don't eat from that specific thing, don't drink from the specific thing, this is how I want you to pray, because prayer is good for you. Allah says in Quran39:7 فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ غَنِىٌّ عَنكُمْ ۖ Allah is free from you. He doesn't need anything from you!", "When we pray (you know people that meditate) we don't meditate. We pray because our prayer is a connection to our Lord. We don't have anxiety, we don't have depression; we have the lowest rates of depression in our countries, lowest rates of anxiety. Why? Because you're connected to God all the time, five times a day.", "We have certain set prayers over the day. The times change depending on the movement of the sun, the time of the day, because time changes. So those prayers, the units are repeated; for example, a prayer has two units, but what you recite in the prayer is your choice. So you recite chapter one and then you can decide any part of the Quran that you like, that you desire. During the prayer you can ask God anything you like in different prayers. So it's not like the same prayer would really be 100% identical to another prayer in any time.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Polish Student Amazed By Islamic Teachings! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pf1BQGnAXZc", ((673, "11:13–11:36"), (701, "11:41–11:55"), (727, "12:07–12:38"),), id: 800)
