#passage(("The most important act in Islam is Prayer. There is nothing more important for a Muslim to do than to pray 5 times a day. Why? Because the word prayer in Arabic language is the word صلاة. Salah comes from the Arabic word “صلة”, which means \"to connect\". So our prayer is our daily dose of connection with God every day. So if you're separated from the prayer, you're separated from connecting with the Creator, you're separated from connecting with Allah! That's why it's an essential part of our life as Muslims. For you to be a Muslim, you need to be practicing that in your life by praying five times a day.", "I don't like to use the English word to say \"the prayer\", i.e. \"A Muslim Prayer\", to describe a Muslim prayer. Why? Because the English word \"prayer\" just really means asking God for something. Most people, when you say prayer in English, they think [raising] your hand, or asking God for something. In Islam prayer is much more than that; it's not just raising your hand and asking God for something. There's much more to the prayer as a Muslim: there's physical acts that you do, there's a lot of meaning behind it, and how it was legislated for Muslims.", "So prayer can teach you so many things as a human being. For example, a prayer will teach you to be someone who values commitment, someone who's punctual, who's in time. Why? Because the daily prayers have a specific time that you need to pray in. You can not delay after that time. You have to pray in the time, when the prayer time comes. So it teaches you to be punctual, because if you miss the prayer time you're sinning! So you need to be there in your appointments when the time comes; you have to be there.", "It teaches you to tame yourself, it teaches you to have discipline, when you wake up in the morning, because one of our prayers are at dawn. We pray at dawn, the time of dawn; we pray a prayer called فجر. Fajr Prayer literally means dawn. So the Fajr prayer is at the time of dawn, so it's early in the morning, depending on the sun, when dawn is. But now it's 4:30a.m, 4:20, 4:10, something like that. So you wake up at that time to pray, so it teaches you discipline: to put God first in your life! Sleeping is very beautiful! I like sleeping! But God comes first!", "That's why the call of prayer that we do in Fajr time is very unique. It has an extra thing; it says الصلاة خير من النوم (Prayer is better than sleeping). This part is only in the Fajr time, because that prayer is a prayer that teaches you discipline.", "Also, the prayer teaches you to completely eliminate racism, and that's something that many religions struggle with! In certain Churches you find the Irish Church, black Church, White Church, African Church. In Islam everyone prays in the same Mosque! And when you pray, you have your feet next to other person's feet, and your shoulder next to the other person's shoulder. So you cannot be looking at that person with any type of racism, that he's less than you. You have to stand with him for 5 times a day; you have to meet that individual, you speak to him, and he speaks to him. You say سلام (which is greetings of peace to one another). So [it] completely eliminates racism.", "That's why you will find the people who struggled a lot with racism, for example, Malcolm X, or Muhammad Ali Clay the boxer. So those people struggled with racism back then, because it was very prevalent in America and many other places, and they became Muslims. And if you read the book of Malcolm X, he said, when he went to pilgrimage, he saw that the only religion that is eliminating racism is Islam! He said it was the only place where he felt that everyone is the same! Everyone is wearing the same clothes, everyone is doing the same action; there's no difference between you based on your color and your race.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Non-Muslim Audience Asks Muslim Difficult Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=imKsFyzx-Yo", ((991, "16:31–17:04"), (1029, "17:09–17:34"), (1057, "17:37–18:01"), (1092, "18:12–18:41"), (1128, "18:48–19:09"), (1149, "19:09–19:46"), (1186, "19:46–20:18"),), id: 801)
// U ML369:307-334 | The Muslim Lantern | 3
#passage(("How to pray, it has to be taught person to person. I have to show you what to say, the acts of ablution, or a video at least, and you have to look at it. But even from a video you probably might make mistakes here and there. So probably you would need a mentor, in a way, to show you exactly what is the right acts to do this and that. So it's a gradual step.", "But that is the thing: a person becomes a Muslim and he focuses on two things: he reads the Quran, or continues to read the Quran, and in the same time he learns how to pray. That's the beginning. Once you do that, then we will move you to the second stage. But this is the most important thing. You don't go astray, because the Quran says that the prayer forbids you from evil deeds and actions. Why? Because I have a five day reminder from God: fear God, ask God to guide you. Because in every prayer you recite the Quran, you ask Allah to guide you, you ask Allah not to have anger on you and not to make you from the misguided people.", "So when you do that on a daily basis, you are not going to finish that and go do something bad, because just two minutes ago you were speaking to God.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “If You Answer My QUESTIONS I will Accept Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=C2LVHjA4HbM", ((926, "15:26–15:53"), (953, "15:53–16:30"), (993, "16:33"),), id: 802)
// U ML079:252-275 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("The Christians remember God when it benefits them. I'm not going to say everyone, but we say the majority. They go: Christmas! Let's celebrate! This is what they want to remember God: eating and drinking and celebrating! The church is empty. No one is praying, no one is going there.", "If you want to really have a true relationship with God, you remember God five times a day at least. Minimum! This is the minimum requirement. But a lot of people think Muslims only pray five times a day. You can pray more! It's not the only thing that you do in your day to remember God. And when you pray, you say God is greater than everything. You think about Allah, you think about The Creator. This is the best connection! You speak with God in your prayer. Nobody has a closer relationship to God than Muslims. Anyone who tells you other than that has no clue what Islam is about.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “This Christian Came To Convert Muslim But He Didn't Expect This! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MGZ5L15SzXk", ((804, "13:24–13:40"), (824, "13:44–14:18"),), id: 803)
