#passage(("If Allah created you, and he's given you everything, he has a right over you; he deserves gratitude. You might go to a coffee shop and someone gives you a free coffee without asking. What are you going to say? Thank you. So when you say thank you, do they need thank you? Will it make them taller, more Rich? No. But you believe they deserve gratitude for what they have given you, because it's a gift.", "Now, who's [given] you everything that you have? Who's [given] you your hands? Allah, the Creator, God. Now, what kind of gratitude that Allah deserves? Maximal gratitude that you can never repay. Because every minute you're breathing, and every minute you [need] to thank him for giving you that; and every minute you see something, every minute you're able to smell: all of these blessings that the creator has given you, that you can never fully repay. And therefore we're indebted to God from the minute we're born till the minute we die.", "And that's why we believe in Islam nobody deserves Paradise, but Allah gives it to you out of his Mercy. Nobody deserves it, even The Messengers of God. Prophet Muhammad, he said nobody will enter [Paradise] with his deeds. He said: even you, oh prophet of Allah? He said: even me, except that Allah showers me with his mercy. So everyone in Islam enters Paradise with the mercy of God. But the bare minimum requirement is that you do as much as you can. You're never going to be perfect, but you have to do as much as you can.", "So the most important thing in gratitude is praying to God: the prayer, which is a form of gratitude. You thank the Creator, because the first thing we say, and which is the first chapter of the Quran, we say alhamdulillah, all praise and gratitude is due to Allah, the lord of the worlds. It's the first thing we would be reciting. So it's us showing gratitude daily to the Creator who created us. So Allah would require these things of you as a Muslim to do, and these things will be for your benefit yourself, and you'll be rewarded for in the afterlife.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Sincere Lady About To Accept Islam But This Happens! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V2bQy_K4u5g", ((474, "7:54–8:22"), (502, "8:22–8:49"), (529, "8:49–9:19"), (559, "9:19–9:56"),), id: 804)

