// U ML293:23-48 | The Muslim Lantern | 3
#passage(("Prayer is very easy; it's not difficult for anyone, because 80% of the Muslims in the world are not Arabs, and they all, ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّٰهِ (Alhamdulillah: Praise is due to God), pray in Arabic.", "Chapter one is the most important thing to memorise, which is seven verses, very small. And then you have certain very small chapters which are one line, that you can memorise as well. Then, some things that you'll be saying during the prayer, which is very easy: you'll be saying سُبْحَانَ ٱللَّٰهِ (SubhanAllah: Glory be to God), سُبْحَانَ رَبِّيَ الأَعْلَى (Glory is to my Lord, the Most High), سُبْحَانَ رَبِّيَ الْعَظِيمِ (Glory is to my Lord, the Greatest), these type of things: one statement, one word that you will be repeating in certain parts of the prayer.", "Once people become Muslim, it doesn't take them a long time to learn how to pray, because even in the beginning, you're allowed to pray by just repeating one word or one statement, just praising and glorifying Allah while you learn. So it's not like when someone becomes Muslim, straight away, now, he has to pray exactly. No, it's a step by step process, and you're rewarded every step of the way by learning how to pray by Allah.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Asks God For A Sign Then This Happens! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HhJvhr8ihyY", ((99, "1:39–1:45"), (110, "1:50–2:11"), (140, "2:20–2:34"),), id: 809)
// U ML319:204-264 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("It's one of the Wisdoms we can see: us reading the Quran is a way to preserve the Quran. It's a way for us to keep the Quran: the preservation of the Quran, not everyone reading it, doing it his own way and then perhaps polluting and changing the words of the Quran, the preserved Words of the Creator.", "But not only that: if I'm reading in a different language, it's no longer the Quran. So when I'm praying, I'm not reading the Miraculous Words of God; I'm reading an understanding in a different language of the Miraculous Word of God. It WILL be slightly different. The richness of the Arabic language is above any other language. So it will never preserve or contain all the meaning when you're reading in a different one; you will miss some of the meaning if you're reading in a different language.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Sincere Romanian Asks Questions About Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eixflyogKg4", ((776, "12:56–13:29"), (809, "13:29–14:01"),), id: 810)
// U ML254:38-110 | The Muslim Lantern | 5
#passage(("It's a House of God, just like the Christians have a church and the Jews have a synagogue, etc., so I'm bringing the idea closer. But of course, the Ka’ba is not a church.", "There was a previous Qibla (Direction of Prayer) before the Ka’ba. It was the Mosque in Jerusalem first; that was the first Qibla that was made, and the Quran mentions that in chapter:2 (Albaqara2:142), for example, onwards. It says: سَيَقُولُ ٱلسُّفَهَآءُ مِنَ ٱلنَّاسِ مَا وَلَّىٰهُمْ عَن قِبْلَتِهِمُ ٱلَّتِى كَانُوا۟ عَلَيْهَا (The ignorant from the people will ask \"What made them change the Direction of Prayer?\") So there was the first Direction of Prayer, and then Allah changed the Direction of the Prayer, and that first Direction of the Prayer was a test that Allahﷻ was making for the people, which is mentioned in these verses of the Quran if you read them onwards.", "Allahﷻ is testing the people, because that Direction of Prayer is the same Direction of Prayer for previous People of the Book: the Christians or the Jews specifically. They were directing themselves towards Jerusalem, so Allahﷻ made that as a test, as well, for the Believers: to make the same Direction of Prayer and to see what kind of reaction the Believers would have towards the Prophetﷺ making the same command to direct yourself to the same Direction of the Prayer as the Jews, for example. Then, Allahﷻ changed the Direction of Prayer towards Almasjid Alharam (in Mecca;The Ka’ba).", "I didn't say it started with Abraham, then to Jerusalem, then back to the Ka’ba. Scholars have a disagreement about whether the Ka’ba was first built by Adam, and then rebuilt on the foundations by Abraham, or if it was first built by Abraham; and I’m inclined to the position that it was first built by Adam and then rebuilt by Abraham, because the Quran says that he was raising the foundation (Albaqara2:127), so there were already foundations of the house existing that he was raising. That is one way to look at it.", "Now, regarding the change of direction: when the Prophetﷺ came to the people, the first direction was Jerusalem. We're not saying it was the house, then it was Jerusalem. No! Not everyone was praying everywhere at the beginning of Islam and then the Ka’ba was introduced. No, there was a Direction of Prayer, and then that Direction of Prayer was changed into a different direction.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic \"Confused\" By Simple Islamic Concepts?! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OLmq6y3PiVo", ((126, "2:06–2:12"), (159, "2:39–3:09"), (193, "3:13–3:43"), (260, "4:20–4:51"), (291, "4:51–5:25"),), id: 811)
