#passage(("So Fajr: the thing is, it's a sin, and it does not mean that someone is not going to be a Muslim, because there are many Muslims, sadly, who don't wake up. But do you have to wake up from an Islam point of view? Yes. Is it a big sin? Yes. So Allah says in the Quran (anNisa4:103) that the prayers are كِتَـٰبًۭا مَّوْقُوتًۭا (Set appointed times for the prayers). There is a benefit for you as an individual in obedience, of course in your afterlife without a shadow of a doubt, but even in this life, in following the commands of Allah ﷻ. Also there's a huge level of discipline within it. There's a huge level of obedience; there's a huge thing that would give you virtue over many other people that are praying while you are waking up.", "There are virtues given specifically to these prayers. Like the Prophet ﷺ says, \"The hypocrites, the two most difficult prayers for them are the late-Night prayer and the Morning prayer\", which is Fajr. The Prophet said that if you pray these two prayers in congregation, it's as if you stood the whole night praying.", "Allah says in the Quran (alisra17:78), إِنَّ قُرْءَانَ ٱلْفَجْرِ كَانَ مَشْهُودًۭا The Quran that you recite at that time of dawn is witnessed by the angels. There's so many things that are given as virtue specifically for these prayers, because they are, of course, a bit more difficult to do, specifically the prayer of Fajr, than other ones, due to its time. And you will see, it becomes a part of someone's habit when he does it.", "But the thing I always say to the people: imagine I say to you, I'm going to give you 10,000€ if you wake up every day at a specific time. I guarantee that not just you but everyone will, exactly at that specific time of the day, wake up to take that money. They will put it as a priority. So why can we not have God as our priority, when He is commanding us to do something beneficial for us, more beneficial than the money that we wake up for? And we would rather put the money first over Allahﷻ.", "I'm going to bring a pool of Muslims and I’m going to say, “You guys are going to do this social experiment. If you give me proof, you call me on that day at the time of Fajr, I'll give you 10,000”, you'll see how many people will. But for the prayer, how many people will do it? Sadly not most people are doing it.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Compares Islam And Christianity! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Igzqbqr2Pew", ((699, "11:39–12:27"), (750, "12:30–12:47"), (770, "12:50–13:20"), (805, "13:25–13:51"), (844, "14:04–14:20"),), id: 813)
