// U ML289:537-586 | The Muslim Lantern | 5
#passage(("If someone sleeps, the Prophetﷺ, he said: مَنْ نامَ عَنْ صَلاةٍ أو نَسِيَها فَلْيُصَلِّها إِذا ذَكَرَها (whoever sleeps on a prayer or forgets about it, he prays it whenever he remembers it). So the minute you remember, you pray. The Prophetﷺ made the exceptions there; these are the exceptions: you forget about the prayer, or you sleep and you miss the prayer.", "But there is a condition there in the sleeping. The condition in the sleeping is that you're putting effort to wake up, meaning I'm trying to sleep as early as I can. I know my schedule, I know what works with me. Find someone sleeping 30 minutes before the prayer: that person is sinning 100%, because he waited all that time, and that 30 minutes he slept instead of praying. So it doesn't work there. The condition for you to not be held accountable is that you try your best. You sleep as early as you can, you leave the alarm; if you know someone who can wake you up, you tell them to wake you up; you're taking all the means. If you did that, Allah knows your intention.", "It happens with everyone. Of course I miss the prayer sometimes, and the reason being, for example, let's say I'm travelling. I travel to a different country, the plane was six hours, and then I reach there towards 12 o'clock, and فجر (Fajr: the morning prayer) is 4 o'clock. So it's not like I slept late, but I came from the travel and I slept, and I was so tired that I could not stay awake for four more hours. But due to the tiredness, even though I put the alarm and try my best, I couldn't wake up, because I was so tired; I missed that prayer. So then, I pray it when I wake up.", "The Prophetﷺ himself, he missed a prayer, so let alone everyone else. The Prophetﷺ was with his Companions, and it was also the morning prayer, and they were travelling, and on the way, they put one person to stay awake, one of the Companions of the Prophetﷺ. The Prophet said, you stay awake and wake us up. And the rest of the people went to sleep. That person who was supposed to stay awake, he slept; he couldn't stay awake as he was told. So he slept, and everyone also continued to sleep, and the Prophetﷺ. Because they are travelling, they were very tired; they only woke up from the heat of the sun. The sun is now burning, it's too hot, so they wake up.", "And then the Prophetﷺ prayed that prayer with everyone, that they missed, and he didn't say anything, because he knows that person was tired in the travel, and all of that, and he tried to stay awake but he slept. So we're all human. No one is perfect. Don't think that there would be me or someone who's a record of perfect score.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Popular Youtuber Asks Muslim Difficult Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S7bA8bsNs20", ((1961, "32:41–32:58"), (1978, "32:58–33:33"), (2019, "33:39–34:23"), (2068, "34:28–35:02"), (2102, "35:02–35:18"),), id: 814)

