#passage(("You grow as a person. When it comes to the worldly life and the worldly perspective, of course you grow, as many things you learn, you gain experiences, you learn more information, perhaps you discover things about yourself, you discover your own flaws more; all of these things do happen.", "But when it comes to the religious beliefs, if you've reached the truth, then there's nothing to grow after that. So if I've reached what the truth is, of course in Islam it's a sea of knowledge, so you're going to learn every day. So from a spiritual sense, you are growing. I'm not going to say you don't grow at all. You learn more about your own spirituality and about the teachings that is coming from God, about the guidance. So if you mean that side of growth, then everyone grows every day from that sense. Every Muslim should seek knowledge. The prophet told us, actually, it's an obligation upon every Muslim to seek knowledge. So we need to grow when it comes to our Islamic knowledge, and as people, we need to improve.", "And this life is a test. It's a never-ending test until you die. The minute you die, the test ends. But as long as you're living, it's always a test. It doesn't stop. Every action that you take, every word that you say, the things that comes across you, situations, how you going to behave: all of these things are tests. Your own children, the money, the wealth: Islam says all of these things are a test for you. So from that perspective, I've grown, learned more about my religion, about myself. But the question is, have you grown enough to know the truth yet or not? That's the question.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “The Muslim Lantern, Sneako and Arab Debate Religion! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QiBVA3ZecoI", ((73, "1:13–1:30"), (90, "1:30–2:08"), (128, "2:08–2:44"),), id: 828)
