#passage(("The point is this: ادْعُونِي أَسْتَجِبْ لَكُمْ (Quran4:60), وَإِذَا سَأَلَكَ عِبَادِي عَنِّي فَإِنِّي قَرِيبٌ ۖ أُجِيبُ دَعْوَةَ الدَّاعِ إِذَا دَعَانِ (Quran2:186). These are certain verses you're talking about. But you need to take the whole religion together; you cannot take a part without a part. The Prophetﷺ told us that Allahﷻ will answer the prayer of an individual if he's not hasty. So the Prophetﷺ put few conditions first. Let's understand them.", "If you ask Allah for إثم or قطيعة رحم, so if you ask Allah for something which is a sin or cutting family ties, the Prophet said you're not going to get answered. Number 1, it's not any prayer. Number 2, you make Du'aa and you're certain that Allah can do that thing. If you're not certain that Allah can do that thing, Allah does not answer the Du'aa of a قلبٍ لاهٍ, a heart which is not there: you're just saying words and you're not even thinking of what you're saying. Which a lot of people do. So, this is another condition. Now (3), the Prophetﷺ said that Allah will answer all of your Du'aaa if you're not in rush. You cannot be in a rush. The Prophet said being in rush means saying “Why am I not getting the answer? Why am I not getting answered?”, which is being in rush, and you stop making Du'aa.", "Then (4), the Prophet also, and the Scholars, they explained that the answer can be in different ways. For example, it can be answered later on. I may ask Allah for money and Allah doesn't give me money today, because Allah knows it's not good for me to get money today. If I get money today, something bad will happen to me, so Allah gives you money after 10 years, after 20 years. You might ask Allah for a righteous wife when you're 21 and you get married at 28, but that is a righteous wife. So Allah doesn't say “I will instantly answer you” in the verse, but that's the assumption of certain people.", "Also, scholars said that Allah can keep that Du'aa for the Day of Judgment and elevate your status with that Du'aa. Allah can remove some of your sins using that.", "Certain things, Allah is not going to give them to you, because he said to you in the (Quran2:216) وَعَسَىٰٓ أَن تَكْرَهُوا۟ شَيْـًۭٔا وَهُوَ خَيْرٌۭ لَّكُمْ ۖ وَعَسَىٰٓ أَن تُحِبُّوا۟ شَيْـًۭٔا وَهُو شَرٌّۭلَّكُمْ ۗ وَٱللَّهُ يَعْلَمُ وَأَنتُمْ لَا تَعْلَمُونَ (Maybe you love something and it is bad for you and maybe you hate something and it is good for you and Allah knows and you do not know). So, maybe Allah will not give you something because He knows that thing is not good for you. So He will stop that thing from you and He will not give it to you, but that's good for you. This question is very easily answered when you take the whole Islamic perspective together and not just one verse out of context.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Tunisian Girl Questions Muslim On Women's Rights! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l68vK6nDhbA", ((1873, "31:13–31:46"), (1906, "31:46–32:28"), (1950, "32:30–32:52"), (1979, "32:59–33:04"), (1984, "33:04–33:30"),), id: 830)
