#passage(("In Islam we don't believe we fast Ramadan because the God's power is in Ramadan. No: Allah says we fast so we can attain [taqwa], God Consciousness. Muslims fast because they want to attain God Consciousness.", "When we fast we don't eat or drink or have sexual intercourse, and we try to maintain our anger. It's many things; it's not just food or drink, as many people think: self-control. Now the question is: within these hours from dawn to sunset that we fast, who sees you? If you sneak and you drink or eat, who can know? No one, only the Creator can know. So you practice something which we call God Consciousness: that you know that God observes you and he sees you 24 hours. Even though you could, when you're hungry, when you're thirsty, drink and eat, you don't, because you know the Creator is watching.", "So that is developed within you as a human being. Now throughout the year, whenever you are in any situation, you have God in your mind: God sees me right now when I'm alone; God sees me right now, before I help this person or not help this person, if I have the opportunity. So you practice the idea of God Consciousness throughout the year through fasting.", "So many wisdoms behind fasting; these are the wisdom, not something to do with the power of God. That would be polytheism. Creator told us to fast for these specific reasons, and that specific month as well.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Hindu Questions Muslim On Polytheism! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6Nbn5J51AtE", ((889, "14:49–15:07"), (907, "15:07–15:42"), (944, "15:44–16:02"), (973, "16:13–16:38"),), id: 835)
