#passage(("Fasting is very important on a spiritual level between you and your Creator. Just like prayer is, fasting also is very important. Allah says: الصَّوْم فإنَّه لي، وَأَنَا أَجْزِي به The fasting is for me and I'll reward accordingly. Allah sees you, he sees how you do: were you struggling when fasting? Were you trying to play games here and there? Or were you actually uniquely fasting for Allah?", "So it teaches us that there is one camera that is never shut, and that's God! People behave very differently when the camera is on, but when you realise there is a camera that's 24 hours on you, then your behavior will also be accordingly. That's the most important thing you learn from fasting.", "But there are many other things that we learn. One thing is teaching you discipline: you have access to something, but you prevent yourself from that thing; even though you can access it, you're preventing yourself from it, to learn discipline. It teaches you to know about people who are less fortunate than you, people who don't have money and food. A lot of us can say, \"Oh yeah, I feel bad for you\", but have you ever been in a situation where you couldn't eat or drink? As a Muslim you can say always yes! For a whole month I couldn't eat or drink, so I realized what kind of thirst or hunger that person might go through, the person who doesn't have food. So when I'm giving him money, that encourages me hundred times more to give that person money, because I know what he's going through; it's not just I'm saying I know what you're going through.", "And that's why Muslims are the most charitable people on Earth! They're the most charitable people in the UK according to the Daily Mail, and they are the most charitable people in the US, because we understand that giving charity is very important; it's a part of the teachings of Islam. And fasting brings you closer to that and teaches you that, teaches you the discipline, teaches you to appreciate what you have.", "Fasting, and Zakah, which is obligatory charity that is given every year, and what we call Shahada, which is testimony of Faith, to say there's only One God and Prophet Muhammad is His Messenger, and Pilgrimage: these are the 5 pillars of Islam. Islam is built on these 5 pillars; these are the most important actions in Islam, the pillars where actually Islam stays on, and each one of them will have so many lessons.", "You can just research \"intermediate fasting\" and see how many benefits medically are for you for fasting: the detoxification, and all poison away from your body, and all of the benefits for your heart, and for your body generally. But we don't do it for the medical benefits; we do it because God commanded us to do it, and we know if God commanded us to do it, then definitely there is a benefit in it.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Non-Muslim Audience Asks Muslim Difficult Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=imKsFyzx-Yo", ((1645, "27:25–28:06"), (1686, "28:06–28:37"), (1721, "28:41–29:25"), (1769, "29:29–29:41"), (1787, "29:47–30:06"), (1818, "30:18–30:36"),), id: 836)
