#passage(("That's why it's a struggle: how do you differentiate? You get extensive whispers from the [Shaytan]: \"Oh, this is not for the sake of Allah.\" First you say, \"This is for the sake of Allah.\" You ignore these whispers; you say, \"No, this is for the sake of Allah, I'm doing it for the sake of Allah.\" You stick with your deed, you ignore these whispers, and you try to purify your intention as much as possible. Because you know when you're not doing it for Allah, regardless of the whispers. The whispers you ignore them, but when you're doing the actions, you know your intention. Keeping an eye on it and observing it, you will know when it's deviating left and right, and then you come back and return.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Eddie @TheDeenShowTV Interviews The Muslim Lantern | Masjid Dar Al-Qur'an | Chicago - USA”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sLfJyJGj_eg", ((4821, "1:20:21–1:21:04"),), id: 843)
// U ML233:1798-1877 | The Muslim Lantern | 4
#passage(("When it comes to the intentions: the companions of the Prophet sallallah alaihi wasallam, the best of the people after the prophets of God, they didn't struggle with anything more than they did with the intention. If anyone does not struggle with the intention, there's a problem with sincerity. You're a human being, and certain things influences you: money influences you, fame, people's praise influences you. You have to always renew your intention. [Umar] was asking: \"Am I among the names of the Hypocrites?\" What should we do, me and you?", "So we ask Allah continuously to give us sincerity. We always check ourselves on a day-to-day basis, because the intention shifts very quickly. You [start] for the sake of Allah and gradually you move into a different purpose, and you see that happening in many people: you don't notice sincerity slipping away from you.", "So that's a very important thing: that you call Allah, ask Allah first, before anything else, to keep you sincere, because this is what the prophet sallallah wasallam used to do: \"[Turner] of Hearts, keep my heart firm on your religion.\" Allah says: \"Do not shift our hearts.\" Allah says about the prophet: \"If we did not keep you firm…\" Allah is the one who kept him firm; he is the one who can keep us firm, and anyone firm. So: asking Allah.", "And then the second thing is: have deeds that no one knows, because then this is 100% going to be sincere, because no one knows about it, only Allah. This is the most important of the deeds, because they are free from any insincerity. No one hears about it, no one knows about it; you take it to the grave. Each of us needs to have deeds like this.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Eddie @TheDeenShowTV Interviews The Muslim Lantern | Masjid Dar Al-Qur'an | Chicago - USA”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sLfJyJGj_eg", ((3904, "1:05:04–1:06:01"), (3961, "1:06:01–1:06:34"), (3994, "1:06:34–1:07:16"), (4036, "1:07:16–1:07:54"),), id: 844)
