#passage(("The Hadith of the Prophet is clear: whoever does an action that he associates with, Allah leaves him and who he associates with. That's Allah himself describing this.", "Now, can someone do something with Allah as his main intention, and then the other things are consequences? Be careful here: as consequences that are bound to come, because Allah told you they're going to come. But you obeying Allah: that is perfectly acceptable, and that's what everyone does. Meaning that you thank Allah because you believe he's worthy of being thanked, and you know that an outcome that is going to come is: Allah is going to increase you, not just some money; increase you in everything. Allah says, \"I will increase you\", in anything, and everything can be increased. So we know that's a consequence. For example happiness: we know that's a consequence of obeying Allah's command.", "So if you're doing the action and you know that these are consequences, in your heart and your mind, but the main intention for you, you're doing this for Allah, you know that other thing is just a consequence that is bound to come by obeying Allah: there is no problem. The problem is where both of them, or the main intention, is that worldly thing.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Aqeedah (Creed) And Its Significance In Islam | AIM Conference 2024 NJ | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ULnwXbVf_cM", ((9319, "2:35:19–2:35:37"), (9341, "2:35:41–2:36:29"), (9389, "2:36:29–2:36:50"),), id: 845)
// U ML219:1536-1618 | The Muslim Lantern | 1
#passage(("Your argument against the fact that people do things to get to paradise is because it's a selfish reason. That's the argument. Doing it to feel good is also a selfish reason. So, whatever reason you're going to choose to do, in the end, is going to end up being something selfish. You're never going to be the perfect being that do good just because you love the creator and you have nothing ever in your mind while you're doing it. So, that is a hypothetical that does not happen in reality. So, if there is any selfishness in it, then whether that selfishness is to get paradise and rewarded, that you deserve because of what you did in a way, or the mercy of God as well, or that you want to feel good, there's no really difference between the two.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Lantern | Arab | Sneak0 | Young Don | Warner | Discuss Religion”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XCqP_UWikkY", ((4954, "1:22:34–1:23:13"),), id: 846)
