#passage(("It's not like that, that there's necessarily a Prohibition on repeating a specific verse of the Quran. The intention was about sincerity, and the people who try to do certain things in their recitation to bring attention to their voice, to bring attention to them as individuals, rather than being for the sake of Allah: for instance, repeating the same verse 100 times. He keeps repeating, and the reason: attention. He's trying to beautify as much as possible to bring attention to him, his voice; it's no longer about the speech of Allah. If you trace the prophet, the companion, it's not something that was commonly done. So we were just highlighting the importance of sincerity, the importance of doing things for the sake of Allah.", "That's why in the Hadith, the very frightening actually Hadith of the first three people, the three people that would be used to increase the Fire, or the severity of the fire, one of them is a person who's a reciter of the Quran.", "I experienced this, some parts here in the US. I was just praying, and the brother keeps repeating the verse, repeating the verse, and you're trying to pray, you're trying to be connected with Allah, but he keeps repeating.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Eddie @TheDeenShowTV Interviews The Muslim Lantern | Masjid Dar Al-Qur'an | Chicago - USA”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sLfJyJGj_eg", ((3486, "58:06–59:06"), (3546, "59:06–59:40"), (3626, "1:00:26–1:00:42"),), id: 847)
