#passage(("We should be thankful, because when you do one حسنة (Hasana: Good Deed), how many rewards do you get? You get 10. But when you do one bad deed, how many bad deeds do you get? It's the same. So does that look like someone who wants you to be rewarded, who wants you to go to paradise, or does it look like someone who wants to punish you? Allah says in the Quran (Hud11:114) إِنَّ ٱلْحَسَنَـٰتِ يُذْهِبْنَ ٱلسَّيِّـَٔاتِ (Indeed, good deeds do away with misdeeds). What does that mean? The good deeds that you do remove the sins without you doing anything. The minor sins that you're doing: Allah says (you do good), Allah will remove your bad deeds.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Ex-Muslim Questions The Rationality Behind Islamic Laws! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l86scGUnVXI", ((934, "15:34–16:11"),), id: 848)
