#passage(("Allah didn't say, إن السيئات يذهبن الحسنات (Allah didn't say, doing bad deeds, will remove your good deeds). He could have said, and that would be equal and just one-for-one. But no, Allah wills good for you. So Allah said, one good deed is with 10, actually to 700. وَاللَّهُ يُضَاعِفُ لِمَن يَشَاءُ Allah multiplies for whom He wills (alBaqara2:261). Not just 10, it could be 700, it could be more, for whom Allah wills, if Allah sees sincerity in that individual.", "Allah gives you ways to have forgiveness from the sins that you do: repent, that's it! You repent, you get good deeds. There's a narration: if you have an intention to do a bad deed and you stop, you get a reward. But you wanted to do bad; you wanted to do evil. So that is a Creator that is Merciful with His Creation. That is a Creator that is giving more than just a chance; He's making it easy for the people to reach paradise. And that's what you should be thankful for. There's something that we are supposed to be thankful for: for Him allowing us and putting us in this place, to begin with.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Ex-Muslim Questions The Rationality Behind Islamic Laws! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l86scGUnVXI", ((1100, "18:20–18:40"), (1126, "18:46–19:20"),), id: 849)
