#passage(("The thing about Muslims is this (you compare this to any other faith): if you go to a Muslim, even sometimes if the Muslim is very bad, he's living a sinful life, when you go and you call to him what the Quran says or the Prophets says, there's always this level of respect (we're talking about the overwhelming majority now), and waking up and coming back to the teachings of God, on submitting. Because it's a very essential teaching of Islam.", "And even advising others: this is even a more important aspect of Islam that you're not gonna find in other religions. If a Muslims sees another Muslim doing wrong, we advise. We say, \"This is wrong. Don't do this.\" The Prophet said: \"Aid your brother if he is the oppressor or if he's oppressed.\" Then they said, \"If he's oppressed we're gonna aid him, but if he's the oppressor, how do we aid him?\" The Prophet said, \"You stop him from his oppression.\" So even if our Muslim brother is oppressing someone, we have to go and stop that Muslim from oppressing other people. These are the teachings of Islam that we believe in.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Catholic Grandfather Examines The Teachings Of Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tyYeayKMNwM", ((2191, "36:31–36:55"), (2215, "36:55–37:21"),), id: 850)

