#passage(("I'm not telling you [wear] or don't wear the hijab. But I'll tell you something. The Quran gives examples of different people. Allah says in the Quran there's an example of someone who [disobeys] Allah, but he's trying to improve his life. Allah says: others admitted their mistakes, their sins; then Allah says that may Allah forgive them, may Allah pardon them. So this is a group of people. Then Allah mentions another group of people: Allah says the person that, if you say to him, \"Fear Allah, this is wrong\", starts being pridefully arrogant, meaning: \"No, I'm not doing something wrong.\"", "So I'm not saying that you're a bad person, you're evil person, you're not wearing the hijab, you're going to hell. I'm not saying any of that. But to say that Islam doesn't teach it because I'm not wearing it: that's a very different thing. Why? Because you have teachings of Allah. You have shortcomings that we have. I'm not perfect. I'm making my own mistakes. But I admit. If someone comes to me: \"Brother, this is wrong. Why didn't you pray this? Why did you say that?\", I agree: \"This is wrong. May Allah make me better.\"", "That is not going to work with someone who has pride. There are people who, when it comes to Allah and his messenger, they put their pride down. Yes, I have pride in the dunya. But if someone comes to me and says the messenger of Allah sallallahu alaihi [wasallam said], I put my head down. That's what Muslim means. Muslim is from Islam, from submission: you submit to Allah and his messenger. This is what a believer needs to do. So you don't have a choice in that.", "Allah is making an oath. Look at this verse: they make you a judge in their affairs; you don't even feel any discomfort. Allah is even adding upon that: and completely submit. This is what a believer is. Allah is saying you will not become a believer until you submit to the judgment of the messenger, have nothing in your heart, and completely submit. So it wasn't for a believing man or a woman, if Allah decided something, we have a choice in it.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Non-Hijabi Woman Confronts Muslim On The Hijab Not Being In The Quran! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BzefH8uharg", ((540, "9:00–9:42"), (585, "9:45–10:13"), (631, "10:31–10:56"), (663, "11:03–11:39"),), id: 858)

