#passage(("What Islam teaches us is different: you have to have forbearance with the people. It's something important for us to understand: when Allah opened the door of repentance, it does not matter what you do in this life, the door of repentance is still open for a reason. Because imagine you were that person who's done all of these evil actions, evil deeds. If you were that person, and you know there's no repentance, what would you do? You will continue; not only continue, you're going to transgress 10 times more: \"Okay, the door of forgiveness is shut, so why should I stop? Let me continue doing it.\" The wisdom of Allah is far beyond our human basic knowledge and information. So that door is open because it's more beneficial that these people would return and come back and repent to Allah [than] it is them continuing in transgression, killing and raping and stealing and murdering and all of that.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Eddie @TheDeenShowTV Interviews The Muslim Lantern | Masjid Dar Al-Qur'an | Chicago - USA”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sLfJyJGj_eg", ((937, "15:37–16:30"),), id: 859)
