#passage(("Repentance has three conditions, or four if you commit something against another person. What is regret? Feeling regret is the feeling that if I were to come back, I wouldn't do that thing that I did; I wouldn't disobey God in that way. That's what regret is. So you sincerely ask God for repentance with that, and Allah says that he would forgive you if you're sincere in your repentance.", "How do we know? We know he promised us he will forgive those who repent. Now, if you repent and you're punished for the sins in the afterlife, then would it make sense for you to repent? It's like: \"Why would I repent? I'm going to be punished anyways.\" Repentance forgives, and the prophet told us that repentance destroys everything before it, i.e. any sins that he did. There's a narration that mentions the person who repents from a sin is like the person who's sinless, like you never committed a sin. So Allah is a merciful God, but he's given us the opportunity until death comes.", "Allah is clear in the Quran: he calls the Christians and Jews who worship other than God, he calls them disbelievers. We're saying those who get the message: remember, condition is to hear the message and to die rejecting the message.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim and Christian Sisters Enquire About Hellfire In Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7sdgLSIwzHQ", ((1276, "21:16–22:06"), (1340, "22:20–22:54"), (1396, "23:16–23:35"),), id: 860)
