#passage(("Believe in 3 things. First is to testify with your tongue. Second is to believe in your heart. Third is to do the actions that Islam tells you to do, as much as you can. Allahﷻ says in the Quran: obey Allah as much as you CAN (atTaghabun64:16). No one can be perfect. I've read the Bible: (Luke18:18) Jesus said \"no one is good except God\".", "3 conditions must be present, 4 if it's a different type of sin. Let's start with the 3. First thing: let's say my sin is between me and God. For example, I look at women lustfully; it's a sin. So the first thing you need to do is to stop it. No longer are you looking at women lustfully. The second thing is your intention: in your heart, you're never doing it again. You're not thinking tomorrow, \"I'm repenting today; tomorrow, I'm going back to looking at women again.\" No! You stop, and your intention in your heart is to make the determination: \"I'm not going to come back to look at women again.\" Third thing is that in your heart, you sincerely regret what you did, and you seek forgiveness. Then, we believe Allah will forgive you if you have these three things in place.", "Now, a fourth condition is needed if it is a sin between you and Creation as well; not only against God but also against creation. For example, a sin against God and the Creation: I steal your bag. It's a sin against you, and a sin against God, because God said don't steal; it's a sin against Him. Sin against you because I took your possession. In Islam, you have to do the 3 things; the 4th thing, you have to give back what you stole.", "Say the person you stole from went to a completely different country; you can't find him. Then what we say in Islam is that you give charity with the equal amount of that which you stole. Meaning: I stole from you this, let's say it's worth 10 pounds. I go giving charity 10 pounds; my intention, I'm giving the 10 pounds on your behalf. So you get the reward from the donation I gave in this life. It's called صد