#passage(("You have to submit to your creator. And submission to your creator is affirming there's nothing worthy of worship except him, and accepting all of his messengers, prophet Muhammad, Jesus, Moses, Noah, all of them, and then living your life as best as you can. I'm not perfect. I do many things wrong. But we repent. We don't say repent is like some traditions do: you go to the church, you say a few words, or you go to the church and the father: \"Oh, I forgive you, my son\", and you come back next week. No. Repentance in Islam has conditions. These conditions must apply. If they don't apply, no forgiveness for you. So, once these things are done, you live your life, you do as much as you can, you obey the creator, you do as much good as you can, and you try to spread goodness to other people.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Curious Couple Ask A Muslim To Explain World Suffering! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9AACeXB0A9Q", ((1247, "20:47–21:40"),), id: 862)
