#passage(("A lot of people might have hatred towards you, because what you said you did, or what they see happening to the children, all of that. But this is the difference between us as humans acting emotionally and Allah. Allah is a Forgiving God, a Forgiving and a Merciful Creator. And the Prophetﷺ told us of a story of a man who killed 99 Souls. Then he went to a monk and he asked him, \"Is there any forgiveness?\" So the monk said \"no\", so he killed the monk! Then he went to the person of Knowledge and he said to him, \"Is there any forgiveness?\" So the person of Knowledge told him, \"Who can close the door of repentance for you?\" No one can stop the forgiveness of God from coming to you. No one can stop God from forgiving an individual.", "I've read the Bible, I've read (1Samuel15:3) for example, or what Jeremiah was doing: going around killing the children, taking over the Land from the Canaanites. I understand. And they told you these things, and they teach you these things, and they tell you \"this is the right thing to do\", \"We're God's chosen people\", \"you're doing the right thing\". But you, deep down, because you have a conscience, as a human being, you start feeling \"this is not the right thing to do\". When you look at a child, you're still a human being; you still have a heart.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “IDF Soldier Confronted A Muslim Live Then THIS HAPPENED! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-qnYJXIxSpc", ((667, "11:07–11:44"), (717, "11:57–12:20"),), id: 864)
