#passage(("In Islam is very simple: a person can repent and come back to Allahﷻ as long as he does not die. So as long as he's alive, his soul is not leaving his body, and the Major Signs of the Day of Judgement do not happen, that person still has a chance to repent. A lot of Scholars hold the position that he will still have to account on the Day of Judgment, of the rights of other people. Not the right of Allah: the normal sins between him and God, God forgives him for it after accepting Islam. But those kind of major things, of him killing other Souls, many Scholars hold the position that that person will still be accountable for them on the Day of Judgement. Some Scholars don't. But you can see the wisdom behind them being forgiven: the forgiveness of their previous sins, it is there, because it's harder for someone who lived very evil life to come back to the Truth than it is for a normal person.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Intelligent Man Examines The Evidences For Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CyXdIF4BXok", ((763, "12:43–13:43"),), id: 865)
