#passage(("What if Satanyaho, in his deathbed, comes and says the Shahada? He's dying now and he's saying the Shahada! That doesn't help, because there's two reasons why that wouldn't help. Number one: مَنْ عَاشَ عَلَى شَيْءٍ مَاتَ عَلَيْه وَمَنْ مَاتَ عَلَى شَيْءٍ بُعِثَ عَلَيْه (Who lives upon something will die upon that thing) (And who dies upon something will be resurrected upon that thing). So there is a divine justice that takes place.", "Also, if you are in the moment of dying and then you seek repentance, then that repentance is not accepted from you, in Islam. And Allah gives us a clear example about Pharaoh, the story of Pharaoh in the Quran (Yunus10:90-91). He was drowning and dying, and then, when he was drowning, he said: (I believe in the Lord of Moses). He didn't even say, \"I believe in God\"! He just says, I believe in the Lord that Moses believed in, or his people believed in. Then Allah responded saying: ءَاۤلۡـَٔـٰنَ (Now?) (When you disbelieved and lived a wrongful life?) So, it wasn't accepted from him, because he was drowning, he was dying, and then he was trying to repent!", "And Allah says in the Quran, in chapter 4 (anNisa4:18): (That repentance is not for those..) حَتَّىٰۤ إِذَا حَضَرَ أَحَدَهُمُ ٱلۡمَوۡتُ (when death comes to one of them, they say, I believe now). Repentance is not for those people. Repentance is for people who come with sincerity, with an open heart, regretting what they did.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Omnist Left Speechless After Hearing This Muslim's Answer! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yVHQD2W5S0c", ((718, "11:58–12:20"), (743, "12:23–13:00"), (782, "13:02–13:16"),), id: 871)
